takeholder Needs:**  ISO 9001:2015 underlines the importance of understanding and meeting customer requirements, including statutory and regulatory requirements applicable to the product or service. The organization also needs to determine and address the needs and expectations of other stakeholders (e.g., suppliers, employees, regulatory agencies). **In the context of GxP, "customer" expands beyond the direct purchaser to include patients, healthcare professionals, and regulatory bodies.** This means that the QMS must be designed to ensure that products and services consistently meet the needs of all stakeholders, including safety, efficacy, and compliance requirements.\n\nThese three points highlight the shift in ISO 9001:2015 towards a more holistic, risk-based, and leadership-driven approach to quality management, which is highly relevant and beneficial for organizations operating in the regulated GxP environment.\n	completed	f	\N	f	36	498	534	0.00020280000000000002	3992	\N	\N	\N	{"fallbackUsed": false}	1774410632416-78f83cf2	2026-03-25 03:50:36.975+00	2026-03-25 03:50:36.975669+00	2026-03-25 03:50:36.975669+00
