8d1eb022-9095-4924-a419-bc096697a4d8	7558ddb2-d93e-46aa-8069-2ff02f92099c	352d7e21-5155-4ff8-8169-284bf5ece3e7	0.1	0	1	approved	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	1. Purpose\nThis SOP defines the procedures for sterile manufacturing.\n\n2. Scope\nApplies to all sterile manufacturing areas.\n\n3. Procedure\n3.1 Gowning\n3.2 Environmental Monitoring\n3.3 Aseptic Processing	\N	Initial draft	\N	4ccf68ad-485c-495a-935b-10d74b173a52	2026-03-25 09:08:52.549921+00	\N	\N	4ccf68ad-485c-495a-935b-10d74b173a52	2026-03-25 09:08:30.874497+00	platform	\N
8f51264d-c092-4c4b-a8a5-ace977309ed2	f4631330-c990-4e05-9bf4-396ee9480b1d	352d7e21-5155-4ff8-8169-284bf5ece3e7	0.1	0	1	draft	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	SERVICE SPECIFICATION\n\nFile Attachment Services\n\n\n\nQAssure Multi-Tenant SaaS Platform\n\nVersion 1.0   ·   February 2026\n\n\n\n1. Feature of Service\n\nSERVICE NAME: FILE ATTACHMENT SERVICES\n\nCentralised, tenant-isolated, binary file lifecycle engine that governs how files (documents, images, reports, specifications, audit evidence, training materials) are uploaded, stored, versioned, downloaded, previewed, shared, and deleted across multi-tenant regulated environments. All binary file operations across the QAssure platform and module applications are routed through this single service.\n\n\n\nCore capabilities:\n\n\n\n1. File Upload & Storage --- Single and multi-file upload (up to 10 files per request) with multer memory storage, 100MB max file size enforcement, blocked dangerous extensions (.exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .ps1, .msi, .dll, .com, .scr, .vbs, .js), SHA-256 checksum calculation via crypto.createHash('sha256'), and automatic tenant-scoped folder hierarchy: {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext. Files are linked to any platform entity via entity_type + entity_id (e.g., entity_type='documents', entity_id=document_uuid). Source module is auto-derived from authentication context: module code for combined JWT + API Key mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf') where module identity is captured from the API key even though user identity comes from JWT; 'platform' for JWT-only users; moduleCode for API key-only modules (e.g., 'aice', 'dhf'); or 'api_key' as fallback if an API key has no linked module. Priority order: req.module.code (combined mode) → req.user.moduleCode (API key mode) → 'platform' (JWT mode). Duplicate detection prevents re-upload of identical files to the same entity (enforced by checksum + entity match on active records).\n\n2. File Versioning --- Each file supports immutable version history. Uploading a new version via POST /:id/versions marks the previous version as is_current_version=false and creates a new record with incremented version number, linked via previous_version_id. Version history is retrieved via recursive CTE (Common Table Expression) that traverses the chain in both directions, returning complete lineage. Only the current version is returned in standard queries.\n\n3. Download & Preview --- Download endpoint (GET /:id/download) serves files with Content-Disposition: attachment header for browser download prompt. Preview endpoint (GET /:id/preview) serves with Content-Disposition: inline for in-browser rendering. Both use storageProvider.getFullPath() with path.resolve() for absolute path resolution. File access is logged in file_access_logs table with user_id, IP address, user agent, and action type.\n\n4. File Sharing with Token-Based Access --- Create time-limited, download-limited share links via POST /:id/share. Generates 64-character hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32). Supports configurable parameters: expires_at (absolute timestamp), expires_in_hours (convenience --- auto-converted to expires_at), max_downloads (download cap), share_type ('link' or 'user'), shared_with_user_id, shared_with_email, and permissions ('view' or 'download'). Access via GET /shared/:token is a PUBLIC route (no authentication required). The service validates token existence, checks expiry, enforces max_downloads limit, increments current_downloads counter, and serves the file. Share revocation via DELETE /shares/:shareId deactivates the share.\n\n5. Storage Quota Management --- Per-tenant storage quotas tracked in storage_quotas table: max_storage_bytes (default 10GB), used_storage_bytes, file_count, max_file_size_bytes (default 100MB), allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions. Quota auto-creates on first upload if not present. PostgreSQL trigger (trg_update_storage_usage) automatically increments/decrements used_storage_bytes and file_count on INSERT, DELETE, and UPDATE (soft-delete via SET deleted_at). Quota is checked before every upload: individual file size vs max_file_size_bytes, and total used + new file vs max_storage_bytes. Admin-only PUT /quota endpoint allows updating quota limits (requires files:admin permission).\n\n6. Soft Delete with Hard Delete Option --- Default DELETE /:id performs soft delete (sets deleted_at timestamp). PostgreSQL trigger automatically decrements quota on soft delete. Hard delete via DELETE /:id?hard=true permanently removes the database record AND the physical file from storage via storageProvider.delete(). Orphaned file cleanup: if database INSERT fails after file is saved to disk, the file is automatically cleaned up in the catch block.\n\n7. Storage Provider Abstraction (S3-Ready) --- All file I/O goes through LocalStorageProvider with 4 methods: save(relativePath, buffer), delete(relativePath), exists(relativePath), getFullPath(relativePath). No controller or service code touches the filesystem directly. Migrating to S3 requires implementing an S3StorageProvider with the same interface --- zero code changes in controllers or service logic.\n\n8. Three Authentication Modes --- Every endpoint (except public share access) supports three authentication modes via authenticate middleware: (a) JWT only --- QAssure UI users authenticate via Authorization: Bearer header; tenant derived from JWT claims; user permissions enforced via authorize(); (b) JWT + API Key combined --- module applications acting on behalf of a logged-in user send both Authorization: Bearer (JWT from verify-launch-token) and X-API-Key headers; tenant derived from JWT (X-Tenant-ID not needed); user permissions enforced (not module bypass); source_module set from module identity (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf') for accurate audit attribution; (c) API Key + X-Tenant-ID --- module system/cron operations with no user context send X-API-Key and X-Tenant-ID headers; module gets full access bypass on authorize(). This enables QAssure UI users, module applications acting on behalf of users (with real user identity in audit trails), and module background processes to consume the file attachment service. Routes use authorize() for permission checks: files:read for GET endpoints, files:write for POST/PUT/DELETE endpoints, files:admin for quota management.\n\n9. Multi-Tenant Data Isolation --- All queries are tenant-scoped. Every file, share, quota, and access log belongs to a tenant_id. API Key middleware validates module-tenant assignment via the tenant_module_access table (enabled = true) before granting access. Missing X-Tenant-ID returns error code MISSING_TENANT. Unassigned tenant returns MODULE_NOT_ASSIGNED. In combined mode (JWT + API Key), if the JWT's tenant does not match the API key's assigned tenant, error code TENANT_MISMATCH is returned; if the module is deactivated for the tenant, error code MODULE_NOT_ACTIVE is returned. Users cannot see or access files belonging to other tenants under any circumstance.\n\n10. Security Hardening --- UUID validation middleware on all :id route parameters returns 400 (INVALID_ID_FORMAT) for malformed UUIDs instead of leaking PostgreSQL errors. Error sanitization function (sanitizeErrorResponse) on all 17 controller catch blocks classifies errors into client-safe categories (QUOTA_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, VALIDATION_ERROR, etc.) and returns generic 'An internal error occurred' for unexpected failures --- never exposing constraint names, table structures, or query details. Blocked file extensions prevent executable uploads. Path traversal is impossible because stored names use UUID-based naming, not user-controlled paths.\n\n11. Observability --- Redis caching with graceful degradation (file cache 300s TTL, quota 60s, share 3600s, entity files 120s). Elasticsearch indexing for file searchability. File access logging with IP/user-agent tracking. Storage statistics with per-entity-type and per-module breakdowns. All infrastructure dependencies (Redis, Elasticsearch) fail gracefully --- the service continues operating without caching or indexing if either is unavailable.\n\n\n\n2. Scope\n\nIN SCOPE (Phase 1):\n\nFull file CRUD: upload single file (with auto-generated tenant-scoped storage path, checksum, source_module derivation), upload multiple files (up to 10, parallel via Promise.all), read (single by ID with Redis cache, paginated list with filtering, by entity with pagination), update metadata (description, tags, category, metadata JSONB), soft delete (with quota trigger), hard delete (with physical file removal).\n\nFile versioning: upload new version (marks previous as not current, increments version number, links via previous_version_id), retrieve version history (recursive CTE traversal in both directions).\n\nDownload and preview with correct Content-Disposition headers (attachment for download, inline for preview), file access logging, and path resolution via storageProvider abstraction.\n\nFile sharing: create share link with configurable expiry (expires_at or expires_in_hours), max_downloads cap, share_type (link/user), permissions (view/download). Public access via token (no auth required). Share revocation. Expired/exhausted shares return 404.\n\nStorage quota management: auto-create on first upload, per-tenant limits (max_storage_bytes, max_file_size_bytes, allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions), quota enforcement on every upload, admin-only quota configuration updates (files:admin permission), PostgreSQL trigger for automatic used_storage_bytes/file_count tracking on INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.\n\nThree authentication modes (JWT only, JWT + API Key combined, API Key + X-Tenant-ID) on all 16 authenticated endpoints via authenticate middleware (1 public route excluded: GET /shared/:token). Combined mode derives tenant from JWT (X-Tenant-ID not needed), enforces user permissions, and sets source_module from module identity for accurate audit attribution.\n\nMulti-tenant isolation on all read and write operations.\n\nAPI Key middleware validates module-tenant access via tenant_module_access table.\n\nUUID validation middleware on all :id parameters --- returns 400 for invalid UUIDs.\n\nError sanitization on all 17 catch blocks --- never leaks database internals.\n\nFile access audit trail via file_access_logs with user_id, IP address, user agent, action.\n\nStorage statistics with quota summary, file type counts, by_entity and by_module breakdowns.\n\nPagination via limit and offset query parameters (default limit 50). Response is a JSON array of file objects.\n\nFilter support on list: source_module, mime_type, entity_type, category, search (ILIKE on original_name), sort (created_at, file_size, original_name), date range (created_after, created_before).\n\nOrphaned file cleanup: if DB INSERT fails after file save, file is automatically removed from storage.\n\nRedis caching with graceful degradation (operates without Redis).\n\nElasticsearch indexing with graceful degradation (operates without ES).\n\n\n\nOUT OF SCOPE (Phase 1 --- File Attachment Service boundary):\n\nS3/MinIO object storage migration --- LocalStorageProvider is production-ready; S3StorageProvider is a config swap planned for Phase 2. Storage provider abstraction is already in place.\n\nVirus/malware scanning --- scan_status and scanned_at columns exist in file_attachments table but no scanning service is integrated.\n\nImage thumbnail generation --- has_thumbnail, thumbnail_path columns exist but no thumbnail generation pipeline is implemented.\n\nFull-text content extraction from uploaded files (PDF text extraction, OCR).\n\nVector embedding of file content for semantic search via Qdrant.\n\nReal-time file upload progress (WebSocket-based progress tracking).\n\nClient-side chunked upload for files larger than 100MB.\n\nCDN integration for cached file delivery.\n\nFile format conversion (PDF to image, document to PDF, etc.).\n\nWatermarking or digital stamping of downloaded files.\n\nBulk import/export of files.\n\nFile-level access control lists (ACLs) --- access is controlled at entity level via entity_type permissions, not per-file.\n\nRetention policy enforcement --- soft-deleted files remain in database indefinitely until hard-deleted.\n\nEmail/SMS notifications on file events (handled by Notification Service separately).\n\nDocument lifecycle management (SOPs, versioning, review/approval) --- handled by separate Document Service (document.service.js).\n\n\n\n3. Clear Responsibility Split\n\n3.1 SaaS Platform (Owned by Platform Team):\n\nProvide and maintain the File Attachment Service as a centralised, tenant-isolated binary file management engine.\n\nEnforce file upload constraints: 100MB max file size (multer + quota), blocked dangerous extensions, per-tenant storage quotas with auto-creation and trigger-based tracking.\n\nGenerate and manage tenant-scoped storage paths: {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext.\n\nCalculate SHA-256 checksums on every upload for integrity verification.\n\nAuto-derive source_module from authentication context with priority: req.module.code for combined JWT + API Key mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf'), req.user.moduleCode for API key-only modules, 'platform' for JWT-only users, 'api_key' fallback for API keys without linked modules. This ensures files uploaded by modules on behalf of users are correctly attributed to the originating module in storage statistics.\n\nManage file versioning: version number increment, previous_version_id linking, is_current_version flagging, recursive CTE version history retrieval.\n\nMaintain storage provider abstraction (LocalStorageProvider) with save, delete, exists, getFullPath methods for future S3 migration.\n\nEnforce tenant isolation on all queries via tenant_id filtering. No cross-tenant file access is possible.\n\nProvide three authentication modes on all 16 authenticated endpoints via authenticate middleware (1 public route excluded: GET /shared/:token): (a) JWT only for QAssure UI users, (b) JWT + API Key combined for module applications acting on behalf of logged-in users (tenant from JWT, user permissions enforced, source_module from module identity), (c) API Key + X-Tenant-ID for module system/cron operations.\n\nValidate module-tenant access via tenant_module_access table (enabled = true check). Return MISSING_TENANT or MODULE_NOT_ASSIGNED errors for invalid API Key requests. In combined mode, return TENANT_MISMATCH if JWT tenant differs from API key's assigned tenant, and MODULE_NOT_ACTIVE if the module is deactivated for the tenant.\n\nProvide UUID validation middleware for all route parameters. Return 400 INVALID_ID_FORMAT for malformed UUIDs.\n\nSanitise all error responses to prevent database internal leakage.\n\nProvide file sharing infrastructure: token generation, expiry enforcement, max_downloads enforcement, public access route.\n\nProvide storage statistics with per-entity-type and per-module breakdowns.\n\nLog all file access events (download, preview, checkout, checkin) in file_access_logs.\n\nProvide Redis caching and Elasticsearch indexing with graceful degradation.\n\nExpose admin-only quota management endpoint (files:admin permission).\n\n\n\n3.2 Module Applications (Residing on Platform; Owned by App Teams --- LTTS):\n\nUse the File Attachment Service API with the appropriate authentication mode:\n\nFor user-context operations (user uploads a file via module UI): Send both Authorization: Bearer (JWT obtained from verify-launch-token) and X-API-Key headers. X-Tenant-ID is NOT needed --- tenant is derived from JWT. User permissions (files:read, files:write) are enforced. uploaded_by and file_access_logs.user_id record the real user identity. source_module records the module identity (e.g., 'coc').\n\nFor system/cron operations (no user context): Send X-API-Key + X-Tenant-ID headers. Module gets full access bypass. source_module records the module identity from API key.\n\nSpecify entity_type and entity_id when uploading files to link them to the correct module entity (e.g., entity_type='documents', entity_id=<document_uuid> for Document Service; entity_type='capa', entity_id=<capa_uuid> for CAPA module).\n\nProvide required fields on upload: file (multipart), entity_type (string), entity_id (UUID). Optional fields: description, category, tags, metadata (JSONB).\n\nUse the version upload endpoint (POST /:id/versions) for updating files rather than deleting and re-uploading. This preserves version history and audit trail.\n\nUse the share endpoint to generate time-limited, download-limited links for external stakeholders (e.g., auditors, suppliers) without granting platform login access.\n\nDo NOT implement custom file storage logic --- always delegate to platform's file attachment service.\n\nDo NOT store file metadata in the module's own database --- use platform as the system of record for all file attachments. Use the entity link (entity_type + entity_id) to associate files with module records.\n\nDo NOT construct file paths manually or access the uploads directory directly --- always use service API endpoints for file access.\n\nUse SSO launch token flow to obtain both tenant context and user session JWT dynamically in production: call POST /modules/verify-launch-token with X-API-Key and the launch token to receive a JWT (24h expiry), user details (including department, designation, user category), tenant details, and permissions. Use this JWT in Authorization: Bearer header alongside X-API-Key for all user-context platform calls. Use .env TENANT_ID + X-Tenant-ID header for development and system/cron operations only.\n\n\n\n4. API List (Refer to Excel Sheet shared)\n\n\n\n#\n\nMethod\n\nEndpoint\n\nAuth\n\nDescription\n\n1\n\nPOST\n\n/api/v1/files/upload\n\nauthenticate + files:write\n\nUpload single file (multipart)\n\n2\n\nPOST\n\n/api/v1/files/upload/multiple\n\nauthenticate + files:write\n\nUpload multiple files (up to 10)\n\n3\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files\n\nauthenticate + files:read\n\nList files (paginated, filterable)\n\n4\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/:id\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nGet single file by ID\n\n5\n\nPUT\n\n/api/v1/files/:id\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nUpdate file metadata\n\n6\n\nDELETE\n\n/api/v1/files/:id\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nDelete file (soft; ?hard=true for permanent)\n\n7\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/download\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nDownload file (Content-Disposition: attachment)\n\n8\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/preview\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nPreview file (Content-Disposition: inline)\n\n9\n\nPOST\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/versions\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nUpload new version of existing file\n\n10\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/versions\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nGet version history (recursive CTE)\n\n11\n\nPOST\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/share\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nCreate share link (token, expiry, max_downloads)\n\n12\n\nDELETE\n\n/api/v1/files/shares/:shareId\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nRevoke share link\n\n13\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/shared/:token\n\nPUBLIC (no auth)\n\nAccess shared file via token\n\n14\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/entity/:entity_type/:entity_id\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nGet files by entity (paginated)\n\n15\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/stats\n\nauthenticate + files:read\n\nGet storage statistics (by entity, by module)\n\n16\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/quota\n\nauthenticate + files:read\n\nGet tenant storage quota\n\n17\n\nPUT\n\n/api/v1/files/quota\n\nauthenticate + files:admin\n\nUpdate tenant storage quota (admin only)\n\n\n\nRoute ordering note: /stats, /quota, /entity/:type/:id, /shared/:token are registered BEFORE /:id to prevent Express matching static segments as UUID parameters.\n\n\n\n5. Typical Workflow\n\n5.1 Write Path (File Upload & Management):\n\n1. Upload Single File: Tenant user or module calls POST /api/v1/files/upload with multipart form data: file (required, binary), entity_type (required, e.g., 'documents'), entity_id (required, UUID of parent entity), and optional: description, category, tags (comma-separated string or JSON array), metadata (JSONB). The API validates: file presence (returns VALIDATION_ERROR 'No file uploaded'), entity_type and entity_id presence (returns VALIDATION_ERROR 'entity_type and entity_id are required'), file extension not in blocked list (.exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .ps1, .msi, .dll, .com, .scr, .vbs, .js --- returns error 'File type .exe is not allowed'), file size under 100MB (returns FILE_TOO_LARGE 'File size exceeds 100MB limit'), tenant quota not exceeded (returns QUOTA_ERROR for both individual file and total storage).\n\nPlatform generates: stored_name as {uuid}_{sanitized_original_name}.ext, storage path as {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{stored_name}, SHA-256 checksum via crypto.createHash('sha256').update(buffer).digest('hex'), source_module derived from auth context with priority: req.module.code for combined mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf'), 'platform' for JWT-only users, req.user.moduleCode for API key-only modules (e.g., 'aice', 'dhf'), or 'api_key' fallback if API key has no linked module. File is saved to storage via storageProvider.save(relativePath, buffer), then database record is inserted into file_attachments. If DB INSERT fails, file is automatically cleaned up from storage (orphan prevention). Redis cache is invalidated for entity files list. Elasticsearch index is updated via IndexingHooks. Returns full file object with 201 status.\n\n2. Upload Multiple Files: POST /api/v1/files/upload/multiple accepts up to 10 files via multer array ('files' field, max 10). All files are uploaded in parallel via Promise.all, sharing the same entity_type and entity_id. Returns array of results with per-file success/error status. Quota is checked per file individually.\n\n3. Update Metadata: PUT /api/v1/files/:id updates allowed fields: description (text), category (varchar), tags (cast as text[]), metadata (cast as JSONB). File content changes go through versioning (POST /:id/versions), not metadata update. Sets updated_at timestamp. Returns 'No valid fields to update' error if no recognized fields provided. Returns full file object with 200 status.\n\n4. Soft Delete: DELETE /api/v1/files/:id sets deleted_at = NOW() timestamp. PostgreSQL trigger (trg_update_storage_usage) automatically decrements used_storage_bytes and file_count in storage_quotas using GREATEST(..., 0) to prevent negative values. File remains on disk for potential recovery. Redis cache invalidated. Elasticsearch index updated. Returns { success: true, message: 'File deleted' }.\n\n5. Hard Delete: DELETE /api/v1/files/:id?hard=true permanently removes: database record (DELETE FROM file_attachments WHERE id = $1 AND tenant_id = $2), physical file from storage via storageProvider.delete(file_path), thumbnail if exists via storageProvider.delete(thumbnail_path). Returns 404 on subsequent GET. Irreversible. Quota adjusts via DELETE trigger.\n\n\n\n5.2 Versioning:\n\nMinor Versioning: Default behavior. Every POST /api/v1/files/:id/versions with new file (multipart) performs: fetches current record by ID and tenant_id, marks it as is_current_version=false via UPDATE, inserts new record with version = previous_version + 1, is_current_version=true, previous_version_id = old record ID. SHA-256 checksum is calculated for the new file. Both old and new records remain in database --- version history is immutable and never deleted.\n\nVersion History Retrieval: GET /api/v1/files/:id/versions uses a recursive CTE (Common Table Expression) that traverses the previous_version_id chain in both directions (forward via self-join on previous_version_id, backward via matching previous_version_id = id). Returns complete version lineage with: id, version, file_size, checksum, original_name, uploaded_by_email (resolved via LEFT JOIN users), created_at for each version. Ordered by version number ascending.\n\nVersion Chain Structure: file_attachments.previous_version_id creates a self-referencing linked list. Version 1 has previous_version_id=null. Version 2 points to Version 1. Version 3 points to Version 2. Only the latest version has is_current_version=true. Standard queries (list, get by entity) only return current versions (WHERE is_current_version = true AND deleted_at IS NULL).\n\n\n\n5.3 Read/Search Path:\n\nGet by ID: GET /api/v1/files/:id --- Redis cached (300s TTL). Returns full file object with uploaded_by_email resolved via LEFT JOIN users. Filters by tenant_id for isolation.\n\nList Files: GET /api/v1/files?limit=50&offset=0 --- returns a JSON array of file objects. Supports limit and offset query parameters for pagination. Supports filters: source_module, mime_type, entity_type, category, search (ILIKE on original_name), sort_by (created_at|file_size|original_name), sort_order (ASC|DESC), created_after, created_before. Only returns active files (deleted_at IS NULL, is_current_version = true).\n\nGet by Entity: GET /api/v1/files/entity/:entity_type/:entity_id --- returns a JSON array of all files linked to a specific entity. Used by Document Service, CAPA module, Training module, etc. to retrieve their linked files.\n\nStorage Stats: GET /api/v1/files/stats --- returns four sections: quota (max_storage, used_storage, available, usage_percent), files (total, images, pdfs, documents counts), by_entity (count + size per entity_type), and by_module (count + size per source_module e.g., 'platform', 'coc').\n\nStorage Quota: GET /api/v1/files/quota --- returns current quota status: max_storage_bytes, used_storage_bytes, file_count, max_file_size_bytes, allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions, usage_percentage.\n\n\n\n5.4 File Sharing Path:\n\nCreate Share: POST /api/v1/files/:id/share with body: share_type ('link'|'user'), permissions ('view'|'download'), expires_at (ISO timestamp) or expires_in_hours (number, auto-converted), max_downloads (integer), shared_with_user_id, shared_with_email. Service generates 64-char hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32). Returns share object with share_token, share_url, expires_at, max_downloads. Redis cached (3600s TTL).\n\nAccess Shared File: GET /api/v1/files/shared/:token --- PUBLIC route (no authentication). Service: looks up share by token (Redis cached), validates expiry (expires_at > NOW()), validates download count (current_downloads < max_downloads), increments current_downloads, resolves file path via storageProvider.getFullPath(), serves file with correct Content-Type and Content-Disposition headers. Returns 404 if share not found, expired, or download limit reached.\n\nRevoke Share: DELETE /api/v1/files/shares/:shareId --- sets is_active=false. Invalidates Redis cache for the share token.\n\n\n\n5.5 Retention/Deletion:\n\nPhase 1: No automated retention policy enforcement. Soft-deleted files remain in database with deleted_at timestamp set. Hard delete permanently removes file and database record.\n\nQuota Recovery: Soft delete triggers automatic quota decrement via PostgreSQL trigger. Restoring a soft-deleted file (clearing deleted_at) would trigger quota increment.\n\nPlanned Phase 2: Configurable retention periods per entity_type. Scheduled cleanup job to hard-delete files past retention period. Archived storage tier for long-term retention at reduced cost.\n\n\n\n5.6 Audit Trail:\n\nfile_access_logs records (inserted on download, preview, and any file access): file_id, tenant_id, user_id, action ('download'|'preview'|'access'), ip_address (from req.ip), user_agent (from req.headers), created_at.\n\nStorage quota changes tracked via PostgreSQL trigger --- every INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on file_attachments automatically adjusts used_storage_bytes and file_count.\n\nShare access tracked via current_downloads counter and last_accessed_at timestamp on file_shares.\n\nAuthentication mode impacts audit attribution: In combined JWT + API Key mode, uploaded_by and file_access_logs.user_id record the real user identity (from JWT), while source_module records the originating module (from API key). This provides GxP-compliant traceability --- auditors can see both who performed the action and which module facilitated it. In API Key-only mode, uploaded_by records the module service account and source_module records the module code. In JWT-only mode, uploaded_by records the platform user and source_module is set to 'platform'.\n\n\n\n6. PostgreSQL DB --- MODEL\n\nThe File Attachment Service uses 4 PostgreSQL tables: file_attachments (master record with binary file metadata, entity linking, versioning, and storage path), storage_quotas (per-tenant storage limits with trigger-maintained usage counters), file_shares (token-based file sharing with expiry and download limits), and file_access_logs (audit trail for file access events). All tables enforce multi-tenant isolation via tenant_id foreign key with ON DELETE CASCADE. The file_attachments table serves as the central entity. A PostgreSQL trigger function (update_storage_usage) automatically maintains used_storage_bytes and file_count in storage_quotas on INSERT, UPDATE (soft-delete/restore), and DELETE operations.\n\n6.1 ER Diagram:\n\n\n\nFigure 6.1: Entity Relationship Diagram --- File Attachment Service\n\nfile_attachments.tenant_id → tenants.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n\nfile_attachments.uploaded_by → users.id\n\nfile_attachments.previous_version_id → file_attachments.id (self-referencing version chain)\n\nstorage_quotas.tenant_id → tenants.id (UNIQUE --- one quota per tenant)\n\nfile_shares.tenant_id → tenants.id, file_shares.file_id → file_attachments.id\n\nfile_access_logs.file_id → file_attachments.id, file_access_logs.user_id → users.id\n\n6.2 Entities & Attributes:\n\n6.2.1 Entity: file_attachments (32 columns)\n\n\n\nAttribute\n\nData Type\n\nConstraint / FK\n\nDescription\n\nExample\n\nid\n\nUUID\n\nPK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\nUnique file identifier\n\ndaf3c8ad-...\n\ntenant_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, INDEX\n\nTenant isolation\n\nc0000000-...\n\noriginal_name\n\nVARCHAR(500)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nUser-uploaded filename\n\ntest-upload.txt\n\nstored_name\n\nVARCHAR(500)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nUUID-based stored name\n\ndaf3c8ad_test-upload.txt\n\nfile_path\n\nVARCHAR(1000)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nRelative storage path\n\nc000.../documents/2026/02/daf3...txt\n\nmime_type\n\nVARCHAR(255)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nMIME type\n\ntext/plain\n\nfile_size\n\nBIGINT\n\nNOT NULL\n\nFile size in bytes\n\n18\n\nchecksum\n\nVARCHAR(128)\n\nNullable\n\nSHA-256 hash\n\na591a6d40...\n\nstorage_provider\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nDEFAULT 'local'\n\nStorage backend\n\nlocal\n\nstorage_bucket\n\nVARCHAR(255)\n\nNullable\n\nS3 bucket (Phase 2)\n\nnull\n\nstorage_region\n\nVARCHAR(100)\n\nNullable\n\nS3 region (Phase 2)\n\nnull\n\nentity_type\n\nVARCHAR(100)\n\nNOT NULL, INDEX\n\nParent entity type\n\ndocuments\n\nentity_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, INDEX\n\nParent entity ID\n\nUUID\n\ncategory\n\nVARCHAR(100)\n\nNullable\n\nFile category\n\nspecification\n\ndescription\n\nTEXT\n\nNullable\n\nFile description\n\nTest file upload\n\ntags\n\nTEXT[]\n\nNullable\n\nPostgreSQL text array\n\n{sop,quality}\n\nversion\n\nINTEGER\n\nDEFAULT 1\n\nVersion number\n\n1\n\nis_current_version\n\nBOOLEAN\n\nDEFAULT true, INDEX (partial)\n\nActive version flag\n\ntrue\n\nprevious_version_id\n\nUUID\n\nFK → file_attachments(id), Nullable\n\nVersion chain link\n\nUUID or null\n\nis_public\n\nBOOLEAN\n\nDEFAULT false\n\nPublic access flag\n\nfalse\n\naccess_level\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nDEFAULT 'private'\n\nAccess level\n\nprivate\n\ndownload_count\n\nINTEGER\n\nDEFAULT 0\n\nTotal downloads\n\n5\n\nhas_thumbnail\n\nBOOLEAN\n\nDEFAULT false\n\nThumbnail exists\n\nfalse\n\nthumbnail_path\n\nVARCHAR(1000)\n\nNullable\n\nThumbnail storage path\n\nnull\n\nmetadata\n\nJSONB\n\nDEFAULT '{}'\n\nExtensible metadata\n\n{}\n\nscan_status\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nNullable\n\nVirus scan status (Phase 2)\n\nnull\n\nscanned_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nNullable\n\nScan timestamp (Phase 2)\n\nnull\n\nuploaded_by\n\nUUID\n\nFK → users(id), Nullable\n\nUploader user ID\n\nUUID\n\nsource_module\n\nVARCHAR(100)\n\nDEFAULT 'platform', INDEX\n\nOrigin module\n\nplatform\n\ncreated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nCreated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\nupdated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nUpdated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\ndeleted_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nNullable, INDEX\n\nSoft delete timestamp\n\nnull\n\n\n\nNOTES: tags is TEXT[] not JSONB. file_size is BIGINT (returns as string from node-pg, parsed to integer in _formatAttachment). is_current_version partial index filters WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND is_current_version = TRUE. previous_version_id creates a self-referencing linked list for version chains. source_module is auto-derived from auth context, never user-supplied.\n\n\n\n6.2.2 Entity: storage_quotas (10 columns)\n\n\n\nAttribute\n\nData Type\n\nConstraint / FK\n\nDescription\n\nExample\n\nid\n\nUUID\n\nPK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\nQuota record ID\n\nUUID\n\ntenant_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → tenants(id), UNIQUE\n\nTenant isolation\n\nc0000000-...\n\nmax_storage_bytes\n\nBIGINT\n\nDEFAULT 10737418240 (10GB)\n\nMax total storage\n\n10737418240\n\nused_storage_bytes\n\nBIGINT\n\nDEFAULT 0\n\nCurrent usage (trigger-maintained)\n\n1536\n\nfile_count\n\nINTEGER\n\nDEFAULT 0\n\nActive file count (trigger-maintained)\n\n15\n\nmax_file_size_bytes\n\nBIGINT\n\nDEFAULT 104857600 (100MB)\n\nMax single file size\n\n104857600\n\nallowed_mime_types\n\nTEXT[]\n\nNullable\n\nWhitelist (null = all allowed)\n\nnull\n\nblocked_extensions\n\nTEXT[]\n\nNullable\n\nBlacklist\n\n{.exe,.bat}\n\ncreated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nCreated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\nupdated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nUpdated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\n\n\nNOTES: max_storage_bytes and used_storage_bytes are BIGINT. PostgreSQL trigger update_storage_usage() maintains used_storage_bytes and file_count automatically on file_attachments INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE. The trigger uses GREATEST(..., 0) to prevent negative values. Quota auto-creates via service when first upload occurs for a tenant.\n\n\n\nPostgreSQL Trigger Function:\n\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_storage_usage() --- Handles INSERT (increment), DELETE (decrement), UPDATE with NEW.deleted_at IS NOT NULL AND OLD.deleted_at IS NULL (soft-delete decrement), UPDATE with NEW.deleted_at IS NULL AND OLD.deleted_at IS NOT NULL (restore increment). Uses GREATEST(used_storage_bytes - file_size, 0) and GREATEST(file_count - 1, 0) to prevent negative values.\n\n6.2.3 Entity: file_shares (15 columns)\n\n\n\nAttribute\n\nData Type\n\nConstraint / FK\n\nDescription\n\nExample\n\nid\n\nUUID\n\nPK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\nShare record ID\n\nUUID\n\ntenant_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n\nTenant isolation\n\nc0000000-...\n\nfile_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → file_attachments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n\nShared file\n\nUUID\n\nshare_token\n\nVARCHAR(255)\n\nNOT NULL, UNIQUE\n\n64-char hex token\n\na3f8c2d1...\n\nshare_type\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nDEFAULT 'link'\n\nShare type\n\nlink\n\nshared_with_user_id\n\nUUID\n\nFK → users(id), Nullable\n\nTarget user (for 'user' type)\n\nnull\n\nshared_with_email\n\nVARCHAR(255)\n\nNullable\n\nTarget email\n\nnull\n\npermissions\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nDEFAULT 'view'\n\nAccess level\n\nview/download\n\nexpires_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nNullable\n\nExpiry timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\nmax_downloads\n\nINTEGER\n\nNullable\n\nDownload cap (null = unlimited)\n\n5\n\ncurrent_downloads\n\nINTEGER\n\nDEFAULT 0\n\nDownloads consumed\n\n2\n\nis_active\n\nBOOLEAN\n\nDEFAULT true\n\nActive flag (false = revoked)\n\ntrue\n\nlast_accessed_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nNullable\n\nLast access time\n\nISO datetime\n\ncreated_by\n\nUUID\n\nFK → users(id), Nullable\n\nShare creator\n\nUUID\n\ncreated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nCreated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\n\n\nNOTES: share_token is UNIQUE. expires_at can be set directly or auto-calculated from expires_in_hours (service converts: new Date(Date.now() + hours * 3600000).toISOString()). max_downloads null means unlimited. current_downloads is incremented atomically on each access. is_active=false means share has been revoked.\n\n\n\n6.2.4 Entity: file_access_logs (8 columns)\n\n\n\nAttribute\n\nData Type\n\nConstraint / FK\n\nDescription\n\nExample\n\nid\n\nUUID\n\nPK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\nLog record ID\n\nUUID\n\ntenant_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n\nTenant isolation\n\nUUID\n\nfile_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → file_attachments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n\nFile accessed\n\nUUID\n\nuser_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → users(id)\n\nWho accessed\n\nUUID\n\naction\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nAction type\n\ndownload/preview/access\n\nip_address\n\nINET\n\nNullable\n\nClient IP\n\n192.168.1.1\n\nuser_agent\n\nTEXT\n\nNullable\n\nBrowser UA string\n\nMozilla/5.0...\n\ncreated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nWhen accessed\n\nISO datetime\n\n\n\nNOTES: Records are insert-only (append-only audit log). ip_address and user_agent are captured from Express request object when available. action values include 'download', 'preview', 'access' for share access.\n\n\n\n7. Qdrant (Vector DB)\n\nPhase 1 Status: NOT USED by File Attachment Service.\n\nBinary file content is stored on the filesystem via LocalStorageProvider. File metadata is stored in PostgreSQL (file_attachments table). No vector embeddings of file content are generated in Phase 1.\n\n\n\nPlanned for Phase 2:\n\nCollection Name: file_content_vec_v1\n\nVector Dimension: 1536 (OpenAI text-embedding-3-small) or 768 (sentence-transformers)\n\nPayload Fields: file_id (string), tenant_id (string --- mandatory filter), original_name (string), entity_type (string), entity_id (string), mime_type (string), category (string), source_module (string), created_at (ISO string)\n\nPayload Indexes: tenant_id, entity_type, mime_type, source_module, created_at\n\nUse Case: Semantic search across extracted file content (PDF text, document text), similar file discovery, AI-powered content recommendations, duplicate detection via vector similarity rather than checksum matching.\n\nPrerequisite: Content extraction pipeline (PDF text extraction, OCR for images, document parsing) must be implemented first to generate text from binary files before vector embedding.\n\n\n\n8. Object Storage\n\nFolder Structure Hierarchy:\n\nRoot: UPLOAD_DIR (default: ./uploads/, configurable via environment variable)\n\nPattern: {UPLOAD_DIR}/{tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext\n\n\n\nExample hierarchy:\n\nuploads/\n\n  c0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/   (Tenant: Pharma Corp)\n\n    documents/   (Entity type)\n\n      2026/   (Year)\n\n        02/   (Month)\n\n          daf3c8ad-3660-4c13-8b57-0daf3cc9aaf0_test-upload.txt\n\n          d7cbcb77-a8f1-4e22-b901-3dc77f8e22a1_report-v2.pdf\n\n    capa/\n\n      2026/\n\n        02/\n\n          f1a2b3c4-..._corrective-action-photo.jpg\n\n    training/\n\n      2026/\n\n        01/\n\n          a9b8c7d6-..._sop-training-material.pdf\n\n  d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002/   (Tenant: Another Org)\n\n    documents/\n\n    suppliers/\n\n    temp/   (Temporary storage)\n\n    thumbnails/   (Thumbnail storage)\n\n\n\nStorage Provider Abstraction:\n\nLocalStorageProvider (Phase 1 --- current):\n\nsave(relativePath, buffer) --- Creates directory tree via fs.mkdirSync({recursive: true}), writes buffer via fs.writeFileSync.\n\ndelete(relativePath) --- Removes file via fs.unlinkSync. Silently ignores if file doesn't exist.\n\nexists(relativePath) --- Checks via fs.existsSync.\n\ngetFullPath(relativePath) --- Joins UPLOAD_DIR + relativePath. Controller uses path.resolve() for absolute path.\n\nS3 Migration Path (Phase 2):\n\nImplement S3StorageProvider with identical interface (save, delete, exists, getFullPath). S3 key structure maps 1:1 to local folder hierarchy: s3://{bucket}/{tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{name}.ext. No changes to service or controller code required --- swap provider via configuration.\n\n\n\nSECTION 10 --- REDIS CACHE DETAILS\n\nFile Attachment Service uses 4 Redis cache key patterns with graceful degradation. The service operates normally if Redis is unavailable --- all cache operations are wrapped in try/catch and failures are logged but never block the main operation.\n\n\n\nCache Key Pattern\n\nPurpose\n\nTTL\n\nInvalidation\n\nfile:{tenant_id}:{file_id}\n\nSingle file metadata cache\n\n300s (5 min)\n\nOn update, delete\n\nquota:{tenant_id}\n\nTenant storage quota\n\n60s (1 min)\n\nOn upload, delete, quota update\n\nshare:{share_token}\n\nShare token lookup\n\n3600s (1 hr)\n\nOn revoke\n\nentity_files:{entity_type}:{entity_id}\n\nFiles by entity list\n\n120s (2 min)\n\nOn upload, delete to entity\n\n\n\nRedis Service Integration:\n\nFile: src/infrastructure/cache/redis.service.js --- singleton instance exported as module.exports = new RedisService().\n\nMethods used: get(key, parseJson=true), set(key, value, ttlSeconds), delete(key). Note: The Redis service uses delete() method, NOT del().\n\nCache invalidation method: _invalidateCache(tenantId, fileId, entityType, entityId) --- deletes all relevant cache keys after any write operation (upload, update, delete, share revoke).\n\nLazy initialization: getRedis() function returns singleton Redis instance on first call, returns null if Redis is unavailable. Every cache operation checks for null before proceeding.\n\n\n\nPlatform-level Redis usage that benefits File Attachment Service indirectly:\n\nSession caching: JWT session data cached by AuthService for fast auth validation on every request.\n\nPermission caching: User permissions cached by PermissionService, used by authorization middleware for files:read/files:write/files:admin checks.\n\n\n\nPlanned Phase 2 enhancements:\n\nFile content cache: Large frequently-accessed files cached in Redis for sub-millisecond retrieval.\n\nShare token bloom filter: Probabilistic check before DB lookup for invalid/revoked tokens.\n\nUpload rate limiting: Per-tenant upload rate tracking via Redis INCR + EXPIRE.	<p>SERVICE SPECIFICATION</p><p><strong>File Attachment Services</strong></p><p>QAssure Multi-Tenant SaaS Platform</p><p>Version 1.0   ·   February 2026</p><h1>1. Feature of Service</h1><h3>SERVICE NAME: FILE ATTACHMENT SERVICES</h3><p>Centralised, tenant-isolated, binary file lifecycle engine that governs how files (documents, images, reports, specifications, audit evidence, training materials) are uploaded, stored, versioned, downloaded, previewed, shared, and deleted across multi-tenant regulated environments. All binary file operations across the QAssure platform and module applications are routed through this single service.</p><p><strong>Core capabilities:</strong></p><p><strong>1. File Upload &amp; Storage</strong> --- Single and multi-file upload (up to 10 files per request) with multer memory storage, 100MB max file size enforcement, blocked dangerous extensions (.exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .ps1, .msi, .dll, .com, .scr, .vbs, .js), SHA-256 checksum calculation via crypto.createHash('sha256'), and automatic tenant-scoped folder hierarchy: {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext. Files are linked to any platform entity via entity_type + entity_id (e.g., entity_type='documents', entity_id=document_uuid). Source module is auto-derived from authentication context: module code for combined JWT + API Key mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf') where module identity is captured from the API key even though user identity comes from JWT; 'platform' for JWT-only users; moduleCode for API key-only modules (e.g., 'aice', 'dhf'); or 'api_key' as fallback if an API key has no linked module. Priority order: req.module.code (combined mode) → req.user.moduleCode (API key mode) → 'platform' (JWT mode). Duplicate detection prevents re-upload of identical files to the same entity (enforced by checksum + entity match on active records).</p><p><strong>2. File Versioning</strong> --- Each file supports immutable version history. Uploading a new version via POST /:id/versions marks the previous version as is_current_version=false and creates a new record with incremented version number, linked via previous_version_id. Version history is retrieved via recursive CTE (Common Table Expression) that traverses the chain in both directions, returning complete lineage. Only the current version is returned in standard queries.</p><p><strong>3. Download &amp; Preview</strong> --- Download endpoint (GET /:id/download) serves files with Content-Disposition: attachment header for browser download prompt. Preview endpoint (GET /:id/preview) serves with Content-Disposition: inline for in-browser rendering. Both use storageProvider.getFullPath() with path.resolve() for absolute path resolution. File access is logged in file_access_logs table with user_id, IP address, user agent, and action type.</p><p><strong>4. File Sharing with Token-Based Access</strong> --- Create time-limited, download-limited share links via POST /:id/share. Generates 64-character hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32). Supports configurable parameters: expires_at (absolute timestamp), expires_in_hours (convenience --- auto-converted to expires_at), max_downloads (download cap), share_type ('link' or 'user'), shared_with_user_id, shared_with_email, and permissions ('view' or 'download'). Access via GET /shared/:token is a PUBLIC route (no authentication required). The service validates token existence, checks expiry, enforces max_downloads limit, increments current_downloads counter, and serves the file. Share revocation via DELETE /shares/:shareId deactivates the share.</p><p><strong>5. Storage Quota Management</strong> --- Per-tenant storage quotas tracked in storage_quotas table: max_storage_bytes (default 10GB), used_storage_bytes, file_count, max_file_size_bytes (default 100MB), allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions. Quota auto-creates on first upload if not present. PostgreSQL trigger (trg_update_storage_usage) automatically increments/decrements used_storage_bytes and file_count on INSERT, DELETE, and UPDATE (soft-delete via SET deleted_at). Quota is checked before every upload: individual file size vs max_file_size_bytes, and total used + new file vs max_storage_bytes. Admin-only PUT /quota endpoint allows updating quota limits (requires files:admin permission).</p><p><strong>6. Soft Delete with Hard Delete Option</strong> --- Default DELETE /:id performs soft delete (sets deleted_at timestamp). PostgreSQL trigger automatically decrements quota on soft delete. Hard delete via DELETE /:id?hard=true permanently removes the database record AND the physical file from storage via storageProvider.delete(). Orphaned file cleanup: if database INSERT fails after file is saved to disk, the file is automatically cleaned up in the catch block.</p><p><strong>7. Storage Provider Abstraction (S3-Ready)</strong> --- All file I/O goes through LocalStorageProvider with 4 methods: save(relativePath, buffer), delete(relativePath), exists(relativePath), getFullPath(relativePath). No controller or service code touches the filesystem directly. Migrating to S3 requires implementing an S3StorageProvider with the same interface --- zero code changes in controllers or service logic.</p><p><strong>8. Three Authentication Modes</strong> --- Every endpoint (except public share access) supports three authentication modes via authenticate middleware: (a) JWT only --- QAssure UI users authenticate via Authorization: Bearer header; tenant derived from JWT claims; user permissions enforced via authorize(); (b) JWT + API Key combined --- module applications acting on behalf of a logged-in user send both Authorization: Bearer (JWT from verify-launch-token) and X-API-Key headers; tenant derived from JWT (X-Tenant-ID not needed); user permissions enforced (not module bypass); source_module set from module identity (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf') for accurate audit attribution; (c) API Key + X-Tenant-ID --- module system/cron operations with no user context send X-API-Key and X-Tenant-ID headers; module gets full access bypass on authorize(). This enables QAssure UI users, module applications acting on behalf of users (with real user identity in audit trails), and module background processes to consume the file attachment service. Routes use authorize() for permission checks: files:read for GET endpoints, files:write for POST/PUT/DELETE endpoints, files:admin for quota management.</p><p><strong>9. Multi-Tenant Data Isolation</strong> --- All queries are tenant-scoped. Every file, share, quota, and access log belongs to a tenant_id. API Key middleware validates module-tenant assignment via the tenant_module_access table (enabled = true) before granting access. Missing X-Tenant-ID returns error code MISSING_TENANT. Unassigned tenant returns MODULE_NOT_ASSIGNED. In combined mode (JWT + API Key), if the JWT's tenant does not match the API key's assigned tenant, error code TENANT_MISMATCH is returned; if the module is deactivated for the tenant, error code MODULE_NOT_ACTIVE is returned. Users cannot see or access files belonging to other tenants under any circumstance.</p><p><strong>10. Security Hardening</strong> --- UUID validation middleware on all :id route parameters returns 400 (INVALID_ID_FORMAT) for malformed UUIDs instead of leaking PostgreSQL errors. Error sanitization function (sanitizeErrorResponse) on all 17 controller catch blocks classifies errors into client-safe categories (QUOTA_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, VALIDATION_ERROR, etc.) and returns generic 'An internal error occurred' for unexpected failures --- never exposing constraint names, table structures, or query details. Blocked file extensions prevent executable uploads. Path traversal is impossible because stored names use UUID-based naming, not user-controlled paths.</p><p><strong>11. Observability</strong> --- Redis caching with graceful degradation (file cache 300s TTL, quota 60s, share 3600s, entity files 120s). Elasticsearch indexing for file searchability. File access logging with IP/user-agent tracking. Storage statistics with per-entity-type and per-module breakdowns. All infrastructure dependencies (Redis, Elasticsearch) fail gracefully --- the service continues operating without caching or indexing if either is unavailable.</p><h1>2. Scope</h1><h2>IN SCOPE (Phase 1):</h2><p><strong>Full file CRUD:</strong> upload single file (with auto-generated tenant-scoped storage path, checksum, source_module derivation), upload multiple files (up to 10, parallel via Promise.all), read (single by ID with Redis cache, paginated list with filtering, by entity with pagination), update metadata (description, tags, category, metadata JSONB), soft delete (with quota trigger), hard delete (with physical file removal).</p><p><strong>File versioning:</strong> upload new version (marks previous as not current, increments version number, links via previous_version_id), retrieve version history (recursive CTE traversal in both directions).</p><p><strong>Download and preview</strong> with correct Content-Disposition headers (attachment for download, inline for preview), file access logging, and path resolution via storageProvider abstraction.</p><p><strong>File sharing:</strong> create share link with configurable expiry (expires_at or expires_in_hours), max_downloads cap, share_type (link/user), permissions (view/download). Public access via token (no auth required). Share revocation. Expired/exhausted shares return 404.</p><p><strong>Storage quota management:</strong> auto-create on first upload, per-tenant limits (max_storage_bytes, max_file_size_bytes, allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions), quota enforcement on every upload, admin-only quota configuration updates (files:admin permission), PostgreSQL trigger for automatic used_storage_bytes/file_count tracking on INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.</p><p><strong>Three authentication modes</strong> (JWT only, JWT + API Key combined, API Key + X-Tenant-ID) on all 16 authenticated endpoints via authenticate middleware (1 public route excluded: GET /shared/:token). Combined mode derives tenant from JWT (X-Tenant-ID not needed), enforces user permissions, and sets source_module from module identity for accurate audit attribution.</p><p>Multi-tenant isolation on all read and write operations.</p><p>API Key middleware validates module-tenant access via tenant_module_access table.</p><p>UUID validation middleware on all :id parameters --- returns 400 for invalid UUIDs.</p><p>Error sanitization on all 17 catch blocks --- never leaks database internals.</p><p>File access audit trail via file_access_logs with user_id, IP address, user agent, action.</p><p>Storage statistics with quota summary, file type counts, by_entity and by_module breakdowns.</p><p>Pagination via limit and offset query parameters (default limit 50). Response is a JSON array of file objects.</p><p>Filter support on list: source_module, mime_type, entity_type, category, search (ILIKE on original_name), sort (created_at, file_size, original_name), date range (created_after, created_before).</p><p>Orphaned file cleanup: if DB INSERT fails after file save, file is automatically removed from storage.</p><p>Redis caching with graceful degradation (operates without Redis).</p><p>Elasticsearch indexing with graceful degradation (operates without ES).</p><h2>OUT OF SCOPE (Phase 1 --- File Attachment Service boundary):</h2><p><strong>S3/MinIO object storage migration</strong> --- LocalStorageProvider is production-ready; S3StorageProvider is a config swap planned for Phase 2. Storage provider abstraction is already in place.</p><p><strong>Virus/malware scanning</strong> --- scan_status and scanned_at columns exist in file_attachments table but no scanning service is integrated.</p><p><strong>Image thumbnail generation</strong> --- has_thumbnail, thumbnail_path columns exist but no thumbnail generation pipeline is implemented.</p><p>Full-text content extraction from uploaded files (PDF text extraction, OCR).</p><p>Vector embedding of file content for semantic search via Qdrant.</p><p>Real-time file upload progress (WebSocket-based progress tracking).</p><p>Client-side chunked upload for files larger than 100MB.</p><p>CDN integration for cached file delivery.</p><p>File format conversion (PDF to image, document to PDF, etc.).</p><p>Watermarking or digital stamping of downloaded files.</p><p>Bulk import/export of files.</p><p><strong>File-level access control lists (ACLs)</strong> --- access is controlled at entity level via entity_type permissions, not per-file.</p><p><strong>Retention policy enforcement</strong> --- soft-deleted files remain in database indefinitely until hard-deleted.</p><p><strong>Email/SMS notifications on file events</strong> (handled by Notification Service separately).</p><p><strong>Document lifecycle management</strong> (SOPs, versioning, review/approval) --- handled by separate Document Service (document.service.js).</p><h1>3. Clear Responsibility Split</h1><h2>3.1 SaaS Platform (Owned by Platform Team):</h2><p>Provide and maintain the File Attachment Service as a centralised, tenant-isolated binary file management engine.</p><p>Enforce file upload constraints: 100MB max file size (multer + quota), blocked dangerous extensions, per-tenant storage quotas with auto-creation and trigger-based tracking.</p><p>Generate and manage tenant-scoped storage paths: {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext.</p><p>Calculate SHA-256 checksums on every upload for integrity verification.</p><p>Auto-derive source_module from authentication context with priority: req.module.code for combined JWT + API Key mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf'), req.user.moduleCode for API key-only modules, 'platform' for JWT-only users, 'api_key' fallback for API keys without linked modules. This ensures files uploaded by modules on behalf of users are correctly attributed to the originating module in storage statistics.</p><p>Manage file versioning: version number increment, previous_version_id linking, is_current_version flagging, recursive CTE version history retrieval.</p><p>Maintain storage provider abstraction (LocalStorageProvider) with save, delete, exists, getFullPath methods for future S3 migration.</p><p>Enforce tenant isolation on all queries via tenant_id filtering. No cross-tenant file access is possible.</p><p>Provide three authentication modes on all 16 authenticated endpoints via authenticate middleware (1 public route excluded: GET /shared/:token): (a) JWT only for QAssure UI users, (b) JWT + API Key combined for module applications acting on behalf of logged-in users (tenant from JWT, user permissions enforced, source_module from module identity), (c) API Key + X-Tenant-ID for module system/cron operations.</p><p>Validate module-tenant access via tenant_module_access table (enabled = true check). Return MISSING_TENANT or MODULE_NOT_ASSIGNED errors for invalid API Key requests. In combined mode, return TENANT_MISMATCH if JWT tenant differs from API key's assigned tenant, and MODULE_NOT_ACTIVE if the module is deactivated for the tenant.</p><p>Provide UUID validation middleware for all route parameters. Return 400 INVALID_ID_FORMAT for malformed UUIDs.</p><p>Sanitise all error responses to prevent database internal leakage.</p><p>Provide file sharing infrastructure: token generation, expiry enforcement, max_downloads enforcement, public access route.</p><p>Provide storage statistics with per-entity-type and per-module breakdowns.</p><p>Log all file access events (download, preview, checkout, checkin) in file_access_logs.</p><p>Provide Redis caching and Elasticsearch indexing with graceful degradation.</p><p>Expose admin-only quota management endpoint (files:admin permission).</p><h2>3.2 Module Applications (Residing on Platform; Owned by App Teams --- LTTS):</h2><p>Use the File Attachment Service API with the appropriate authentication mode:</p><p><strong>For user-context operations (user uploads a file via module UI):</strong> Send both Authorization: Bearer (JWT obtained from verify-launch-token) and X-API-Key headers. X-Tenant-ID is NOT needed --- tenant is derived from JWT. User permissions (files:read, files:write) are enforced. uploaded_by and file_access_logs.user_id record the real user identity. source_module records the module identity (e.g., 'coc').</p><p><strong>For system/cron operations (no user context):</strong> Send X-API-Key + X-Tenant-ID headers. Module gets full access bypass. source_module records the module identity from API key.</p><p>Specify entity_type and entity_id when uploading files to link them to the correct module entity (e.g., entity_type='documents', entity_id=&lt;document_uuid&gt; for Document Service; entity_type='capa', entity_id=&lt;capa_uuid&gt; for CAPA module).</p><p>Provide required fields on upload: file (multipart), entity_type (string), entity_id (UUID). Optional fields: description, category, tags, metadata (JSONB).</p><p>Use the version upload endpoint (POST /:id/versions) for updating files rather than deleting and re-uploading. This preserves version history and audit trail.</p><p>Use the share endpoint to generate time-limited, download-limited links for external stakeholders (e.g., auditors, suppliers) without granting platform login access.</p><p>Do NOT implement custom file storage logic --- always delegate to platform's file attachment service.</p><p>Do NOT store file metadata in the module's own database --- use platform as the system of record for all file attachments. Use the entity link (entity_type + entity_id) to associate files with module records.</p><p>Do NOT construct file paths manually or access the uploads directory directly --- always use service API endpoints for file access.</p><p>Use SSO launch token flow to obtain both tenant context and user session JWT dynamically in production: call POST /modules/verify-launch-token with X-API-Key and the launch token to receive a JWT (24h expiry), user details (including department, designation, user category), tenant details, and permissions. Use this JWT in Authorization: Bearer header alongside X-API-Key for all user-context platform calls. Use .env TENANT_ID + X-Tenant-ID header for development and system/cron operations only.</p><h1>4. API List (Refer to Excel Sheet shared)</h1><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>#</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Method</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Endpoint</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Auth</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>1</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>POST</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/upload</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write</p></td><td><p>Upload single file (multipart)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>2</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>POST</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/upload/multiple</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write</p></td><td><p>Upload multiple files (up to 10)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>3</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read</p></td><td><p>List files (paginated, filterable)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>4</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Get single file by ID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>5</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>PUT</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Update file metadata</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>6</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>DELETE</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Delete file (soft; ?hard=true for permanent)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>7</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/download</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Download file (Content-Disposition: attachment)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>8</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/preview</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Preview file (Content-Disposition: inline)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>9</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>POST</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/versions</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Upload new version of existing file</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>10</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/versions</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Get version history (recursive CTE)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>11</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>POST</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/share</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Create share link (token, expiry, max_downloads)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>12</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>DELETE</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/shares/:shareId</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Revoke share link</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>13</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/shared/:token</p></td><td><p>PUBLIC (no auth)</p></td><td><p>Access shared file via token</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>14</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/entity/:entity_type/:entity_id</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Get files by entity (paginated)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>15</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/stats</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read</p></td><td><p>Get storage statistics (by entity, by module)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>16</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/quota</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read</p></td><td><p>Get tenant storage quota</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>17</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>PUT</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/quota</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:admin</p></td><td><p>Update tenant storage quota (admin only)</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Route ordering note: /stats, /quota, /entity/:type/:id, /shared/:token are registered BEFORE /:id to prevent Express matching static segments as UUID parameters.</em></p><h1>5. Typical Workflow</h1><h2>5.1 Write Path (File Upload &amp; Management):</h2><p><strong>1. Upload Single File:</strong> Tenant user or module calls POST /api/v1/files/upload with multipart form data: file (required, binary), entity_type (required, e.g., 'documents'), entity_id (required, UUID of parent entity), and optional: description, category, tags (comma-separated string or JSON array), metadata (JSONB). The API validates: file presence (returns VALIDATION_ERROR 'No file uploaded'), entity_type and entity_id presence (returns VALIDATION_ERROR 'entity_type and entity_id are required'), file extension not in blocked list (.exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .ps1, .msi, .dll, .com, .scr, .vbs, .js --- returns error 'File type .exe is not allowed'), file size under 100MB (returns FILE_TOO_LARGE 'File size exceeds 100MB limit'), tenant quota not exceeded (returns QUOTA_ERROR for both individual file and total storage).</p><p>Platform generates: stored_name as {uuid}_{sanitized_original_name}.ext, storage path as {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{stored_name}, SHA-256 checksum via crypto.createHash('sha256').update(buffer).digest('hex'), source_module derived from auth context with priority: req.module.code for combined mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf'), 'platform' for JWT-only users, req.user.moduleCode for API key-only modules (e.g., 'aice', 'dhf'), or 'api_key' fallback if API key has no linked module. File is saved to storage via storageProvider.save(relativePath, buffer), then database record is inserted into file_attachments. If DB INSERT fails, file is automatically cleaned up from storage (orphan prevention). Redis cache is invalidated for entity files list. Elasticsearch index is updated via IndexingHooks. Returns full file object with 201 status.</p><p><strong>2. Upload Multiple Files:</strong> POST /api/v1/files/upload/multiple accepts up to 10 files via multer array ('files' field, max 10). All files are uploaded in parallel via Promise.all, sharing the same entity_type and entity_id. Returns array of results with per-file success/error status. Quota is checked per file individually.</p><p><strong>3. Update Metadata:</strong> PUT /api/v1/files/:id updates allowed fields: description (text), category (varchar), tags (cast as text[]), metadata (cast as JSONB). File content changes go through versioning (POST /:id/versions), not metadata update. Sets updated_at timestamp. Returns 'No valid fields to update' error if no recognized fields provided. Returns full file object with 200 status.</p><p><strong>4. Soft Delete:</strong> DELETE /api/v1/files/:id sets deleted_at = NOW() timestamp. PostgreSQL trigger (trg_update_storage_usage) automatically decrements used_storage_bytes and file_count in storage_quotas using GREATEST(..., 0) to prevent negative values. File remains on disk for potential recovery. Redis cache invalidated. Elasticsearch index updated. Returns { success: true, message: 'File deleted' }.</p><p><strong>5. Hard Delete:</strong> DELETE /api/v1/files/:id?hard=true permanently removes: database record (DELETE FROM file_attachments WHERE id = $1 AND tenant_id = $2), physical file from storage via storageProvider.delete(file_path), thumbnail if exists via storageProvider.delete(thumbnail_path). Returns 404 on subsequent GET. Irreversible. Quota adjusts via DELETE trigger.</p><h2>5.2 Versioning:</h2><p><strong>Minor Versioning:</strong> Default behavior. Every POST /api/v1/files/:id/versions with new file (multipart) performs: fetches current record by ID and tenant_id, marks it as is_current_version=false via UPDATE, inserts new record with version = previous_version + 1, is_current_version=true, previous_version_id = old record ID. SHA-256 checksum is calculated for the new file. Both old and new records remain in database --- version history is immutable and never deleted.</p><p><strong>Version History Retrieval:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/:id/versions uses a recursive CTE (Common Table Expression) that traverses the previous_version_id chain in both directions (forward via self-join on previous_version_id, backward via matching previous_version_id = id). Returns complete version lineage with: id, version, file_size, checksum, original_name, uploaded_by_email (resolved via LEFT JOIN users), created_at for each version. Ordered by version number ascending.</p><p><strong>Version Chain Structure:</strong> file_attachments.previous_version_id creates a self-referencing linked list. Version 1 has previous_version_id=null. Version 2 points to Version 1. Version 3 points to Version 2. Only the latest version has is_current_version=true. Standard queries (list, get by entity) only return current versions (WHERE is_current_version = true AND deleted_at IS NULL).</p><h2>5.3 Read/Search Path:</h2><p><strong>Get by ID:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/:id --- Redis cached (300s TTL). Returns full file object with uploaded_by_email resolved via LEFT JOIN users. Filters by tenant_id for isolation.</p><p><strong>List Files:</strong> GET /api/v1/files?limit=50&amp;offset=0 --- returns a JSON array of file objects. Supports limit and offset query parameters for pagination. Supports filters: source_module, mime_type, entity_type, category, search (ILIKE on original_name), sort_by (created_at|file_size|original_name), sort_order (ASC|DESC), created_after, created_before. Only returns active files (deleted_at IS NULL, is_current_version = true).</p><p><strong>Get by Entity:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/entity/:entity_type/:entity_id --- returns a JSON array of all files linked to a specific entity. Used by Document Service, CAPA module, Training module, etc. to retrieve their linked files.</p><p><strong>Storage Stats:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/stats --- returns four sections: quota (max_storage, used_storage, available, usage_percent), files (total, images, pdfs, documents counts), by_entity (count + size per entity_type), and by_module (count + size per source_module e.g., 'platform', 'coc').</p><p><strong>Storage Quota:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/quota --- returns current quota status: max_storage_bytes, used_storage_bytes, file_count, max_file_size_bytes, allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions, usage_percentage.</p><h2>5.4 File Sharing Path:</h2><p><strong>Create Share:</strong> POST /api/v1/files/:id/share with body: share_type ('link'|'user'), permissions ('view'|'download'), expires_at (ISO timestamp) or expires_in_hours (number, auto-converted), max_downloads (integer), shared_with_user_id, shared_with_email. Service generates 64-char hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32). Returns share object with share_token, share_url, expires_at, max_downloads. Redis cached (3600s TTL).</p><p><strong>Access Shared File:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/shared/:token --- PUBLIC route (no authentication). Service: looks up share by token (Redis cached), validates expiry (expires_at &gt; NOW()), validates download count (current_downloads &lt; max_downloads), increments current_downloads, resolves file path via storageProvider.getFullPath(), serves file with correct Content-Type and Content-Disposition headers. Returns 404 if share not found, expired, or download limit reached.</p><p><strong>Revoke Share:</strong> DELETE /api/v1/files/shares/:shareId --- sets is_active=false. Invalidates Redis cache for the share token.</p><h2>5.5 Retention/Deletion:</h2><p>Phase 1: No automated retention policy enforcement. Soft-deleted files remain in database with deleted_at timestamp set. Hard delete permanently removes file and database record.</p><p><strong>Quota Recovery:</strong> Soft delete triggers automatic quota decrement via PostgreSQL trigger. Restoring a soft-deleted file (clearing deleted_at) would trigger quota increment.</p><p><strong>Planned Phase 2:</strong> Configurable retention periods per entity_type. Scheduled cleanup job to hard-delete files past retention period. Archived storage tier for long-term retention at reduced cost.</p><h2>5.6 Audit Trail:</h2><p>file_access_logs records (inserted on download, preview, and any file access): file_id, tenant_id, user_id, action ('download'|'preview'|'access'), ip_address (from req.ip), user_agent (from req.headers), created_at.</p><p>Storage quota changes tracked via PostgreSQL trigger --- every INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on file_attachments automatically adjusts used_storage_bytes and file_count.</p><p>Share access tracked via current_downloads counter and last_accessed_at timestamp on file_shares.</p><p><strong>Authentication mode impacts audit attribution:</strong> In combined JWT + API Key mode, uploaded_by and file_access_logs.user_id record the real user identity (from JWT), while source_module records the originating module (from API key). This provides GxP-compliant traceability --- auditors can see both who performed the action and which module facilitated it. In API Key-only mode, uploaded_by records the module service account and source_module records the module code. In JWT-only mode, uploaded_by records the platform user and source_module is set to 'platform'.</p><h1>6. PostgreSQL DB --- MODEL</h1><p>The File Attachment Service uses 4 PostgreSQL tables: file_attachments (master record with binary file metadata, entity linking, versioning, and storage path), storage_quotas (per-tenant storage limits with trigger-maintained usage counters), file_shares (token-based file sharing with expiry and download limits), and file_access_logs (audit trail for file access events). All tables enforce multi-tenant isolation via tenant_id foreign key with ON DELETE CASCADE. The file_attachments table serves as the central entity. A PostgreSQL trigger function (update_storage_usage) automatically maintains used_storage_bytes and file_count in storage_quotas on INSERT, UPDATE (soft-delete/restore), and DELETE operations.</p><h2>6.1 ER Diagram:</h2><p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p><p><em>Figure 6.1: Entity Relationship Diagram --- File Attachment Service</em></p><p>file_attachments.tenant_id → tenants.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)</p><p>file_attachments.uploaded_by → users.id</p><p>file_attachments.previous_version_id → file_attachments.id (self-referencing version chain)</p><p>storage_quotas.tenant_id → tenants.id (UNIQUE --- one quota per tenant)</p><p>file_shares.tenant_id → tenants.id, file_shares.file_id → file_attachments.id</p><p>file_access_logs.file_id → file_attachments.id, file_access_logs.user_id → users.id</p><h2>6.2 Entities &amp; Attributes:</h2><h3>6.2.1 Entity: file_attachments (32 columns)</h3><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Data Type</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Constraint / FK</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Example</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>PK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()</p></td><td><p>Unique file identifier</p></td><td><p>daf3c8ad-...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tenant_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, INDEX</p></td><td><p>Tenant isolation</p></td><td><p>c0000000-...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>original_name</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(500)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>User-uploaded filename</p></td><td><p>test-upload.txt</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>stored_name</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(500)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>UUID-based stored name</p></td><td><p>daf3c8ad_test-upload.txt</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_path</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(1000)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>Relative storage path</p></td><td><p>c000.../documents/2026/02/daf3...txt</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>mime_type</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(255)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>MIME type</p></td><td><p>text/plain</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_size</strong></p></td><td><p>BIGINT</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>File size in bytes</p></td><td><p>18</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>checksum</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(128)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>SHA-256 hash</p></td><td><p>a591a6d40...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>storage_provider</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'local'</p></td><td><p>Storage backend</p></td><td><p>local</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>storage_bucket</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(255)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>S3 bucket (Phase 2)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>storage_region</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(100)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>S3 region (Phase 2)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>entity_type</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(100)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, INDEX</p></td><td><p>Parent entity type</p></td><td><p>documents</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>entity_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, INDEX</p></td><td><p>Parent entity ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>category</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(100)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>File category</p></td><td><p>specification</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>description</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>File description</p></td><td><p>Test file upload</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tags</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT[]</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>PostgreSQL text array</p></td><td><p>{sop,quality}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>version</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 1</p></td><td><p>Version number</p></td><td><p>1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>is_current_version</strong></p></td><td><p>BOOLEAN</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT true, INDEX (partial)</p></td><td><p>Active version flag</p></td><td><p>true</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>previous_version_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>FK → file_attachments(id), Nullable</p></td><td><p>Version chain link</p></td><td><p>UUID or null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>is_public</strong></p></td><td><p>BOOLEAN</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT false</p></td><td><p>Public access flag</p></td><td><p>false</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>access_level</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'private'</p></td><td><p>Access level</p></td><td><p>private</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>download_count</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 0</p></td><td><p>Total downloads</p></td><td><p>5</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>has_thumbnail</strong></p></td><td><p>BOOLEAN</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT false</p></td><td><p>Thumbnail exists</p></td><td><p>false</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>thumbnail_path</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(1000)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Thumbnail storage path</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>metadata</strong></p></td><td><p>JSONB</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT '{}'</p></td><td><p>Extensible metadata</p></td><td><p>{}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>scan_status</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Virus scan status (Phase 2)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>scanned_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Scan timestamp (Phase 2)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>uploaded_by</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>FK → users(id), Nullable</p></td><td><p>Uploader user ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>source_module</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(100)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'platform', INDEX</p></td><td><p>Origin module</p></td><td><p>platform</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Created timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>updated_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Updated timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>deleted_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>Nullable, INDEX</p></td><td><p>Soft delete timestamp</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>NOTES: tags is TEXT[] not JSONB. file_size is BIGINT (returns as string from node-pg, parsed to integer in _formatAttachment). is_current_version partial index filters WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND is_current_version = TRUE. previous_version_id creates a self-referencing linked list for version chains. source_module is auto-derived from auth context, never user-supplied.</em></p><h3>6.2.2 Entity: storage_quotas (10 columns)</h3><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Data Type</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Constraint / FK</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Example</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>PK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()</p></td><td><p>Quota record ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tenant_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → tenants(id), UNIQUE</p></td><td><p>Tenant isolation</p></td><td><p>c0000000-...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>max_storage_bytes</strong></p></td><td><p>BIGINT</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 10737418240 (10GB)</p></td><td><p>Max total storage</p></td><td><p>10737418240</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>used_storage_bytes</strong></p></td><td><p>BIGINT</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 0</p></td><td><p>Current usage (trigger-maintained)</p></td><td><p>1536</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_count</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 0</p></td><td><p>Active file count (trigger-maintained)</p></td><td><p>15</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>max_file_size_bytes</strong></p></td><td><p>BIGINT</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 104857600 (100MB)</p></td><td><p>Max single file size</p></td><td><p>104857600</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>allowed_mime_types</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT[]</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Whitelist (null = all allowed)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>blocked_extensions</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT[]</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Blacklist</p></td><td><p>{.exe,.bat}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Created timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>updated_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Updated timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>NOTES: max_storage_bytes and used_storage_bytes are BIGINT. PostgreSQL trigger update_storage_usage() maintains used_storage_bytes and file_count automatically on file_attachments INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE. The trigger uses GREATEST(..., 0) to prevent negative values. Quota auto-creates via service when first upload occurs for a tenant.</em></p><h3>PostgreSQL Trigger Function:</h3><p>CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_storage_usage() --- Handles INSERT (increment), DELETE (decrement), UPDATE with NEW.deleted_at IS NOT NULL AND OLD.deleted_at IS NULL (soft-delete decrement), UPDATE with NEW.deleted_at IS NULL AND OLD.deleted_at IS NOT NULL (restore increment). Uses GREATEST(used_storage_bytes - file_size, 0) and GREATEST(file_count - 1, 0) to prevent negative values.</p><h3>6.2.3 Entity: file_shares (15 columns)</h3><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Data Type</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Constraint / FK</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Example</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>PK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()</p></td><td><p>Share record ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tenant_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE</p></td><td><p>Tenant isolation</p></td><td><p>c0000000-...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → file_attachments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE</p></td><td><p>Shared file</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>share_token</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(255)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, UNIQUE</p></td><td><p>64-char hex token</p></td><td><p>a3f8c2d1...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>share_type</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'link'</p></td><td><p>Share type</p></td><td><p>link</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>shared_with_user_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>FK → users(id), Nullable</p></td><td><p>Target user (for 'user' type)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>shared_with_email</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(255)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Target email</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>permissions</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'view'</p></td><td><p>Access level</p></td><td><p>view/download</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>expires_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Expiry timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>max_downloads</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Download cap (null = unlimited)</p></td><td><p>5</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>current_downloads</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 0</p></td><td><p>Downloads consumed</p></td><td><p>2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>is_active</strong></p></td><td><p>BOOLEAN</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT true</p></td><td><p>Active flag (false = revoked)</p></td><td><p>true</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>last_accessed_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Last access time</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_by</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>FK → users(id), Nullable</p></td><td><p>Share creator</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Created timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>NOTES: share_token is UNIQUE. expires_at can be set directly or auto-calculated from expires_in_hours (service converts: new Date(Date.now() + hours * 3600000).toISOString()). max_downloads null means unlimited. current_downloads is incremented atomically on each access. is_active=false means share has been revoked.</em></p><h3>6.2.4 Entity: file_access_logs (8 columns)</h3><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Data Type</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Constraint / FK</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Example</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>PK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()</p></td><td><p>Log record ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tenant_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE</p></td><td><p>Tenant isolation</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → file_attachments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE</p></td><td><p>File accessed</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>user_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → users(id)</p></td><td><p>Who accessed</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>action</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>Action type</p></td><td><p>download/preview/access</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>ip_address</strong></p></td><td><p>INET</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Client IP</p></td><td><p>192.168.1.1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>user_agent</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Browser UA string</p></td><td><p>Mozilla/5.0...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>When accessed</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>NOTES: Records are insert-only (append-only audit log). ip_address and user_agent are captured from Express request object when available. action values include 'download', 'preview', 'access' for share access.</em></p><h1>7. Qdrant (Vector DB)</h1><p><strong>Phase 1 Status: NOT USED by File Attachment Service.</strong></p><p>Binary file content is stored on the filesystem via LocalStorageProvider. File metadata is stored in PostgreSQL (file_attachments table). No vector embeddings of file content are generated in Phase 1.</p><h2>Planned for Phase 2:</h2><p>Collection Name: file_content_vec_v1</p><p>Vector Dimension: 1536 (OpenAI text-embedding-3-small) or 768 (sentence-transformers)</p><p>Payload Fields: file_id (string), tenant_id (string --- mandatory filter), original_name (string), entity_type (string), entity_id (string), mime_type (string), category (string), source_module (string), created_at (ISO string)</p><p>Payload Indexes: tenant_id, entity_type, mime_type, source_module, created_at</p><p>Use Case: Semantic search across extracted file content (PDF text, document text), similar file discovery, AI-powered content recommendations, duplicate detection via vector similarity rather than checksum matching.</p><p>Prerequisite: Content extraction pipeline (PDF text extraction, OCR for images, document parsing) must be implemented first to generate text from binary files before vector embedding.</p><h1>8. Object Storage</h1><h2>Folder Structure Hierarchy:</h2><p>Root: UPLOAD_DIR (default: ./uploads/, configurable via environment variable)</p><p>Pattern: {UPLOAD_DIR}/{tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext</p><p><strong>Example hierarchy:</strong></p><p>uploads/</p><p>  c0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/   (Tenant: Pharma Corp)</p><p>    documents/   (Entity type)</p><p>      2026/   (Year)</p><p>        02/   (Month)</p><p>          daf3c8ad-3660-4c13-8b57-0daf3cc9aaf0_test-upload.txt</p><p>          d7cbcb77-a8f1-4e22-b901-3dc77f8e22a1_report-v2.pdf</p><p>    capa/</p><p>      2026/</p><p>        02/</p><p>          f1a2b3c4-..._corrective-action-photo.jpg</p><p>    training/</p><p>      2026/</p><p>        01/</p><p>          a9b8c7d6-..._sop-training-material.pdf</p><p>  d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002/   (Tenant: Another Org)</p><p>    documents/</p><p>    suppliers/</p><p>    temp/   (Temporary storage)</p><p>    thumbnails/   (Thumbnail storage)</p><h3>Storage Provider Abstraction:</h3><p>LocalStorageProvider (Phase 1 --- current):</p><p>save(relativePath, buffer) --- Creates directory tree via fs.mkdirSync({recursive: true}), writes buffer via fs.writeFileSync.</p><p>delete(relativePath) --- Removes file via fs.unlinkSync. Silently ignores if file doesn't exist.</p><p>exists(relativePath) --- Checks via fs.existsSync.</p><p>getFullPath(relativePath) --- Joins UPLOAD_DIR + relativePath. Controller uses path.resolve() for absolute path.</p><h3>S3 Migration Path (Phase 2):</h3><p>Implement S3StorageProvider with identical interface (save, delete, exists, getFullPath). S3 key structure maps 1:1 to local folder hierarchy: s3://{bucket}/{tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{name}.ext. No changes to service or controller code required --- swap provider via configuration.</p><h1>SECTION 10 --- REDIS CACHE DETAILS</h1><p>File Attachment Service uses 4 Redis cache key patterns with graceful degradation. The service operates normally if Redis is unavailable --- all cache operations are wrapped in try/catch and failures are logged but never block the main operation.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Cache Key Pattern</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Purpose</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>TTL</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Invalidation</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>file:{tenant_id}:{file_id}</p></td><td><p>Single file metadata cache</p></td><td><p>300s (5 min)</p></td><td><p>On update, delete</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>quota:{tenant_id}</p></td><td><p>Tenant storage quota</p></td><td><p>60s (1 min)</p></td><td><p>On upload, delete, quota update</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>share:{share_token}</p></td><td><p>Share token lookup</p></td><td><p>3600s (1 hr)</p></td><td><p>On revoke</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>entity_files:{entity_type}:{entity_id}</p></td><td><p>Files by entity list</p></td><td><p>120s (2 min)</p></td><td><p>On upload, delete to entity</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Redis Service Integration:</h3><p>File: src/infrastructure/cache/redis.service.js --- singleton instance exported as module.exports = new RedisService().</p><p>Methods used: get(key, parseJson=true), set(key, value, ttlSeconds), delete(key). Note: The Redis service uses delete() method, NOT del().</p><p>Cache invalidation method: _invalidateCache(tenantId, fileId, entityType, entityId) --- deletes all relevant cache keys after any write operation (upload, update, delete, share revoke).</p><p>Lazy initialization: getRedis() function returns singleton Redis instance on first call, returns null if Redis is unavailable. Every cache operation checks for null before proceeding.</p><h3>Platform-level Redis usage that benefits File Attachment Service indirectly:</h3><p><strong>Session caching:</strong> JWT session data cached by AuthService for fast auth validation on every request.</p><p><strong>Permission caching:</strong> User permissions cached by PermissionService, used by authorization middleware for files:read/files:write/files:admin checks.</p><h3>Planned Phase 2 enhancements:</h3><p><strong>File content cache:</strong> Large frequently-accessed files cached in Redis for sub-millisecond retrieval.</p><p><strong>Share token bloom filter:</strong> Probabilistic check before DB lookup for invalid/revoked tokens.</p><p><strong>Upload rate limiting:</strong> Per-tenant upload rate tracking via Redis INCR + EXPIRE.</p>	Initial draft	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	4ccf68ad-485c-495a-935b-10d74b173a52	2026-03-26 05:45:34.977844+00	platform	\N
b9ad5621-6a57-4c62-bad7-25e124a062ef	06d73554-562d-4cd9-8562-a2dd2a852b60	352d7e21-5155-4ff8-8169-284bf5ece3e7	0.4	0	4	approved	Document-service-api-guide.pdf	352d7e21-5155-4ff8-8169-284bf5ece3e7/documents/2026/03/0314fb37-eb20-4ce5-a563-3d13c9144a79_document-service-api-guide.pdf	491250	application/pdf	a9d8cc9c883f16b07d9b8100ae9d443982c32d8d9219f13859bba19f8b6b34fa	QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nQAssure\nDocument Service API Integration Guide\nFor Module Developers\nAudience \tModule Developers integrating with QAssure Document\nManagement Service\nBase URL (Dev) \thttp://localhost:3000/api/v1\nBase URL (Prod) \thttps://backendqassure.tech4bizsolutions.com/\napi/v1\nLast Verified \t28-Feb-2026 (all 17 endpoints verified)\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 1 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n1. What is the Document Service?\nThe QAssure Document Service provides a centralized, controlled document management system for\nquality-regulated environments (e.g., Pharma, Manufacturing). It allows modules to:\n• Create and manage controlled documents (SOPs, Policies, Forms, Work Instructions, etc.)\n• Version-control document content with major/minor versioning (e.g., 0.1 → 0.2 → 1.0)\n• Drive a full document lifecycle from draft → in_review → approved → effective → obsolete\n• Lock documents for editing via a Checkout/Checkin mechanism (prevents concurrent edits)\n• Auto-number documents by type and year (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)\n• Trigger periodic review alerts based on category-defined review frequencies\n• Maintain a complete audit trail with workflow history, access logs, and user attribution\n2. Authentication Modes\nThe Document Service supports three authentication modes. Choose based on your module's use case:\nMode A — JWT Only (QAssure UI Users)\nStandard user login via the QAssure UI. Best for direct user-driven operations.\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt_token>\nMode B — JWT + API Key (Combined / Recommended for Modules)\nYour module launches via SSO, obtains a module_jwt, and sends both the JWT and your module's API Key. This\nis the recommended mode for user-context operations.\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\n💡 Advantages of Mode B: Audit trail records the real user identity (not a service account). User's actual\nrole-based permissions are enforced. Module identity is tracked for source attribution. X-Tenant-ID is not\nneeded — tenant is derived from the JWT.\nMode C — API Key + Tenant ID (System / Cron Operations)\nFor background module operations with no user context (automated jobs, cron tasks).\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\nX-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid>\n⚠ Requires document:read and document:write permissions configured in api_key_permissions table.\n3. SSO / Module Launch Flow (Recommended)\nFollow these 3 steps to obtain a module_jwt for Mode B (JWT + API Key):\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 2 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nStep 1 — User Logs into QAssure\nPOST /api/v1/auth/login\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"email": "admin@yourcompany.com",\n"password": "YourPassword"\n}\nResponse: Save data.access_token as jwt_token.\nStep 2 — Launch Your Module\nPOST /api/v1/modules/<your_module_id>/launch\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt_token>\nResponse: Contains data.launch_url with a ?token=<launch_token> parameter. Extract and save the\nlaunch_token.\nStep 3 — Verify Launch Token (Exchange for Module Session JWT)\nPOST /api/v1/modules/verify-launch-token\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"token": "<launch_token>"\n}\nResponse Fields:\nField \tDescription\ndata.token \tModule session JWT — use as Bearer token for all subsequent API calls\ndata.user \tFull user object (id, email, name, department, designation)\ndata.tenant \tTenant details (id, name, slug, company_name, logo)\ndata.permissions \tArray of permission strings granted to this user\ndata.module \tModule identity info\ndata.expires_in \t86400 (24 hours)\ndata.expires_at \tISO timestamp of expiry\nSave data.token as your module_jwt. Use it with Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt> + X-API-Key:\n<your_api_key> for all subsequent document API calls.\n4. Permissions Required\nPermission \tDescription\ndocument:read \tView documents, categories, versions, due-for-review list\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 3 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPermission \tDescription\ndocument:write \tCreate, update, version, checkout/checkin, and all lifecycle actions\nWho gets these permissions automatically:\n• Tenant Admin — has both document:read and document:write (seeded)\n• Super Admin — bypasses all permission checks\n• Custom Roles — when a Tenant Admin grants document permissions\n• API Key (Mode C) — requires explicit document:read / document:write in api_key_permissions table\n• JWT + API Key (Mode B) — user's actual role-based permissions are enforced\n5. API Reference\n5.1 Reference Data APIs\nThese are the first APIs to call. They return static/seeded data your module needs to build dropdowns, filter\noptions, and validate inputs.\nGET /api/v1/documents/categories\nReturns tenant-scoped document categories.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nQuery Parameters \tNone\nExample Request (Mode B):\nGET /api/v1/documents/categories\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [\n{\n"id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",\n"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",\n"code": "SOP",\n"description": "SOPs for regulated operations",\n"parent_id": null,\n"requires_training": true,\n"retention_years": 10,\n"review_frequency_months": 12\n},\n{\n"id": "...",\n"name": "Forms",\n"code": "FRM",\n"review_frequency_months": 24\n}\n]\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 4 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n}\nCategory List (Pharma Corp tenant):\nCode \tName \tReview Frequency\nFRM \tForms \t24 months\nPOL \tPolicies \t12 months\nQM \tQuality Manual \t12 months\nSPEC \tSpecifications \t12 months\nSOP \tStandard Operating Procedures \t12 months\nWI \tWork Instructions \t24 months\n💡 Developer Tip: Save category.id from this response — you will need it in category_id when creating\ndocuments. The review_frequency_months field is used to auto-calculate next_review_date when a document\nbecomes effective.\nGET /api/v1/documents/types\nReturns all available document type codes. No document:read permission required — only authentication.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tAuthenticated only\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [\n{ "code": "SOP", "name": "Standard Operating Procedure" },\n{ "code": "WI", "name": "Work Instruction" },\n{ "code": "POL", "name": "Policy" },\n{ "code": "FRM", "name": "Form" },\n{ "code": "SPEC", "name": "Specification" },\n{ "code": "QM", "name": "Quality Manual" },\n{ "code": "PROC", "name": "Procedure" },\n{ "code": "GUIDE", "name": "Guideline" },\n{ "code": "REF", "name": "Reference Document" }\n]\n}\n💡 The code value is what you pass as document_type when creating a document. The auto-number prefix is\nderived from this code (e.g., SOP-2026-0001).\nGET /api/v1/documents/statuses\nReturns all possible document lifecycle statuses. No document:read permission required.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tAuthenticated only\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 5 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [\n{ "code": "draft", \t"name": "Draft", \t"description": "Document is being created or\nedited" },\n{ "code": "in_review", "name": "In Review", "description": "Document is under review" },\n{ "code": "approved", "name": "Approved", "description": "Document has been approved" },\n{ "code": "effective", "name": "Effective", "description": "Document is currently in effect"\n},\n{ "code": "obsolete", "name": "Obsolete", "description": "Document has been superseded" },\n{ "code": "archived", "name": "Archived", "description": "Document is archived for\nhistorical purposes" }\n]\n}\nGET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review\nReturns effective documents whose next_review_date falls within the specified window. Useful for building\ncompliance dashboards or sending review reminders.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nQuery Parameters:\nParameter \tType \tDefault \tDescription\ndays_ahead \tinteger \t30 \tNumber of days ahead to check\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=90\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n• Only returns documents with a non-null next_review_date (i.e., documents linked to a category)\n• Documents without a category will never appear here (their next_review_date is null)\n5.2 Document CRUD APIs\nPOST /api/v1/documents — Create Document\nCreates a new controlled document. An initial version 0.1 is auto-created. Document number is auto-generated.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tHTTP 201 — Full 19-field document object\nRequest Body Fields:\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 6 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\ntitle \tstring \tRequired \tDocument title (max 500 chars)\ndocument_type \tstring \tRequired \tType code from GET /types (e.g., "SOP")\ndescription \tstring \tOptional \tShort description\ncontent \tstring \tOptional \tPlain-text document body (stored in version 0.1)\ncontent_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of the content\ndepartment \tstring \tOptional \tOwning department name\ncategory_id \tUUID \tOptional \tCategory UUID from GET /categories\nowner_id \tUUID \tOptional \tUser UUID; defaults to the authenticated user\ntags \tstring[] \tOptional \tArray of tag strings\ncustom_fields \tobject \tOptional \tAny additional JSONB metadata\nExample Request (Mode B):\nPOST /api/v1/documents\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"description": "Standard operating procedure for sterile manufacturing",\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Gowning",\n"department": "Manufacturing",\n"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",\n"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "gowning"]\n}\nExample Request (Mode C — API Key only):\nPOST /api/v1/documents\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\nX-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Module-Created SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure"\n}\nAuto-behaviors:\n• document_number auto-generated: <TYPE>-<YEAR>-<NNNN> (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)\n• status defaults to "draft"\n• Initial version 0.1 is auto-created in document_versions table\n• IndexingHooks.indexDocument() is triggered for search indexing\nValidation Error (HTTP 400):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "title and document_type are required" }\n}\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 7 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nGET /api/v1/documents — List Documents\nLists documents for the tenant with pagination and filtering.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nQuery Parameters:\nParameter \tType \tDescription\nlimit \tinteger \tResults per page (default: 50)\noffset \tinteger \tPagination offset (default: 0)\nstatus \tstring \tFilter by status code (e.g., draft, effective)\ncategory_id \tUUID \tFilter by category UUID\ndocument_type \tstring \tFilter by type code (e.g., SOP)\nowner_id \tUUID \tFilter by owner UUID\nsearch \tstring \tFull-text ILIKE search on title, document_number, description\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents?status=effective&document_type=SOP&limit=20&offset=0\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [ /* array of Document Summary objects */ ],\n"pagination": {\n"total": 47,\n"limit": 20,\n"offset": 0\n}\n}\nGET /api/v1/documents/:id — Get Single Document\nReturns full details for a single document by its UUID.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tFull 19-field document object\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 8 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n⚠ Checkout status is NOT included in this response. It is tracked separately in the document_checkouts table.\nNot Found (HTTP 404):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": { "code": "NOT_FOUND", "message": "Document not found" }\n}\nPUT /api/v1/documents/:id — Update Document Metadata\nUpdates document metadata only. Content changes must go through versioning (POST /versions).\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tFull 19-field updated document object\nUpdatable Fields:\nField \tType \tDescription\ntitle \tstring \tDocument title\ndescription \tstring \tDescription\ncategory_id \tUUID \tChange category\nowner_id \tUUID \tReassign owner\ndepartment \tstring \tDepartment\ntags \tstring[] \tReplace tags array\ncustom_fields \tobject \tReplace custom JSONB metadata\nExample Request:\nPUT /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP - Revised",\n"department": "Quality Assurance",\n"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "updated"]\n}\n5.3 Version Management APIs\nDocuments use major.minor versioning. Each new version resets the document to draft status.\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 9 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nVersion Type \tExample Transition \tis_major_version\nMinor edit \t0.1 → 0.2 \tfalse (default)\nMajor revision \t0.2 → 1.0, 1.3 → 2.0 \ttrue\nGET /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — List Versions\nReturns all versions for a document, ordered from newest to oldest.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tArray of 13-field version objects\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n⚠ content is NOT included in the version list response — only metadata is returned.\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — Create New Version\nCreates a new version of a document. The document status is reset to draft — it must go through the review\nprocess again.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tHTTP 201 — New 13-field version object\nRequest Body Fields:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\ncontent \tstring \tOptional \tNew plain-text content body\ncontent_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of content\nchange_summary \tstring \tOptional \tBrief description of what changed\nchange_reason \tstring \tOptional \tReason category (e.g., minor_edit, regulatory_update)\nis_major_version \tboolean \tOptional \ttrue for major version bump (default: false)\nfile_name \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file name\nfile_path \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file path/URL\nfile_size \tinteger \tOptional \tFile size in bytes\nmime_type \tstring \tOptional \tMIME type of attached file\nMinor Version Example:\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 10 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. References\\nISO 14644, EU GMP Annex 1",\n"change_summary": "Added references section",\n"change_reason": "minor_edit"\n}\nMajor Version Example:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"content": "Complete rewrite per new regulatory requirements.",\n"change_summary": "Major revision per EU GMP Annex 1 update",\n"change_reason": "regulatory_update",\n"is_major_version": true\n}\nKey Behaviors:\n• SHA-256 hash is auto-calculated from content for integrity verification\n• Document current_version_id is updated to the new version\n• Document status is reset to "draft"\n5.4 Checkout / Checkin APIs\nThe checkout/checkin mechanism prevents concurrent editing by granting an exclusive 24-hour lock on a\ndocument.\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkout — Checkout Document\nLocks the document for exclusive editing by the current user.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\nreason \tstring \tOptional \tWhy the document is being checked out\nExample Request:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Adding new section on environmental monitoring"\n}\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 11 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPossible Responses:\nScenario \tResponse\nSuccessful new checkout \t{ "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "<ISO timestamp +24h>" }\nSame user re-checking out \t{ "already_checked_out": true, "by_current_user": true }\nDifferent user has it checked out \tHTTP 500 — "Document is already checked out by another user"\n• Checkout expires automatically after 24 hours\n• Checkout status is logged in document_access_log\n• Checkout status is NOT visible in the GET /documents/:id response\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkin — Checkin Document\nReleases the exclusive lock. Only the user who performed the checkout can check in.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nRequest Body \tEmpty {} or no body required\nExample Request:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\nSuccess Response: { "checked_in": true }\nError Response (wrong user): "Document is not checked out by you"\n5.5 Lifecycle Workflow APIs\nThese endpoints drive the document through its full lifecycle. Always run them in the correct order.\n💡 Lifecycle Flow: draft → [Submit] → in_review → [Approve] → approved → [Make Effective] → effective →\n[Obsolete] → obsolete. OR: in_review / approved → [Reject] → draft (re-submit to restart)\nAll lifecycle endpoints return the full 19-field document object.\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/submit — Submit for Review\nSubmits a draft document for review. Starts a document_approval workflow instance.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 12 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nAttribute \tValue\nAllowed From \tdraft status only\nRequest Body \tEmpty {} required\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\nWhat happens internally:\n1. Validates document is in draft status\n2. Calls workflowEngine.startWorkflow({ workflowCode: 'document_approval', ... })\n3. Sets document status = 'in_review'\n4. Saves workflow_instance_id on the document\n5. Updates current version's status to in_review\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/approve — Approve Document\nApproves a document that is under review. Logs in workflow history.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \tin_review status only\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\ncomments \tstring \tOptional \tApproval comments\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"comments": "Reviewed and approved per QA checklist"\n}\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/reject — Reject Document\nRejects a document and returns it to draft. Logs in workflow history.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \tin_review or approved status\nRequest Body:\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 13 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\nreason \tstring \tRequired \tMust provide a rejection reason\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/reject\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Needs additional safety section per regulatory requirement"\n}\nValidation Error (missing reason):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": {\n"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",\n"message": "reason is required when rejecting a document"\n}\n}\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/make-effective — Make Effective\nMarks an approved document as effective. Auto-calculates the next review date.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \tapproved status only\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\neffective_date \tstring (ISO date) \tRequired \te.g., "2026-03-01" or "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"\nsignature_id \tUUID \tOptional \te-Signature UUID if applicable\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"effective_date": "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"\n}\nAuto-calculation of next_review_date:\n• If document has a category_id → next_review_date = effective_date +\ncategory.review_frequency_months\n• If no category → next_review_date = null\n• Example: SOP category has 12-month review → next_review_date = effective + 12 months\n⚠ Does NOT insert workflow history — this is by design in the current implementation.\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 14 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/obsolete — Make Obsolete\nMarks an effective document as obsolete (superseded).\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \teffective status only\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\nreason \tstring \tRequired \tWhy this document is being obsoleted\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Superseded by new revision SOP-2026-0010"\n}\nWhat happens internally:\n• Sets obsolete_date = NOW()\n• Inserts into workflow_history (action = 'obsolete', comments = reason) if workflow_instance_id exists\nValidation Error (missing reason):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": {\n"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",\n"message": "reason is required when making a document obsolete"\n}\n}\n6. Document Lifecycle State Machine\nFrom Status \tAction \tTo Status \tRequired Fields\ndraft \tSubmit \tin_review \t—\nin_review \tApprove \tapproved \tcomments (optional)\nin_review \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)\napproved \tMake Effective \teffective \teffective_date (required)\napproved \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)\neffective \tObsolete \tobsolete \treason (required)\n⚠ Creating a new version (POST /versions) from any status always resets the document to draft.\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 15 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nState Flow:\ndraft ──[Submit]──► in_review ──[Approve]──► approved ──[Make Effective]──►\neffective\n▲ \t│ \t│ \t│\n│ \t[Reject] \t[Reject]\n[Obsolete]\n└───────────────────────┘◄─────────────────────────┘ \t▼\nobsolete\n7. Response Schemas\nDocument Object (Full — 19 Fields)\nReturned by: POST /documents, GET /documents/:id, PUT /documents/:id, and all lifecycle endpoints.\n{\n"id": "uuid",\n"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",\n"description": "Description text",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"category": {\n"id": "uuid",\n"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",\n"code": "SOP"\n},\n"status": "draft",\n"current_version": "0.1",\n"version_status": "draft",\n"owner": {\n"id": "uuid",\n"email": "admin@company.com",\n"name": "Jane Doe"\n},\n"department": "Manufacturing",\n"effective_date": "2026-03-01",\n"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",\n"tags": ["sterile", "gmp"],\n"custom_fields": {},\n"workflow_instance_id": "uuid or null",\n"created_by": "admin@company.com",\n"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z",\n"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"\n}\nDocument Summary (10 Fields)\nReturned by: GET /documents (list) and GET /documents/due-for-review.\n{\n"id": "uuid",\n"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"category": "Standard Operating Procedures",\n"status": "effective",\n"current_version": "1.0",\n"owner": "admin@company.com",\n"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 16 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"\n}\nVersion Object (13 Fields)\nReturned by: GET /documents/:id/versions and POST /documents/:id/versions.\n{\n"id": "uuid",\n"version_number": "0.2",\n"major_version": 0,\n"minor_version": 2,\n"status": "draft",\n"file": {\n"name": "document.pdf",\n"path": "/uploads/document.pdf",\n"size": 204800,\n"mime_type": "application/pdf",\n"hash": "sha256-hex-string"\n},\n"change_summary": "Added references section",\n"change_reason": "minor_edit",\n"approved_by": "approver@company.com",\n"approved_at": "2026-02-28T11:00:00Z",\n"signature_id": "uuid or null",\n"created_by": "author@company.com",\n"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:30:00Z"\n}\n💡 file is null if no file attachment exists. content field is NOT included in the version list response.\n8. Error Reference\nAll errors follow a consistent format:\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": {\n"code": "ERROR_CODE",\n"message": "Human-readable message"\n}\n}\nHTTP\nStatus Code \tMessage \tWhen\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR title and document_type are required \tCreating without required fields\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when rejecting a\ndocument Reject without reason\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR effective_date is required \tMake Effective without date\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when making a\ndocument obsolete Obsolete without reason\n404 \tNOT_FOUND \tDocument not found Document not found or wrong\ntenant\n500 \tCREATE_ERROR \terror detail \tDB or internal error on create\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 17 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nHTTP\nStatus Code \tMessage \tWhen\n500 \tCHECKOUT_ERROR Document is already checked out by\nanother user Concurrent checkout\n500 \tCHECKIN_ERROR \tDocument is not checked out by you \tWrong user trying to checkin\n500 \tSUBMIT_ERROR Only draft documents can be submitted\nfor review Wrong status\n500 \tAPPROVE_ERROR Only documents in review can be\napproved Wrong status\n500 \tREJECT_ERROR Only documents in review or approved\ncan be rejected Wrong status\n500 MAKE_EFFECTIVE_E\nRROR\nOnly approved documents can be made\neffective Wrong status\n500 \tOBSOLETE_ERROR Only effective documents can be made\nobsolete Wrong status\n9. Module Integration Patterns\nPattern 1: Module Creates a Document on Behalf of a User (Most Common)\nUse Mode B (JWT + API Key). The audit trail will show the real user.\n1. User logs in to QAssure → get jwt_token\n2. User launches your module → get launch_token\n3. Module backend calls verify-launch-token → get module_jwt\n4. Module calls POST /documents with:\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n5. Document owner/created_by = real user (not your module)\nPattern 2: Module Does Background / Automated Document Operations\nUse Mode C (API Key + Tenant ID). No user context needed.\n1. Configure document:read + document:write in api_key_permissions for your API key\n2. All requests include:\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nX-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid>\n3. No user JWT needed\n4. Audit trail shows module identity (no user)\nPattern 3: Module Shows a Document Compliance Dashboard\n6. Call GET /documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=30 to get documents needing attention\n7. Call GET /documents?status=effective to list currently active documents\n8. Call GET /documents?status=draft to list documents pending submission\n9. Call GET /documents/categories to build category filter dropdowns\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 18 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPattern 4: Module Manages Full Document Authoring Workflow\n1. Create document \t→ POST /documents\n2. Checkout for editing \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkout\n3. Create new version with edits → POST /documents/:id/versions\n4. Checkin \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkin\n5. Submit for review \t→ POST /documents/:id/submit\n6. Approve (by QA) \t→ POST /documents/:id/approve\n7. Make effective (by admin) \t→ POST /documents/:id/make-effective\n8. (Later) Obsolete when superseded → POST /documents/:id/obsolete\n10. Complete Workflow Example\nA complete, annotated request/response sequence for creating and publishing a document via Combined Auth\n(Mode B).\nStep 1 — Get Categories\nGET /api/v1/documents/categories\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n→ Note the id for the SOP category (e.g., 6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5)\nStep 2 — Create Document\nPOST /api/v1/documents\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Equipment Calibration SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"description": "Procedure for equipment calibration in production areas",\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Calibration Steps",\n"department": "Engineering",\n"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",\n"tags": ["calibration", "equipment", "gmp"]\n}\n→ Status: draft, Version: 0.1, document_number: SOP-2026-0002\n→ Save the data.id as document_id\nStep 3 — Checkout for Editing\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Adding section 4 - Frequency of Calibration"\n}\n→ Response: { "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "..." }\nStep 4 — Create a New Version (Minor Edit)\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 19 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. Frequency\\n4.1 Monthly for critical\nequipment",\n"change_summary": "Added frequency section",\n"change_reason": "minor_edit"\n}\n→ Version bumped to 0.2, document status reset to draft\nStep 5 — Checkin\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\n→ Response: { "checked_in": true }\nStep 6 — Submit for Review\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\n→ Status: in_review, workflow_instance_id is now populated\nStep 7 — Approve\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"comments": "Reviewed and approved - meets regulatory standards"\n}\n→ Status: approved\nStep 8 — Make Effective\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"effective_date": "2026-03-17T00:00:00Z"\n}\n→ Status: effective\n→ next_review_date auto-calculated: 2027-03-17 (SOP category = 12 months)\nStep 9 — (Future) Obsolete When Superseded\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 20 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n"reason": "Superseded by Equipment Calibration SOP v2.0 (SOP-2026-0015)"\n}\n→ Status: obsolete, obsolete_date = NOW()\nQuick Reference Card\nAPI Meth\nod Endpoint \tPermission \tRequired Body Fields\nGet Categories \tGET \t/documents/categories \tdocument:read \t—\nGet Types \tGET \t/documents/types \tAuth only \t—\nGet Statuses \tGET \t/documents/statuses \tAuth only \t—\nDue for Review \tGET /documents/due-for-revi\new document:read \t—\nList Documents \tGET \t/documents \tdocument:read \t—\nGet Document \tGET \t/documents/:id \tdocument:read \t—\nCreate Document POST /documents \tdocument:write title, document_type\nUpdate Document PUT \t/documents/:id \tdocument:write at least one field\nGet Versions \tGET \t/documents/:id/versions document:read \t—\nCreate Version \tPOST /documents/:id/versions document:write —\nCheckout \tPOST /documents/:id/checkout document:write —\nCheckin \tPOST /documents/:id/checkin document:write —\nSubmit for Review POST /documents/:id/submit \tdocument:write {}\nApprove \tPOST /documents/:id/approve document:write —\nReject \tPOST /documents/:id/reject \tdocument:write reason (mandatory)\nMake Effective \tPOST /documents/:id/make-eff\nective document:write effective_date (mandatory)\nObsolete \tPOST /documents/:id/obsolete document:write reason (mandatory)\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 21 of 21 --	<p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>QAssure</p><p>Document Service API Integration Guide</p><p>For Module Developers</p><p>Audience \tModule Developers integrating with QAssure Document</p><p>Management Service</p><p>Base URL (Dev) \thttp://localhost:3000/api/v1</p><p>Base URL (Prod) \thttps://backendqassure.tech4bizsolutions.com/</p><p>api/v1</p><p>Last Verified \t28-Feb-2026 (all 17 endpoints verified)</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 1 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>1. What is the Document Service?</p><p>The QAssure Document Service provides a centralized, controlled document management system for</p><p>quality-regulated environments (e.g., Pharma, Manufacturing). It allows modules to:</p><p>• Create and manage controlled documents (SOPs, Policies, Forms, Work Instructions, etc.)</p><p>• Version-control document content with major/minor versioning (e.g., 0.1 → 0.2 → 1.0)</p><p>• Drive a full document lifecycle from draft → in_review → approved → effective → obsolete</p><p>• Lock documents for editing via a Checkout/Checkin mechanism (prevents concurrent edits)</p><p>• Auto-number documents by type and year (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)</p><p>• Trigger periodic review alerts based on category-defined review frequencies</p><p>• Maintain a complete audit trail with workflow history, access logs, and user attribution</p><p>2. Authentication Modes</p><p>The Document Service supports three authentication modes. Choose based on your module's use case:</p><p>Mode A — JWT Only (QAssure UI Users)</p><p>Standard user login via the QAssure UI. Best for direct user-driven operations.</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token></p><p>Mode B — JWT + API Key (Combined / Recommended for Modules)</p><p>Your module launches via SSO, obtains a module_jwt, and sends both the JWT and your module's API Key. This</p><p>is the recommended mode for user-context operations.</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>💡 Advantages of Mode B: Audit trail records the real user identity (not a service account). User's actual</p><p>role-based permissions are enforced. Module identity is tracked for source attribution. X-Tenant-ID is not</p><p>needed — tenant is derived from the JWT.</p><p>Mode C — API Key + Tenant ID (System / Cron Operations)</p><p>For background module operations with no user context (automated jobs, cron tasks).</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>X-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid></p><p>⚠ Requires document:read and document:write permissions configured in api_key_permissions table.</p><p>3. SSO / Module Launch Flow (Recommended)</p><p>Follow these 3 steps to obtain a module_jwt for Mode B (JWT + API Key):</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 2 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Step 1 — User Logs into QAssure</p><p>POST /api/v1/auth/login</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"email": "admin@yourcompany.com",</p><p>"password": "YourPassword"</p><p>}</p><p>Response: Save data.access_token as jwt_token.</p><p>Step 2 — Launch Your Module</p><p>POST /api/v1/modules/<your_module_id>/launch</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token></p><p>Response: Contains data.launch_url with a ?token=<launch_token> parameter. Extract and save the</p><p>launch_token.</p><p>Step 3 — Verify Launch Token (Exchange for Module Session JWT)</p><p>POST /api/v1/modules/verify-launch-token</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"token": "<launch_token>"</p><p>}</p><p>Response Fields:</p><p>Field \tDescription</p><p>data.token \tModule session JWT — use as Bearer token for all subsequent API calls</p><p>data.user \tFull user object (id, email, name, department, designation)</p><p>data.tenant \tTenant details (id, name, slug, company_name, logo)</p><p>data.permissions \tArray of permission strings granted to this user</p><p>data.module \tModule identity info</p><p>data.expires_in \t86400 (24 hours)</p><p>data.expires_at \tISO timestamp of expiry</p><p>Save data.token as your module_jwt. Use it with Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt> + X-API-Key:</p><p><your_api_key> for all subsequent document API calls.</p><p>4. Permissions Required</p><p>Permission \tDescription</p><p>document:read \tView documents, categories, versions, due-for-review list</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 3 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Permission \tDescription</p><p>document:write \tCreate, update, version, checkout/checkin, and all lifecycle actions</p><p>Who gets these permissions automatically:</p><p>• Tenant Admin — has both document:read and document:write (seeded)</p><p>• Super Admin — bypasses all permission checks</p><p>• Custom Roles — when a Tenant Admin grants document permissions</p><p>• API Key (Mode C) — requires explicit document:read / document:write in api_key_permissions table</p><p>• JWT + API Key (Mode B) — user's actual role-based permissions are enforced</p><p>5. API Reference</p><p>5.1 Reference Data APIs</p><p>These are the first APIs to call. They return static/seeded data your module needs to build dropdowns, filter</p><p>options, and validate inputs.</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/categories</p><p>Returns tenant-scoped document categories.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Query Parameters \tNone</p><p>Example Request (Mode B):</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/categories</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",</p><p>"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",</p><p>"code": "SOP",</p><p>"description": "SOPs for regulated operations",</p><p>"parent_id": null,</p><p>"requires_training": true,</p><p>"retention_years": 10,</p><p>"review_frequency_months": 12</p><p>},</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "...",</p><p>"name": "Forms",</p><p>"code": "FRM",</p><p>"review_frequency_months": 24</p><p>}</p><p>]</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 4 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>}</p><p>Category List (Pharma Corp tenant):</p><p>Code \tName \tReview Frequency</p><p>FRM \tForms \t24 months</p><p>POL \tPolicies \t12 months</p><p>QM \tQuality Manual \t12 months</p><p>SPEC \tSpecifications \t12 months</p><p>SOP \tStandard Operating Procedures \t12 months</p><p>WI \tWork Instructions \t24 months</p><p>💡 Developer Tip: Save category.id from this response — you will need it in category_id when creating</p><p>documents. The review_frequency_months field is used to auto-calculate next_review_date when a document</p><p>becomes effective.</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/types</p><p>Returns all available document type codes. No document:read permission required — only authentication.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tAuthenticated only</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [</p><p>{ "code": "SOP", "name": "Standard Operating Procedure" },</p><p>{ "code": "WI", "name": "Work Instruction" },</p><p>{ "code": "POL", "name": "Policy" },</p><p>{ "code": "FRM", "name": "Form" },</p><p>{ "code": "SPEC", "name": "Specification" },</p><p>{ "code": "QM", "name": "Quality Manual" },</p><p>{ "code": "PROC", "name": "Procedure" },</p><p>{ "code": "GUIDE", "name": "Guideline" },</p><p>{ "code": "REF", "name": "Reference Document" }</p><p>]</p><p>}</p><p>💡 The code value is what you pass as document_type when creating a document. The auto-number prefix is</p><p>derived from this code (e.g., SOP-2026-0001).</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/statuses</p><p>Returns all possible document lifecycle statuses. No document:read permission required.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tAuthenticated only</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 5 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [</p><p>{ "code": "draft", \t"name": "Draft", \t"description": "Document is being created or</p><p>edited" },</p><p>{ "code": "in_review", "name": "In Review", "description": "Document is under review" },</p><p>{ "code": "approved", "name": "Approved", "description": "Document has been approved" },</p><p>{ "code": "effective", "name": "Effective", "description": "Document is currently in effect"</p><p>},</p><p>{ "code": "obsolete", "name": "Obsolete", "description": "Document has been superseded" },</p><p>{ "code": "archived", "name": "Archived", "description": "Document is archived for</p><p>historical purposes" }</p><p>]</p><p>}</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review</p><p>Returns effective documents whose next_review_date falls within the specified window. Useful for building</p><p>compliance dashboards or sending review reminders.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Query Parameters:</p><p>Parameter \tType \tDefault \tDescription</p><p>days_ahead \tinteger \t30 \tNumber of days ahead to check</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=90</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>• Only returns documents with a non-null next_review_date (i.e., documents linked to a category)</p><p>• Documents without a category will never appear here (their next_review_date is null)</p><p>5.2 Document CRUD APIs</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents — Create Document</p><p>Creates a new controlled document. An initial version 0.1 is auto-created. Document number is auto-generated.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tHTTP 201 — Full 19-field document object</p><p>Request Body Fields:</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 6 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>title \tstring \tRequired \tDocument title (max 500 chars)</p><p>document_type \tstring \tRequired \tType code from GET /types (e.g., "SOP")</p><p>description \tstring \tOptional \tShort description</p><p>content \tstring \tOptional \tPlain-text document body (stored in version 0.1)</p><p>content_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of the content</p><p>department \tstring \tOptional \tOwning department name</p><p>category_id \tUUID \tOptional \tCategory UUID from GET /categories</p><p>owner_id \tUUID \tOptional \tUser UUID; defaults to the authenticated user</p><p>tags \tstring[] \tOptional \tArray of tag strings</p><p>custom_fields \tobject \tOptional \tAny additional JSONB metadata</p><p>Example Request (Mode B):</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"description": "Standard operating procedure for sterile manufacturing",</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Gowning",</p><p>"department": "Manufacturing",</p><p>"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",</p><p>"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "gowning"]</p><p>}</p><p>Example Request (Mode C — API Key only):</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>X-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Module-Created SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure"</p><p>}</p><p>Auto-behaviors:</p><p>• document_number auto-generated: <TYPE>-<YEAR>-<NNNN> (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)</p><p>• status defaults to "draft"</p><p>• Initial version 0.1 is auto-created in document_versions table</p><p>• IndexingHooks.indexDocument() is triggered for search indexing</p><p>Validation Error (HTTP 400):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "title and document_type are required" }</p><p>}</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 7 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents — List Documents</p><p>Lists documents for the tenant with pagination and filtering.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Query Parameters:</p><p>Parameter \tType \tDescription</p><p>limit \tinteger \tResults per page (default: 50)</p><p>offset \tinteger \tPagination offset (default: 0)</p><p>status \tstring \tFilter by status code (e.g., draft, effective)</p><p>category_id \tUUID \tFilter by category UUID</p><p>document_type \tstring \tFilter by type code (e.g., SOP)</p><p>owner_id \tUUID \tFilter by owner UUID</p><p>search \tstring \tFull-text ILIKE search on title, document_number, description</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents?status=effective&document_type=SOP&limit=20&offset=0</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [ /* array of Document Summary objects */ ],</p><p>"pagination": {</p><p>"total": 47,</p><p>"limit": 20,</p><p>"offset": 0</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/:id — Get Single Document</p><p>Returns full details for a single document by its UUID.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tFull 19-field document object</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 8 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>⚠ Checkout status is NOT included in this response. It is tracked separately in the document_checkouts table.</p><p>Not Found (HTTP 404):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": { "code": "NOT_FOUND", "message": "Document not found" }</p><p>}</p><p>PUT /api/v1/documents/:id — Update Document Metadata</p><p>Updates document metadata only. Content changes must go through versioning (POST /versions).</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tFull 19-field updated document object</p><p>Updatable Fields:</p><p>Field \tType \tDescription</p><p>title \tstring \tDocument title</p><p>description \tstring \tDescription</p><p>category_id \tUUID \tChange category</p><p>owner_id \tUUID \tReassign owner</p><p>department \tstring \tDepartment</p><p>tags \tstring[] \tReplace tags array</p><p>custom_fields \tobject \tReplace custom JSONB metadata</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>PUT /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP - Revised",</p><p>"department": "Quality Assurance",</p><p>"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "updated"]</p><p>}</p><p>5.3 Version Management APIs</p><p>Documents use major.minor versioning. Each new version resets the document to draft status.</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 9 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Version Type \tExample Transition \tis_major_version</p><p>Minor edit \t0.1 → 0.2 \tfalse (default)</p><p>Major revision \t0.2 → 1.0, 1.3 → 2.0 \ttrue</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — List Versions</p><p>Returns all versions for a document, ordered from newest to oldest.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tArray of 13-field version objects</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>⚠ content is NOT included in the version list response — only metadata is returned.</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — Create New Version</p><p>Creates a new version of a document. The document status is reset to draft — it must go through the review</p><p>process again.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tHTTP 201 — New 13-field version object</p><p>Request Body Fields:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>content \tstring \tOptional \tNew plain-text content body</p><p>content_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of content</p><p>change_summary \tstring \tOptional \tBrief description of what changed</p><p>change_reason \tstring \tOptional \tReason category (e.g., minor_edit, regulatory_update)</p><p>is_major_version \tboolean \tOptional \ttrue for major version bump (default: false)</p><p>file_name \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file name</p><p>file_path \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file path/URL</p><p>file_size \tinteger \tOptional \tFile size in bytes</p><p>mime_type \tstring \tOptional \tMIME type of attached file</p><p>Minor Version Example:</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 10 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. References\\nISO 14644, EU GMP Annex 1",</p><p>"change_summary": "Added references section",</p><p>"change_reason": "minor_edit"</p><p>}</p><p>Major Version Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"content": "Complete rewrite per new regulatory requirements.",</p><p>"change_summary": "Major revision per EU GMP Annex 1 update",</p><p>"change_reason": "regulatory_update",</p><p>"is_major_version": true</p><p>}</p><p>Key Behaviors:</p><p>• SHA-256 hash is auto-calculated from content for integrity verification</p><p>• Document current_version_id is updated to the new version</p><p>• Document status is reset to "draft"</p><p>5.4 Checkout / Checkin APIs</p><p>The checkout/checkin mechanism prevents concurrent editing by granting an exclusive 24-hour lock on a</p><p>document.</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkout — Checkout Document</p><p>Locks the document for exclusive editing by the current user.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>reason \tstring \tOptional \tWhy the document is being checked out</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Adding new section on environmental monitoring"</p><p>}</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 11 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Possible Responses:</p><p>Scenario \tResponse</p><p>Successful new checkout \t{ "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "<ISO timestamp +24h>" }</p><p>Same user re-checking out \t{ "already_checked_out": true, "by_current_user": true }</p><p>Different user has it checked out \tHTTP 500 — "Document is already checked out by another user"</p><p>• Checkout expires automatically after 24 hours</p><p>• Checkout status is logged in document_access_log</p><p>• Checkout status is NOT visible in the GET /documents/:id response</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkin — Checkin Document</p><p>Releases the exclusive lock. Only the user who performed the checkout can check in.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Request Body \tEmpty {} or no body required</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>Success Response: { "checked_in": true }</p><p>Error Response (wrong user): "Document is not checked out by you"</p><p>5.5 Lifecycle Workflow APIs</p><p>These endpoints drive the document through its full lifecycle. Always run them in the correct order.</p><p>💡 Lifecycle Flow: draft → [Submit] → in_review → [Approve] → approved → [Make Effective] → effective →</p><p>[Obsolete] → obsolete. OR: in_review / approved → [Reject] → draft (re-submit to restart)</p><p>All lifecycle endpoints return the full 19-field document object.</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/submit — Submit for Review</p><p>Submits a draft document for review. Starts a document_approval workflow instance.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 12 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Allowed From \tdraft status only</p><p>Request Body \tEmpty {} required</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>What happens internally:</p><p>1. Validates document is in draft status</p><p>2. Calls workflowEngine.startWorkflow({ workflowCode: 'document_approval', ... })</p><p>3. Sets document status = 'in_review'</p><p>4. Saves workflow_instance_id on the document</p><p>5. Updates current version's status to in_review</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/approve — Approve Document</p><p>Approves a document that is under review. Logs in workflow history.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \tin_review status only</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>comments \tstring \tOptional \tApproval comments</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"comments": "Reviewed and approved per QA checklist"</p><p>}</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/reject — Reject Document</p><p>Rejects a document and returns it to draft. Logs in workflow history.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \tin_review or approved status</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 13 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>reason \tstring \tRequired \tMust provide a rejection reason</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/reject</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Needs additional safety section per regulatory requirement"</p><p>}</p><p>Validation Error (missing reason):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": {</p><p>"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",</p><p>"message": "reason is required when rejecting a document"</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/make-effective — Make Effective</p><p>Marks an approved document as effective. Auto-calculates the next review date.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \tapproved status only</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>effective_date \tstring (ISO date) \tRequired \te.g., "2026-03-01" or "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"</p><p>signature_id \tUUID \tOptional \te-Signature UUID if applicable</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"effective_date": "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>Auto-calculation of next_review_date:</p><p>• If document has a category_id → next_review_date = effective_date +</p><p>category.review_frequency_months</p><p>• If no category → next_review_date = null</p><p>• Example: SOP category has 12-month review → next_review_date = effective + 12 months</p><p>⚠ Does NOT insert workflow history — this is by design in the current implementation.</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 14 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/obsolete — Make Obsolete</p><p>Marks an effective document as obsolete (superseded).</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \teffective status only</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>reason \tstring \tRequired \tWhy this document is being obsoleted</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Superseded by new revision SOP-2026-0010"</p><p>}</p><p>What happens internally:</p><p>• Sets obsolete_date = NOW()</p><p>• Inserts into workflow_history (action = 'obsolete', comments = reason) if workflow_instance_id exists</p><p>Validation Error (missing reason):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": {</p><p>"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",</p><p>"message": "reason is required when making a document obsolete"</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>6. Document Lifecycle State Machine</p><p>From Status \tAction \tTo Status \tRequired Fields</p><p>draft \tSubmit \tin_review \t—</p><p>in_review \tApprove \tapproved \tcomments (optional)</p><p>in_review \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)</p><p>approved \tMake Effective \teffective \teffective_date (required)</p><p>approved \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)</p><p>effective \tObsolete \tobsolete \treason (required)</p><p>⚠ Creating a new version (POST /versions) from any status always resets the document to draft.</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 15 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>State Flow:</p><p>draft ──[Submit]──► in_review ──[Approve]──► approved ──[Make Effective]──►</p><p>effective</p><p>▲ \t│ \t│ \t│</p><p>│ \t[Reject] \t[Reject]</p><p>[Obsolete]</p><p>└───────────────────────┘◄─────────────────────────┘ \t▼</p><p>obsolete</p><p>7. Response Schemas</p><p>Document Object (Full — 19 Fields)</p><p>Returned by: POST /documents, GET /documents/:id, PUT /documents/:id, and all lifecycle endpoints.</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",</p><p>"description": "Description text",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"category": {</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",</p><p>"code": "SOP"</p><p>},</p><p>"status": "draft",</p><p>"current_version": "0.1",</p><p>"version_status": "draft",</p><p>"owner": {</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"email": "admin@company.com",</p><p>"name": "Jane Doe"</p><p>},</p><p>"department": "Manufacturing",</p><p>"effective_date": "2026-03-01",</p><p>"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",</p><p>"tags": ["sterile", "gmp"],</p><p>"custom_fields": {},</p><p>"workflow_instance_id": "uuid or null",</p><p>"created_by": "admin@company.com",</p><p>"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z",</p><p>"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>Document Summary (10 Fields)</p><p>Returned by: GET /documents (list) and GET /documents/due-for-review.</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"category": "Standard Operating Procedures",</p><p>"status": "effective",</p><p>"current_version": "1.0",</p><p>"owner": "admin@company.com",</p><p>"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 16 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>Version Object (13 Fields)</p><p>Returned by: GET /documents/:id/versions and POST /documents/:id/versions.</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"version_number": "0.2",</p><p>"major_version": 0,</p><p>"minor_version": 2,</p><p>"status": "draft",</p><p>"file": {</p><p>"name": "document.pdf",</p><p>"path": "/uploads/document.pdf",</p><p>"size": 204800,</p><p>"mime_type": "application/pdf",</p><p>"hash": "sha256-hex-string"</p><p>},</p><p>"change_summary": "Added references section",</p><p>"change_reason": "minor_edit",</p><p>"approved_by": "approver@company.com",</p><p>"approved_at": "2026-02-28T11:00:00Z",</p><p>"signature_id": "uuid or null",</p><p>"created_by": "author@company.com",</p><p>"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:30:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>💡 file is null if no file attachment exists. content field is NOT included in the version list response.</p><p>8. Error Reference</p><p>All errors follow a consistent format:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": {</p><p>"code": "ERROR_CODE",</p><p>"message": "Human-readable message"</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>HTTP</p><p>Status Code \tMessage \tWhen</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR title and document_type are required \tCreating without required fields</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when rejecting a</p><p>document Reject without reason</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR effective_date is required \tMake Effective without date</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when making a</p><p>document obsolete Obsolete without reason</p><p>404 \tNOT_FOUND \tDocument not found Document not found or wrong</p><p>tenant</p><p>500 \tCREATE_ERROR \terror detail \tDB or internal error on create</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 17 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>HTTP</p><p>Status Code \tMessage \tWhen</p><p>500 \tCHECKOUT_ERROR Document is already checked out by</p><p>another user Concurrent checkout</p><p>500 \tCHECKIN_ERROR \tDocument is not checked out by you \tWrong user trying to checkin</p><p>500 \tSUBMIT_ERROR Only draft documents can be submitted</p><p>for review Wrong status</p><p>500 \tAPPROVE_ERROR Only documents in review can be</p><p>approved Wrong status</p><p>500 \tREJECT_ERROR Only documents in review or approved</p><p>can be rejected Wrong status</p><p>500 MAKE_EFFECTIVE_E</p><p>RROR</p><p>Only approved documents can be made</p><p>effective Wrong status</p><p>500 \tOBSOLETE_ERROR Only effective documents can be made</p><p>obsolete Wrong status</p><p>9. Module Integration Patterns</p><p>Pattern 1: Module Creates a Document on Behalf of a User (Most Common)</p><p>Use Mode B (JWT + API Key). The audit trail will show the real user.</p><p>1. User logs in to QAssure → get jwt_token</p><p>2. User launches your module → get launch_token</p><p>3. Module backend calls verify-launch-token → get module_jwt</p><p>4. Module calls POST /documents with:</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>5. Document owner/created_by = real user (not your module)</p><p>Pattern 2: Module Does Background / Automated Document Operations</p><p>Use Mode C (API Key + Tenant ID). No user context needed.</p><p>1. Configure document:read + document:write in api_key_permissions for your API key</p><p>2. All requests include:</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>X-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid></p><p>3. No user JWT needed</p><p>4. Audit trail shows module identity (no user)</p><p>Pattern 3: Module Shows a Document Compliance Dashboard</p><p>6. Call GET /documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=30 to get documents needing attention</p><p>7. Call GET /documents?status=effective to list currently active documents</p><p>8. Call GET /documents?status=draft to list documents pending submission</p><p>9. Call GET /documents/categories to build category filter dropdowns</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 18 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Pattern 4: Module Manages Full Document Authoring Workflow</p><p>1. Create document \t→ POST /documents</p><p>2. Checkout for editing \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkout</p><p>3. Create new version with edits → POST /documents/:id/versions</p><p>4. Checkin \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkin</p><p>5. Submit for review \t→ POST /documents/:id/submit</p><p>6. Approve (by QA) \t→ POST /documents/:id/approve</p><p>7. Make effective (by admin) \t→ POST /documents/:id/make-effective</p><p>8. (Later) Obsolete when superseded → POST /documents/:id/obsolete</p><p>10. Complete Workflow Example</p><p>A complete, annotated request/response sequence for creating and publishing a document via Combined Auth</p><p>(Mode B).</p><p>Step 1 — Get Categories</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/categories</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>→ Note the id for the SOP category (e.g., 6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5)</p><p>Step 2 — Create Document</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Equipment Calibration SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"description": "Procedure for equipment calibration in production areas",</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Calibration Steps",</p><p>"department": "Engineering",</p><p>"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",</p><p>"tags": ["calibration", "equipment", "gmp"]</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: draft, Version: 0.1, document_number: SOP-2026-0002</p><p>→ Save the data.id as document_id</p><p>Step 3 — Checkout for Editing</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Adding section 4 - Frequency of Calibration"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Response: { "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "..." }</p><p>Step 4 — Create a New Version (Minor Edit)</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 19 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. Frequency\\n4.1 Monthly for critical</p><p>equipment",</p><p>"change_summary": "Added frequency section",</p><p>"change_reason": "minor_edit"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Version bumped to 0.2, document status reset to draft</p><p>Step 5 — Checkin</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>→ Response: { "checked_in": true }</p><p>Step 6 — Submit for Review</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>→ Status: in_review, workflow_instance_id is now populated</p><p>Step 7 — Approve</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"comments": "Reviewed and approved - meets regulatory standards"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: approved</p><p>Step 8 — Make Effective</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"effective_date": "2026-03-17T00:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: effective</p><p>→ next_review_date auto-calculated: 2027-03-17 (SOP category = 12 months)</p><p>Step 9 — (Future) Obsolete When Superseded</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 20 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>"reason": "Superseded by Equipment Calibration SOP v2.0 (SOP-2026-0015)"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: obsolete, obsolete_date = NOW()</p><p>Quick Reference Card</p><p>API Meth</p><p>od Endpoint \tPermission \tRequired Body Fields</p><p>Get Categories \tGET \t/documents/categories \tdocument:read \t—</p><p>Get Types \tGET \t/documents/types \tAuth only \t—</p><p>Get Statuses \tGET \t/documents/statuses \tAuth only \t—</p><p>Due for Review \tGET /documents/due-for-revi</p><p>ew document:read \t—</p><p>List Documents \tGET \t/documents \tdocument:read \t—</p><p>Get Document \tGET \t/documents/:id \tdocument:read \t—</p><p>Create Document POST /documents \tdocument:write title, document_type</p><p>Update Document PUT \t/documents/:id \tdocument:write at least one field</p><p>Get Versions \tGET \t/documents/:id/versions document:read \t—</p><p>Create Version \tPOST /documents/:id/versions document:write —</p><p>Checkout \tPOST /documents/:id/checkout document:write —</p><p>Checkin \tPOST /documents/:id/checkin document:write —</p><p>Submit for Review POST /documents/:id/submit \tdocument:write {}</p><p>Approve \tPOST /documents/:id/approve document:write —</p><p>Reject \tPOST /documents/:id/reject \tdocument:write reason (mandatory)</p><p>Make Effective \tPOST /documents/:id/make-eff</p><p>ective document:write effective_date (mandatory)</p><p>Obsolete \tPOST /documents/:id/obsolete document:write reason (mandatory)</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 21 of 21 --</p>	\N	minor_edit	\N	\N	\N	\N	4ccf68ad-485c-495a-935b-10d74b173a52	2026-03-26 06:20:26.620637+00	platform	\N
d97c9aa7-9f89-414e-afbe-ab45375defe4	f4631330-c990-4e05-9bf4-396ee9480b1d	352d7e21-5155-4ff8-8169-284bf5ece3e7	0.2	0	2	in_review	FileAttachmentService-Forma.docx	352d7e21-5155-4ff8-8169-284bf5ece3e7/documents/2026/03/718f4ef5-b3b4-44f7-bdef-b28d1a860a78_fileattachmentservice-forma.docx	1158013	application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document	f4a4481561f0a39683f5e8a14ae1d2571d29ea43e4acbaa866d887ad6478de14	SERVICE SPECIFICATION\n\nFile Attachment Services\n\n\n\nQAssure Multi-Tenant SaaS Platform\n\nVersion 1.0   ·   February 2026\n\n\n\n1. Feature of Service\n\nSERVICE NAME: FILE ATTACHMENT SERVICES\n\nCentralised, tenant-isolated, binary file lifecycle engine that governs how files (documents, images, reports, specifications, audit evidence, training materials) are uploaded, stored, versioned, downloaded, previewed, shared, and deleted across multi-tenant regulated environments. All binary file operations across the QAssure platform and module applications are routed through this single service.\n\n\n\nCore capabilities:\n\n\n\n1. File Upload & Storage --- Single and multi-file upload (up to 10 files per request) with multer memory storage, 100MB max file size enforcement, blocked dangerous extensions (.exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .ps1, .msi, .dll, .com, .scr, .vbs, .js), SHA-256 checksum calculation via crypto.createHash('sha256'), and automatic tenant-scoped folder hierarchy: {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext. Files are linked to any platform entity via entity_type + entity_id (e.g., entity_type='documents', entity_id=document_uuid). Source module is auto-derived from authentication context: module code for combined JWT + API Key mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf') where module identity is captured from the API key even though user identity comes from JWT; 'platform' for JWT-only users; moduleCode for API key-only modules (e.g., 'aice', 'dhf'); or 'api_key' as fallback if an API key has no linked module. Priority order: req.module.code (combined mode) → req.user.moduleCode (API key mode) → 'platform' (JWT mode). Duplicate detection prevents re-upload of identical files to the same entity (enforced by checksum + entity match on active records).\n\n2. File Versioning --- Each file supports immutable version history. Uploading a new version via POST /:id/versions marks the previous version as is_current_version=false and creates a new record with incremented version number, linked via previous_version_id. Version history is retrieved via recursive CTE (Common Table Expression) that traverses the chain in both directions, returning complete lineage. Only the current version is returned in standard queries.\n\n3. Download & Preview --- Download endpoint (GET /:id/download) serves files with Content-Disposition: attachment header for browser download prompt. Preview endpoint (GET /:id/preview) serves with Content-Disposition: inline for in-browser rendering. Both use storageProvider.getFullPath() with path.resolve() for absolute path resolution. File access is logged in file_access_logs table with user_id, IP address, user agent, and action type.\n\n4. File Sharing with Token-Based Access --- Create time-limited, download-limited share links via POST /:id/share. Generates 64-character hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32). Supports configurable parameters: expires_at (absolute timestamp), expires_in_hours (convenience --- auto-converted to expires_at), max_downloads (download cap), share_type ('link' or 'user'), shared_with_user_id, shared_with_email, and permissions ('view' or 'download'). Access via GET /shared/:token is a PUBLIC route (no authentication required). The service validates token existence, checks expiry, enforces max_downloads limit, increments current_downloads counter, and serves the file. Share revocation via DELETE /shares/:shareId deactivates the share.\n\n5. Storage Quota Management --- Per-tenant storage quotas tracked in storage_quotas table: max_storage_bytes (default 10GB), used_storage_bytes, file_count, max_file_size_bytes (default 100MB), allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions. Quota auto-creates on first upload if not present. PostgreSQL trigger (trg_update_storage_usage) automatically increments/decrements used_storage_bytes and file_count on INSERT, DELETE, and UPDATE (soft-delete via SET deleted_at). Quota is checked before every upload: individual file size vs max_file_size_bytes, and total used + new file vs max_storage_bytes. Admin-only PUT /quota endpoint allows updating quota limits (requires files:admin permission).\n\n6. Soft Delete with Hard Delete Option --- Default DELETE /:id performs soft delete (sets deleted_at timestamp). PostgreSQL trigger automatically decrements quota on soft delete. Hard delete via DELETE /:id?hard=true permanently removes the database record AND the physical file from storage via storageProvider.delete(). Orphaned file cleanup: if database INSERT fails after file is saved to disk, the file is automatically cleaned up in the catch block.\n\n7. Storage Provider Abstraction (S3-Ready) --- All file I/O goes through LocalStorageProvider with 4 methods: save(relativePath, buffer), delete(relativePath), exists(relativePath), getFullPath(relativePath). No controller or service code touches the filesystem directly. Migrating to S3 requires implementing an S3StorageProvider with the same interface --- zero code changes in controllers or service logic.\n\n8. Three Authentication Modes --- Every endpoint (except public share access) supports three authentication modes via authenticate middleware: (a) JWT only --- QAssure UI users authenticate via Authorization: Bearer header; tenant derived from JWT claims; user permissions enforced via authorize(); (b) JWT + API Key combined --- module applications acting on behalf of a logged-in user send both Authorization: Bearer (JWT from verify-launch-token) and X-API-Key headers; tenant derived from JWT (X-Tenant-ID not needed); user permissions enforced (not module bypass); source_module set from module identity (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf') for accurate audit attribution; (c) API Key + X-Tenant-ID --- module system/cron operations with no user context send X-API-Key and X-Tenant-ID headers; module gets full access bypass on authorize(). This enables QAssure UI users, module applications acting on behalf of users (with real user identity in audit trails), and module background processes to consume the file attachment service. Routes use authorize() for permission checks: files:read for GET endpoints, files:write for POST/PUT/DELETE endpoints, files:admin for quota management.\n\n9. Multi-Tenant Data Isolation --- All queries are tenant-scoped. Every file, share, quota, and access log belongs to a tenant_id. API Key middleware validates module-tenant assignment via the tenant_module_access table (enabled = true) before granting access. Missing X-Tenant-ID returns error code MISSING_TENANT. Unassigned tenant returns MODULE_NOT_ASSIGNED. In combined mode (JWT + API Key), if the JWT's tenant does not match the API key's assigned tenant, error code TENANT_MISMATCH is returned; if the module is deactivated for the tenant, error code MODULE_NOT_ACTIVE is returned. Users cannot see or access files belonging to other tenants under any circumstance.\n\n10. Security Hardening --- UUID validation middleware on all :id route parameters returns 400 (INVALID_ID_FORMAT) for malformed UUIDs instead of leaking PostgreSQL errors. Error sanitization function (sanitizeErrorResponse) on all 17 controller catch blocks classifies errors into client-safe categories (QUOTA_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, VALIDATION_ERROR, etc.) and returns generic 'An internal error occurred' for unexpected failures --- never exposing constraint names, table structures, or query details. Blocked file extensions prevent executable uploads. Path traversal is impossible because stored names use UUID-based naming, not user-controlled paths.\n\n11. Observability --- Redis caching with graceful degradation (file cache 300s TTL, quota 60s, share 3600s, entity files 120s). Elasticsearch indexing for file searchability. File access logging with IP/user-agent tracking. Storage statistics with per-entity-type and per-module breakdowns. All infrastructure dependencies (Redis, Elasticsearch) fail gracefully --- the service continues operating without caching or indexing if either is unavailable.\n\n\n\n2. Scope\n\nIN SCOPE (Phase 1):\n\nFull file CRUD: upload single file (with auto-generated tenant-scoped storage path, checksum, source_module derivation), upload multiple files (up to 10, parallel via Promise.all), read (single by ID with Redis cache, paginated list with filtering, by entity with pagination), update metadata (description, tags, category, metadata JSONB), soft delete (with quota trigger), hard delete (with physical file removal).\n\nFile versioning: upload new version (marks previous as not current, increments version number, links via previous_version_id), retrieve version history (recursive CTE traversal in both directions).\n\nDownload and preview with correct Content-Disposition headers (attachment for download, inline for preview), file access logging, and path resolution via storageProvider abstraction.\n\nFile sharing: create share link with configurable expiry (expires_at or expires_in_hours), max_downloads cap, share_type (link/user), permissions (view/download). Public access via token (no auth required). Share revocation. Expired/exhausted shares return 404.\n\nStorage quota management: auto-create on first upload, per-tenant limits (max_storage_bytes, max_file_size_bytes, allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions), quota enforcement on every upload, admin-only quota configuration updates (files:admin permission), PostgreSQL trigger for automatic used_storage_bytes/file_count tracking on INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.\n\nThree authentication modes (JWT only, JWT + API Key combined, API Key + X-Tenant-ID) on all 16 authenticated endpoints via authenticate middleware (1 public route excluded: GET /shared/:token). Combined mode derives tenant from JWT (X-Tenant-ID not needed), enforces user permissions, and sets source_module from module identity for accurate audit attribution.\n\nMulti-tenant isolation on all read and write operations.\n\nAPI Key middleware validates module-tenant access via tenant_module_access table.\n\nUUID validation middleware on all :id parameters --- returns 400 for invalid UUIDs.\n\nError sanitization on all 17 catch blocks --- never leaks database internals.\n\nFile access audit trail via file_access_logs with user_id, IP address, user agent, action.\n\nStorage statistics with quota summary, file type counts, by_entity and by_module breakdowns.\n\nPagination via limit and offset query parameters (default limit 50). Response is a JSON array of file objects.\n\nFilter support on list: source_module, mime_type, entity_type, category, search (ILIKE on original_name), sort (created_at, file_size, original_name), date range (created_after, created_before).\n\nOrphaned file cleanup: if DB INSERT fails after file save, file is automatically removed from storage.\n\nRedis caching with graceful degradation (operates without Redis).\n\nElasticsearch indexing with graceful degradation (operates without ES).\n\n\n\nOUT OF SCOPE (Phase 1 --- File Attachment Service boundary):\n\nS3/MinIO object storage migration --- LocalStorageProvider is production-ready; S3StorageProvider is a config swap planned for Phase 2. Storage provider abstraction is already in place.\n\nVirus/malware scanning --- scan_status and scanned_at columns exist in file_attachments table but no scanning service is integrated.\n\nImage thumbnail generation --- has_thumbnail, thumbnail_path columns exist but no thumbnail generation pipeline is implemented.\n\nFull-text content extraction from uploaded files (PDF text extraction, OCR).\n\nVector embedding of file content for semantic search via Qdrant.\n\nReal-time file upload progress (WebSocket-based progress tracking).\n\nClient-side chunked upload for files larger than 100MB.\n\nCDN integration for cached file delivery.\n\nFile format conversion (PDF to image, document to PDF, etc.).\n\nWatermarking or digital stamping of downloaded files.\n\nBulk import/export of files.\n\nFile-level access control lists (ACLs) --- access is controlled at entity level via entity_type permissions, not per-file.\n\nRetention policy enforcement --- soft-deleted files remain in database indefinitely until hard-deleted.\n\nEmail/SMS notifications on file events (handled by Notification Service separately).\n\nDocument lifecycle management (SOPs, versioning, review/approval) --- handled by separate Document Service (document.service.js).\n\n\n\n3. Clear Responsibility Split\n\n3.1 SaaS Platform (Owned by Platform Team):\n\nProvide and maintain the File Attachment Service as a centralised, tenant-isolated binary file management engine.\n\nEnforce file upload constraints: 100MB max file size (multer + quota), blocked dangerous extensions, per-tenant storage quotas with auto-creation and trigger-based tracking.\n\nGenerate and manage tenant-scoped storage paths: {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext.\n\nCalculate SHA-256 checksums on every upload for integrity verification.\n\nAuto-derive source_module from authentication context with priority: req.module.code for combined JWT + API Key mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf'), req.user.moduleCode for API key-only modules, 'platform' for JWT-only users, 'api_key' fallback for API keys without linked modules. This ensures files uploaded by modules on behalf of users are correctly attributed to the originating module in storage statistics.\n\nManage file versioning: version number increment, previous_version_id linking, is_current_version flagging, recursive CTE version history retrieval.\n\nMaintain storage provider abstraction (LocalStorageProvider) with save, delete, exists, getFullPath methods for future S3 migration.\n\nEnforce tenant isolation on all queries via tenant_id filtering. No cross-tenant file access is possible.\n\nProvide three authentication modes on all 16 authenticated endpoints via authenticate middleware (1 public route excluded: GET /shared/:token): (a) JWT only for QAssure UI users, (b) JWT + API Key combined for module applications acting on behalf of logged-in users (tenant from JWT, user permissions enforced, source_module from module identity), (c) API Key + X-Tenant-ID for module system/cron operations.\n\nValidate module-tenant access via tenant_module_access table (enabled = true check). Return MISSING_TENANT or MODULE_NOT_ASSIGNED errors for invalid API Key requests. In combined mode, return TENANT_MISMATCH if JWT tenant differs from API key's assigned tenant, and MODULE_NOT_ACTIVE if the module is deactivated for the tenant.\n\nProvide UUID validation middleware for all route parameters. Return 400 INVALID_ID_FORMAT for malformed UUIDs.\n\nSanitise all error responses to prevent database internal leakage.\n\nProvide file sharing infrastructure: token generation, expiry enforcement, max_downloads enforcement, public access route.\n\nProvide storage statistics with per-entity-type and per-module breakdowns.\n\nLog all file access events (download, preview, checkout, checkin) in file_access_logs.\n\nProvide Redis caching and Elasticsearch indexing with graceful degradation.\n\nExpose admin-only quota management endpoint (files:admin permission).\n\n\n\n3.2 Module Applications (Residing on Platform; Owned by App Teams --- LTTS):\n\nUse the File Attachment Service API with the appropriate authentication mode:\n\nFor user-context operations (user uploads a file via module UI): Send both Authorization: Bearer (JWT obtained from verify-launch-token) and X-API-Key headers. X-Tenant-ID is NOT needed --- tenant is derived from JWT. User permissions (files:read, files:write) are enforced. uploaded_by and file_access_logs.user_id record the real user identity. source_module records the module identity (e.g., 'coc').\n\nFor system/cron operations (no user context): Send X-API-Key + X-Tenant-ID headers. Module gets full access bypass. source_module records the module identity from API key.\n\nSpecify entity_type and entity_id when uploading files to link them to the correct module entity (e.g., entity_type='documents', entity_id=<document_uuid> for Document Service; entity_type='capa', entity_id=<capa_uuid> for CAPA module).\n\nProvide required fields on upload: file (multipart), entity_type (string), entity_id (UUID). Optional fields: description, category, tags, metadata (JSONB).\n\nUse the version upload endpoint (POST /:id/versions) for updating files rather than deleting and re-uploading. This preserves version history and audit trail.\n\nUse the share endpoint to generate time-limited, download-limited links for external stakeholders (e.g., auditors, suppliers) without granting platform login access.\n\nDo NOT implement custom file storage logic --- always delegate to platform's file attachment service.\n\nDo NOT store file metadata in the module's own database --- use platform as the system of record for all file attachments. Use the entity link (entity_type + entity_id) to associate files with module records.\n\nDo NOT construct file paths manually or access the uploads directory directly --- always use service API endpoints for file access.\n\nUse SSO launch token flow to obtain both tenant context and user session JWT dynamically in production: call POST /modules/verify-launch-token with X-API-Key and the launch token to receive a JWT (24h expiry), user details (including department, designation, user category), tenant details, and permissions. Use this JWT in Authorization: Bearer header alongside X-API-Key for all user-context platform calls. Use .env TENANT_ID + X-Tenant-ID header for development and system/cron operations only.\n\n\n\n4. API List (Refer to Excel Sheet shared)\n\n\n\n#\n\nMethod\n\nEndpoint\n\nAuth\n\nDescription\n\n1\n\nPOST\n\n/api/v1/files/upload\n\nauthenticate + files:write\n\nUpload single file (multipart)\n\n2\n\nPOST\n\n/api/v1/files/upload/multiple\n\nauthenticate + files:write\n\nUpload multiple files (up to 10)\n\n3\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files\n\nauthenticate + files:read\n\nList files (paginated, filterable)\n\n4\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/:id\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nGet single file by ID\n\n5\n\nPUT\n\n/api/v1/files/:id\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nUpdate file metadata\n\n6\n\nDELETE\n\n/api/v1/files/:id\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nDelete file (soft; ?hard=true for permanent)\n\n7\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/download\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nDownload file (Content-Disposition: attachment)\n\n8\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/preview\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nPreview file (Content-Disposition: inline)\n\n9\n\nPOST\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/versions\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nUpload new version of existing file\n\n10\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/versions\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nGet version history (recursive CTE)\n\n11\n\nPOST\n\n/api/v1/files/:id/share\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nCreate share link (token, expiry, max_downloads)\n\n12\n\nDELETE\n\n/api/v1/files/shares/:shareId\n\nauthenticate + files:write + validateUUID\n\nRevoke share link\n\n13\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/shared/:token\n\nPUBLIC (no auth)\n\nAccess shared file via token\n\n14\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/entity/:entity_type/:entity_id\n\nauthenticate + files:read + validateUUID\n\nGet files by entity (paginated)\n\n15\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/stats\n\nauthenticate + files:read\n\nGet storage statistics (by entity, by module)\n\n16\n\nGET\n\n/api/v1/files/quota\n\nauthenticate + files:read\n\nGet tenant storage quota\n\n17\n\nPUT\n\n/api/v1/files/quota\n\nauthenticate + files:admin\n\nUpdate tenant storage quota (admin only)\n\n\n\nRoute ordering note: /stats, /quota, /entity/:type/:id, /shared/:token are registered BEFORE /:id to prevent Express matching static segments as UUID parameters.\n\n\n\n5. Typical Workflow\n\n5.1 Write Path (File Upload & Management):\n\n1. Upload Single File: Tenant user or module calls POST /api/v1/files/upload with multipart form data: file (required, binary), entity_type (required, e.g., 'documents'), entity_id (required, UUID of parent entity), and optional: description, category, tags (comma-separated string or JSON array), metadata (JSONB). The API validates: file presence (returns VALIDATION_ERROR 'No file uploaded'), entity_type and entity_id presence (returns VALIDATION_ERROR 'entity_type and entity_id are required'), file extension not in blocked list (.exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .ps1, .msi, .dll, .com, .scr, .vbs, .js --- returns error 'File type .exe is not allowed'), file size under 100MB (returns FILE_TOO_LARGE 'File size exceeds 100MB limit'), tenant quota not exceeded (returns QUOTA_ERROR for both individual file and total storage).\n\nPlatform generates: stored_name as {uuid}_{sanitized_original_name}.ext, storage path as {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{stored_name}, SHA-256 checksum via crypto.createHash('sha256').update(buffer).digest('hex'), source_module derived from auth context with priority: req.module.code for combined mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf'), 'platform' for JWT-only users, req.user.moduleCode for API key-only modules (e.g., 'aice', 'dhf'), or 'api_key' fallback if API key has no linked module. File is saved to storage via storageProvider.save(relativePath, buffer), then database record is inserted into file_attachments. If DB INSERT fails, file is automatically cleaned up from storage (orphan prevention). Redis cache is invalidated for entity files list. Elasticsearch index is updated via IndexingHooks. Returns full file object with 201 status.\n\n2. Upload Multiple Files: POST /api/v1/files/upload/multiple accepts up to 10 files via multer array ('files' field, max 10). All files are uploaded in parallel via Promise.all, sharing the same entity_type and entity_id. Returns array of results with per-file success/error status. Quota is checked per file individually.\n\n3. Update Metadata: PUT /api/v1/files/:id updates allowed fields: description (text), category (varchar), tags (cast as text[]), metadata (cast as JSONB). File content changes go through versioning (POST /:id/versions), not metadata update. Sets updated_at timestamp. Returns 'No valid fields to update' error if no recognized fields provided. Returns full file object with 200 status.\n\n4. Soft Delete: DELETE /api/v1/files/:id sets deleted_at = NOW() timestamp. PostgreSQL trigger (trg_update_storage_usage) automatically decrements used_storage_bytes and file_count in storage_quotas using GREATEST(..., 0) to prevent negative values. File remains on disk for potential recovery. Redis cache invalidated. Elasticsearch index updated. Returns { success: true, message: 'File deleted' }.\n\n5. Hard Delete: DELETE /api/v1/files/:id?hard=true permanently removes: database record (DELETE FROM file_attachments WHERE id = $1 AND tenant_id = $2), physical file from storage via storageProvider.delete(file_path), thumbnail if exists via storageProvider.delete(thumbnail_path). Returns 404 on subsequent GET. Irreversible. Quota adjusts via DELETE trigger.\n\n\n\n5.2 Versioning:\n\nMinor Versioning: Default behavior. Every POST /api/v1/files/:id/versions with new file (multipart) performs: fetches current record by ID and tenant_id, marks it as is_current_version=false via UPDATE, inserts new record with version = previous_version + 1, is_current_version=true, previous_version_id = old record ID. SHA-256 checksum is calculated for the new file. Both old and new records remain in database --- version history is immutable and never deleted.\n\nVersion History Retrieval: GET /api/v1/files/:id/versions uses a recursive CTE (Common Table Expression) that traverses the previous_version_id chain in both directions (forward via self-join on previous_version_id, backward via matching previous_version_id = id). Returns complete version lineage with: id, version, file_size, checksum, original_name, uploaded_by_email (resolved via LEFT JOIN users), created_at for each version. Ordered by version number ascending.\n\nVersion Chain Structure: file_attachments.previous_version_id creates a self-referencing linked list. Version 1 has previous_version_id=null. Version 2 points to Version 1. Version 3 points to Version 2. Only the latest version has is_current_version=true. Standard queries (list, get by entity) only return current versions (WHERE is_current_version = true AND deleted_at IS NULL).\n\n\n\n5.3 Read/Search Path:\n\nGet by ID: GET /api/v1/files/:id --- Redis cached (300s TTL). Returns full file object with uploaded_by_email resolved via LEFT JOIN users. Filters by tenant_id for isolation.\n\nList Files: GET /api/v1/files?limit=50&offset=0 --- returns a JSON array of file objects. Supports limit and offset query parameters for pagination. Supports filters: source_module, mime_type, entity_type, category, search (ILIKE on original_name), sort_by (created_at|file_size|original_name), sort_order (ASC|DESC), created_after, created_before. Only returns active files (deleted_at IS NULL, is_current_version = true).\n\nGet by Entity: GET /api/v1/files/entity/:entity_type/:entity_id --- returns a JSON array of all files linked to a specific entity. Used by Document Service, CAPA module, Training module, etc. to retrieve their linked files.\n\nStorage Stats: GET /api/v1/files/stats --- returns four sections: quota (max_storage, used_storage, available, usage_percent), files (total, images, pdfs, documents counts), by_entity (count + size per entity_type), and by_module (count + size per source_module e.g., 'platform', 'coc').\n\nStorage Quota: GET /api/v1/files/quota --- returns current quota status: max_storage_bytes, used_storage_bytes, file_count, max_file_size_bytes, allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions, usage_percentage.\n\n\n\n5.4 File Sharing Path:\n\nCreate Share: POST /api/v1/files/:id/share with body: share_type ('link'|'user'), permissions ('view'|'download'), expires_at (ISO timestamp) or expires_in_hours (number, auto-converted), max_downloads (integer), shared_with_user_id, shared_with_email. Service generates 64-char hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32). Returns share object with share_token, share_url, expires_at, max_downloads. Redis cached (3600s TTL).\n\nAccess Shared File: GET /api/v1/files/shared/:token --- PUBLIC route (no authentication). Service: looks up share by token (Redis cached), validates expiry (expires_at > NOW()), validates download count (current_downloads < max_downloads), increments current_downloads, resolves file path via storageProvider.getFullPath(), serves file with correct Content-Type and Content-Disposition headers. Returns 404 if share not found, expired, or download limit reached.\n\nRevoke Share: DELETE /api/v1/files/shares/:shareId --- sets is_active=false. Invalidates Redis cache for the share token.\n\n\n\n5.5 Retention/Deletion:\n\nPhase 1: No automated retention policy enforcement. Soft-deleted files remain in database with deleted_at timestamp set. Hard delete permanently removes file and database record.\n\nQuota Recovery: Soft delete triggers automatic quota decrement via PostgreSQL trigger. Restoring a soft-deleted file (clearing deleted_at) would trigger quota increment.\n\nPlanned Phase 2: Configurable retention periods per entity_type. Scheduled cleanup job to hard-delete files past retention period. Archived storage tier for long-term retention at reduced cost.\n\n\n\n5.6 Audit Trail:\n\nfile_access_logs records (inserted on download, preview, and any file access): file_id, tenant_id, user_id, action ('download'|'preview'|'access'), ip_address (from req.ip), user_agent (from req.headers), created_at.\n\nStorage quota changes tracked via PostgreSQL trigger --- every INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on file_attachments automatically adjusts used_storage_bytes and file_count.\n\nShare access tracked via current_downloads counter and last_accessed_at timestamp on file_shares.\n\nAuthentication mode impacts audit attribution: In combined JWT + API Key mode, uploaded_by and file_access_logs.user_id record the real user identity (from JWT), while source_module records the originating module (from API key). This provides GxP-compliant traceability --- auditors can see both who performed the action and which module facilitated it. In API Key-only mode, uploaded_by records the module service account and source_module records the module code. In JWT-only mode, uploaded_by records the platform user and source_module is set to 'platform'.\n\n\n\n6. PostgreSQL DB --- MODEL\n\nThe File Attachment Service uses 4 PostgreSQL tables: file_attachments (master record with binary file metadata, entity linking, versioning, and storage path), storage_quotas (per-tenant storage limits with trigger-maintained usage counters), file_shares (token-based file sharing with expiry and download limits), and file_access_logs (audit trail for file access events). All tables enforce multi-tenant isolation via tenant_id foreign key with ON DELETE CASCADE. The file_attachments table serves as the central entity. A PostgreSQL trigger function (update_storage_usage) automatically maintains used_storage_bytes and file_count in storage_quotas on INSERT, UPDATE (soft-delete/restore), and DELETE operations.\n\n6.1 ER Diagram:\n\n\n\nFigure 6.1: Entity Relationship Diagram --- File Attachment Service\n\nfile_attachments.tenant_id → tenants.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n\nfile_attachments.uploaded_by → users.id\n\nfile_attachments.previous_version_id → file_attachments.id (self-referencing version chain)\n\nstorage_quotas.tenant_id → tenants.id (UNIQUE --- one quota per tenant)\n\nfile_shares.tenant_id → tenants.id, file_shares.file_id → file_attachments.id\n\nfile_access_logs.file_id → file_attachments.id, file_access_logs.user_id → users.id\n\n6.2 Entities & Attributes:\n\n6.2.1 Entity: file_attachments (32 columns)\n\n\n\nAttribute\n\nData Type\n\nConstraint / FK\n\nDescription\n\nExample\n\nid\n\nUUID\n\nPK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\nUnique file identifier\n\ndaf3c8ad-...\n\ntenant_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, INDEX\n\nTenant isolation\n\nc0000000-...\n\noriginal_name\n\nVARCHAR(500)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nUser-uploaded filename\n\ntest-upload.txt\n\nstored_name\n\nVARCHAR(500)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nUUID-based stored name\n\ndaf3c8ad_test-upload.txt\n\nfile_path\n\nVARCHAR(1000)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nRelative storage path\n\nc000.../documents/2026/02/daf3...txt\n\nmime_type\n\nVARCHAR(255)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nMIME type\n\ntext/plain\n\nfile_size\n\nBIGINT\n\nNOT NULL\n\nFile size in bytes\n\n18\n\nchecksum\n\nVARCHAR(128)\n\nNullable\n\nSHA-256 hash\n\na591a6d40...\n\nstorage_provider\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nDEFAULT 'local'\n\nStorage backend\n\nlocal\n\nstorage_bucket\n\nVARCHAR(255)\n\nNullable\n\nS3 bucket (Phase 2)\n\nnull\n\nstorage_region\n\nVARCHAR(100)\n\nNullable\n\nS3 region (Phase 2)\n\nnull\n\nentity_type\n\nVARCHAR(100)\n\nNOT NULL, INDEX\n\nParent entity type\n\ndocuments\n\nentity_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, INDEX\n\nParent entity ID\n\nUUID\n\ncategory\n\nVARCHAR(100)\n\nNullable\n\nFile category\n\nspecification\n\ndescription\n\nTEXT\n\nNullable\n\nFile description\n\nTest file upload\n\ntags\n\nTEXT[]\n\nNullable\n\nPostgreSQL text array\n\n{sop,quality}\n\nversion\n\nINTEGER\n\nDEFAULT 1\n\nVersion number\n\n1\n\nis_current_version\n\nBOOLEAN\n\nDEFAULT true, INDEX (partial)\n\nActive version flag\n\ntrue\n\nprevious_version_id\n\nUUID\n\nFK → file_attachments(id), Nullable\n\nVersion chain link\n\nUUID or null\n\nis_public\n\nBOOLEAN\n\nDEFAULT false\n\nPublic access flag\n\nfalse\n\naccess_level\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nDEFAULT 'private'\n\nAccess level\n\nprivate\n\ndownload_count\n\nINTEGER\n\nDEFAULT 0\n\nTotal downloads\n\n5\n\nhas_thumbnail\n\nBOOLEAN\n\nDEFAULT false\n\nThumbnail exists\n\nfalse\n\nthumbnail_path\n\nVARCHAR(1000)\n\nNullable\n\nThumbnail storage path\n\nnull\n\nmetadata\n\nJSONB\n\nDEFAULT '{}'\n\nExtensible metadata\n\n{}\n\nscan_status\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nNullable\n\nVirus scan status (Phase 2)\n\nnull\n\nscanned_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nNullable\n\nScan timestamp (Phase 2)\n\nnull\n\nuploaded_by\n\nUUID\n\nFK → users(id), Nullable\n\nUploader user ID\n\nUUID\n\nsource_module\n\nVARCHAR(100)\n\nDEFAULT 'platform', INDEX\n\nOrigin module\n\nplatform\n\ncreated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nCreated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\nupdated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nUpdated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\ndeleted_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nNullable, INDEX\n\nSoft delete timestamp\n\nnull\n\n\n\nNOTES: tags is TEXT[] not JSONB. file_size is BIGINT (returns as string from node-pg, parsed to integer in _formatAttachment). is_current_version partial index filters WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND is_current_version = TRUE. previous_version_id creates a self-referencing linked list for version chains. source_module is auto-derived from auth context, never user-supplied.\n\n\n\n6.2.2 Entity: storage_quotas (10 columns)\n\n\n\nAttribute\n\nData Type\n\nConstraint / FK\n\nDescription\n\nExample\n\nid\n\nUUID\n\nPK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\nQuota record ID\n\nUUID\n\ntenant_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → tenants(id), UNIQUE\n\nTenant isolation\n\nc0000000-...\n\nmax_storage_bytes\n\nBIGINT\n\nDEFAULT 10737418240 (10GB)\n\nMax total storage\n\n10737418240\n\nused_storage_bytes\n\nBIGINT\n\nDEFAULT 0\n\nCurrent usage (trigger-maintained)\n\n1536\n\nfile_count\n\nINTEGER\n\nDEFAULT 0\n\nActive file count (trigger-maintained)\n\n15\n\nmax_file_size_bytes\n\nBIGINT\n\nDEFAULT 104857600 (100MB)\n\nMax single file size\n\n104857600\n\nallowed_mime_types\n\nTEXT[]\n\nNullable\n\nWhitelist (null = all allowed)\n\nnull\n\nblocked_extensions\n\nTEXT[]\n\nNullable\n\nBlacklist\n\n{.exe,.bat}\n\ncreated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nCreated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\nupdated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nUpdated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\n\n\nNOTES: max_storage_bytes and used_storage_bytes are BIGINT. PostgreSQL trigger update_storage_usage() maintains used_storage_bytes and file_count automatically on file_attachments INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE. The trigger uses GREATEST(..., 0) to prevent negative values. Quota auto-creates via service when first upload occurs for a tenant.\n\n\n\nPostgreSQL Trigger Function:\n\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_storage_usage() --- Handles INSERT (increment), DELETE (decrement), UPDATE with NEW.deleted_at IS NOT NULL AND OLD.deleted_at IS NULL (soft-delete decrement), UPDATE with NEW.deleted_at IS NULL AND OLD.deleted_at IS NOT NULL (restore increment). Uses GREATEST(used_storage_bytes - file_size, 0) and GREATEST(file_count - 1, 0) to prevent negative values.\n\n6.2.3 Entity: file_shares (15 columns)\n\n\n\nAttribute\n\nData Type\n\nConstraint / FK\n\nDescription\n\nExample\n\nid\n\nUUID\n\nPK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\nShare record ID\n\nUUID\n\ntenant_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n\nTenant isolation\n\nc0000000-...\n\nfile_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → file_attachments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n\nShared file\n\nUUID\n\nshare_token\n\nVARCHAR(255)\n\nNOT NULL, UNIQUE\n\n64-char hex token\n\na3f8c2d1...\n\nshare_type\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nDEFAULT 'link'\n\nShare type\n\nlink\n\nshared_with_user_id\n\nUUID\n\nFK → users(id), Nullable\n\nTarget user (for 'user' type)\n\nnull\n\nshared_with_email\n\nVARCHAR(255)\n\nNullable\n\nTarget email\n\nnull\n\npermissions\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nDEFAULT 'view'\n\nAccess level\n\nview/download\n\nexpires_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nNullable\n\nExpiry timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\nmax_downloads\n\nINTEGER\n\nNullable\n\nDownload cap (null = unlimited)\n\n5\n\ncurrent_downloads\n\nINTEGER\n\nDEFAULT 0\n\nDownloads consumed\n\n2\n\nis_active\n\nBOOLEAN\n\nDEFAULT true\n\nActive flag (false = revoked)\n\ntrue\n\nlast_accessed_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nNullable\n\nLast access time\n\nISO datetime\n\ncreated_by\n\nUUID\n\nFK → users(id), Nullable\n\nShare creator\n\nUUID\n\ncreated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nCreated timestamp\n\nISO datetime\n\n\n\nNOTES: share_token is UNIQUE. expires_at can be set directly or auto-calculated from expires_in_hours (service converts: new Date(Date.now() + hours * 3600000).toISOString()). max_downloads null means unlimited. current_downloads is incremented atomically on each access. is_active=false means share has been revoked.\n\n\n\n6.2.4 Entity: file_access_logs (8 columns)\n\n\n\nAttribute\n\nData Type\n\nConstraint / FK\n\nDescription\n\nExample\n\nid\n\nUUID\n\nPK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\nLog record ID\n\nUUID\n\ntenant_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n\nTenant isolation\n\nUUID\n\nfile_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → file_attachments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n\nFile accessed\n\nUUID\n\nuser_id\n\nUUID\n\nNOT NULL, FK → users(id)\n\nWho accessed\n\nUUID\n\naction\n\nVARCHAR(50)\n\nNOT NULL\n\nAction type\n\ndownload/preview/access\n\nip_address\n\nINET\n\nNullable\n\nClient IP\n\n192.168.1.1\n\nuser_agent\n\nTEXT\n\nNullable\n\nBrowser UA string\n\nMozilla/5.0...\n\ncreated_at\n\nTIMESTAMPTZ\n\nDEFAULT NOW()\n\nWhen accessed\n\nISO datetime\n\n\n\nNOTES: Records are insert-only (append-only audit log). ip_address and user_agent are captured from Express request object when available. action values include 'download', 'preview', 'access' for share access.\n\n\n\n7. Qdrant (Vector DB)\n\nPhase 1 Status: NOT USED by File Attachment Service.\n\nBinary file content is stored on the filesystem via LocalStorageProvider. File metadata is stored in PostgreSQL (file_attachments table). No vector embeddings of file content are generated in Phase 1.\n\n\n\nPlanned for Phase 2:\n\nCollection Name: file_content_vec_v1\n\nVector Dimension: 1536 (OpenAI text-embedding-3-small) or 768 (sentence-transformers)\n\nPayload Fields: file_id (string), tenant_id (string --- mandatory filter), original_name (string), entity_type (string), entity_id (string), mime_type (string), category (string), source_module (string), created_at (ISO string)\n\nPayload Indexes: tenant_id, entity_type, mime_type, source_module, created_at\n\nUse Case: Semantic search across extracted file content (PDF text, document text), similar file discovery, AI-powered content recommendations, duplicate detection via vector similarity rather than checksum matching.\n\nPrerequisite: Content extraction pipeline (PDF text extraction, OCR for images, document parsing) must be implemented first to generate text from binary files before vector embedding.\n\n\n\n8. Object Storage\n\nFolder Structure Hierarchy:\n\nRoot: UPLOAD_DIR (default: ./uploads/, configurable via environment variable)\n\nPattern: {UPLOAD_DIR}/{tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext\n\n\n\nExample hierarchy:\n\nuploads/\n\n  c0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/   (Tenant: Pharma Corp)\n\n    documents/   (Entity type)\n\n      2026/   (Year)\n\n        02/   (Month)\n\n          daf3c8ad-3660-4c13-8b57-0daf3cc9aaf0_test-upload.txt\n\n          d7cbcb77-a8f1-4e22-b901-3dc77f8e22a1_report-v2.pdf\n\n    capa/\n\n      2026/\n\n        02/\n\n          f1a2b3c4-..._corrective-action-photo.jpg\n\n    training/\n\n      2026/\n\n        01/\n\n          a9b8c7d6-..._sop-training-material.pdf\n\n  d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002/   (Tenant: Another Org)\n\n    documents/\n\n    suppliers/\n\n    temp/   (Temporary storage)\n\n    thumbnails/   (Thumbnail storage)\n\n\n\nStorage Provider Abstraction:\n\nLocalStorageProvider (Phase 1 --- current):\n\nsave(relativePath, buffer) --- Creates directory tree via fs.mkdirSync({recursive: true}), writes buffer via fs.writeFileSync.\n\ndelete(relativePath) --- Removes file via fs.unlinkSync. Silently ignores if file doesn't exist.\n\nexists(relativePath) --- Checks via fs.existsSync.\n\ngetFullPath(relativePath) --- Joins UPLOAD_DIR + relativePath. Controller uses path.resolve() for absolute path.\n\nS3 Migration Path (Phase 2):\n\nImplement S3StorageProvider with identical interface (save, delete, exists, getFullPath). S3 key structure maps 1:1 to local folder hierarchy: s3://{bucket}/{tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{name}.ext. No changes to service or controller code required --- swap provider via configuration.\n\n\n\nSECTION 10 --- REDIS CACHE DETAILS\n\nFile Attachment Service uses 4 Redis cache key patterns with graceful degradation. The service operates normally if Redis is unavailable --- all cache operations are wrapped in try/catch and failures are logged but never block the main operation.\n\n\n\nCache Key Pattern\n\nPurpose\n\nTTL\n\nInvalidation\n\nfile:{tenant_id}:{file_id}\n\nSingle file metadata cache\n\n300s (5 min)\n\nOn update, delete\n\nquota:{tenant_id}\n\nTenant storage quota\n\n60s (1 min)\n\nOn upload, delete, quota update\n\nshare:{share_token}\n\nShare token lookup\n\n3600s (1 hr)\n\nOn revoke\n\nentity_files:{entity_type}:{entity_id}\n\nFiles by entity list\n\n120s (2 min)\n\nOn upload, delete to entity\n\n\n\nRedis Service Integration:\n\nFile: src/infrastructure/cache/redis.service.js --- singleton instance exported as module.exports = new RedisService().\n\nMethods used: get(key, parseJson=true), set(key, value, ttlSeconds), delete(key). Note: The Redis service uses delete() method, NOT del().\n\nCache invalidation method: _invalidateCache(tenantId, fileId, entityType, entityId) --- deletes all relevant cache keys after any write operation (upload, update, delete, share revoke).\n\nLazy initialization: getRedis() function returns singleton Redis instance on first call, returns null if Redis is unavailable. Every cache operation checks for null before proceeding.\n\n\n\nPlatform-level Redis usage that benefits File Attachment Service indirectly:\n\nSession caching: JWT session data cached by AuthService for fast auth validation on every request.\n\nPermission caching: User permissions cached by PermissionService, used by authorization middleware for files:read/files:write/files:admin checks.\n\n\n\nPlanned Phase 2 enhancements:\n\nFile content cache: Large frequently-accessed files cached in Redis for sub-millisecond retrieval.\n\nShare token bloom filter: Probabilistic check before DB lookup for invalid/revoked tokens.\n\nUpload rate limiting: Per-tenant upload rate tracking via Redis INCR + EXPIRE.	<p>SERVICE SPECIFICATION</p><p><strong>File Attachment Services</strong></p><p>QAssure Multi-Tenant SaaS Platform</p><p>Version 1.0   ·   February 2026</p><h1>1. Feature of Service</h1><h3>SERVICE NAME: FILE ATTACHMENT SERVICES</h3><p>Centralised, tenant-isolated, binary file lifecycle engine that governs how files (documents, images, reports, specifications, audit evidence, training materials) are uploaded, stored, versioned, downloaded, previewed, shared, and deleted across multi-tenant regulated environments. All binary file operations across the QAssure platform and module applications are routed through this single service.</p><p><strong>Core capabilities:</strong></p><p><strong>1. File Upload &amp; Storage</strong> --- Single and multi-file upload (up to 10 files per request) with multer memory storage, 100MB max file size enforcement, blocked dangerous extensions (.exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .ps1, .msi, .dll, .com, .scr, .vbs, .js), SHA-256 checksum calculation via crypto.createHash('sha256'), and automatic tenant-scoped folder hierarchy: {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext. Files are linked to any platform entity via entity_type + entity_id (e.g., entity_type='documents', entity_id=document_uuid). Source module is auto-derived from authentication context: module code for combined JWT + API Key mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf') where module identity is captured from the API key even though user identity comes from JWT; 'platform' for JWT-only users; moduleCode for API key-only modules (e.g., 'aice', 'dhf'); or 'api_key' as fallback if an API key has no linked module. Priority order: req.module.code (combined mode) → req.user.moduleCode (API key mode) → 'platform' (JWT mode). Duplicate detection prevents re-upload of identical files to the same entity (enforced by checksum + entity match on active records).</p><p><strong>2. File Versioning</strong> --- Each file supports immutable version history. Uploading a new version via POST /:id/versions marks the previous version as is_current_version=false and creates a new record with incremented version number, linked via previous_version_id. Version history is retrieved via recursive CTE (Common Table Expression) that traverses the chain in both directions, returning complete lineage. Only the current version is returned in standard queries.</p><p><strong>3. Download &amp; Preview</strong> --- Download endpoint (GET /:id/download) serves files with Content-Disposition: attachment header for browser download prompt. Preview endpoint (GET /:id/preview) serves with Content-Disposition: inline for in-browser rendering. Both use storageProvider.getFullPath() with path.resolve() for absolute path resolution. File access is logged in file_access_logs table with user_id, IP address, user agent, and action type.</p><p><strong>4. File Sharing with Token-Based Access</strong> --- Create time-limited, download-limited share links via POST /:id/share. Generates 64-character hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32). Supports configurable parameters: expires_at (absolute timestamp), expires_in_hours (convenience --- auto-converted to expires_at), max_downloads (download cap), share_type ('link' or 'user'), shared_with_user_id, shared_with_email, and permissions ('view' or 'download'). Access via GET /shared/:token is a PUBLIC route (no authentication required). The service validates token existence, checks expiry, enforces max_downloads limit, increments current_downloads counter, and serves the file. Share revocation via DELETE /shares/:shareId deactivates the share.</p><p><strong>5. Storage Quota Management</strong> --- Per-tenant storage quotas tracked in storage_quotas table: max_storage_bytes (default 10GB), used_storage_bytes, file_count, max_file_size_bytes (default 100MB), allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions. Quota auto-creates on first upload if not present. PostgreSQL trigger (trg_update_storage_usage) automatically increments/decrements used_storage_bytes and file_count on INSERT, DELETE, and UPDATE (soft-delete via SET deleted_at). Quota is checked before every upload: individual file size vs max_file_size_bytes, and total used + new file vs max_storage_bytes. Admin-only PUT /quota endpoint allows updating quota limits (requires files:admin permission).</p><p><strong>6. Soft Delete with Hard Delete Option</strong> --- Default DELETE /:id performs soft delete (sets deleted_at timestamp). PostgreSQL trigger automatically decrements quota on soft delete. Hard delete via DELETE /:id?hard=true permanently removes the database record AND the physical file from storage via storageProvider.delete(). Orphaned file cleanup: if database INSERT fails after file is saved to disk, the file is automatically cleaned up in the catch block.</p><p><strong>7. Storage Provider Abstraction (S3-Ready)</strong> --- All file I/O goes through LocalStorageProvider with 4 methods: save(relativePath, buffer), delete(relativePath), exists(relativePath), getFullPath(relativePath). No controller or service code touches the filesystem directly. Migrating to S3 requires implementing an S3StorageProvider with the same interface --- zero code changes in controllers or service logic.</p><p><strong>8. Three Authentication Modes</strong> --- Every endpoint (except public share access) supports three authentication modes via authenticate middleware: (a) JWT only --- QAssure UI users authenticate via Authorization: Bearer header; tenant derived from JWT claims; user permissions enforced via authorize(); (b) JWT + API Key combined --- module applications acting on behalf of a logged-in user send both Authorization: Bearer (JWT from verify-launch-token) and X-API-Key headers; tenant derived from JWT (X-Tenant-ID not needed); user permissions enforced (not module bypass); source_module set from module identity (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf') for accurate audit attribution; (c) API Key + X-Tenant-ID --- module system/cron operations with no user context send X-API-Key and X-Tenant-ID headers; module gets full access bypass on authorize(). This enables QAssure UI users, module applications acting on behalf of users (with real user identity in audit trails), and module background processes to consume the file attachment service. Routes use authorize() for permission checks: files:read for GET endpoints, files:write for POST/PUT/DELETE endpoints, files:admin for quota management.</p><p><strong>9. Multi-Tenant Data Isolation</strong> --- All queries are tenant-scoped. Every file, share, quota, and access log belongs to a tenant_id. API Key middleware validates module-tenant assignment via the tenant_module_access table (enabled = true) before granting access. Missing X-Tenant-ID returns error code MISSING_TENANT. Unassigned tenant returns MODULE_NOT_ASSIGNED. In combined mode (JWT + API Key), if the JWT's tenant does not match the API key's assigned tenant, error code TENANT_MISMATCH is returned; if the module is deactivated for the tenant, error code MODULE_NOT_ACTIVE is returned. Users cannot see or access files belonging to other tenants under any circumstance.</p><p><strong>10. Security Hardening</strong> --- UUID validation middleware on all :id route parameters returns 400 (INVALID_ID_FORMAT) for malformed UUIDs instead of leaking PostgreSQL errors. Error sanitization function (sanitizeErrorResponse) on all 17 controller catch blocks classifies errors into client-safe categories (QUOTA_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, VALIDATION_ERROR, etc.) and returns generic 'An internal error occurred' for unexpected failures --- never exposing constraint names, table structures, or query details. Blocked file extensions prevent executable uploads. Path traversal is impossible because stored names use UUID-based naming, not user-controlled paths.</p><p><strong>11. Observability</strong> --- Redis caching with graceful degradation (file cache 300s TTL, quota 60s, share 3600s, entity files 120s). Elasticsearch indexing for file searchability. File access logging with IP/user-agent tracking. Storage statistics with per-entity-type and per-module breakdowns. All infrastructure dependencies (Redis, Elasticsearch) fail gracefully --- the service continues operating without caching or indexing if either is unavailable.</p><h1>2. Scope</h1><h2>IN SCOPE (Phase 1):</h2><p><strong>Full file CRUD:</strong> upload single file (with auto-generated tenant-scoped storage path, checksum, source_module derivation), upload multiple files (up to 10, parallel via Promise.all), read (single by ID with Redis cache, paginated list with filtering, by entity with pagination), update metadata (description, tags, category, metadata JSONB), soft delete (with quota trigger), hard delete (with physical file removal).</p><p><strong>File versioning:</strong> upload new version (marks previous as not current, increments version number, links via previous_version_id), retrieve version history (recursive CTE traversal in both directions).</p><p><strong>Download and preview</strong> with correct Content-Disposition headers (attachment for download, inline for preview), file access logging, and path resolution via storageProvider abstraction.</p><p><strong>File sharing:</strong> create share link with configurable expiry (expires_at or expires_in_hours), max_downloads cap, share_type (link/user), permissions (view/download). Public access via token (no auth required). Share revocation. Expired/exhausted shares return 404.</p><p><strong>Storage quota management:</strong> auto-create on first upload, per-tenant limits (max_storage_bytes, max_file_size_bytes, allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions), quota enforcement on every upload, admin-only quota configuration updates (files:admin permission), PostgreSQL trigger for automatic used_storage_bytes/file_count tracking on INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.</p><p><strong>Three authentication modes</strong> (JWT only, JWT + API Key combined, API Key + X-Tenant-ID) on all 16 authenticated endpoints via authenticate middleware (1 public route excluded: GET /shared/:token). Combined mode derives tenant from JWT (X-Tenant-ID not needed), enforces user permissions, and sets source_module from module identity for accurate audit attribution.</p><p>Multi-tenant isolation on all read and write operations.</p><p>API Key middleware validates module-tenant access via tenant_module_access table.</p><p>UUID validation middleware on all :id parameters --- returns 400 for invalid UUIDs.</p><p>Error sanitization on all 17 catch blocks --- never leaks database internals.</p><p>File access audit trail via file_access_logs with user_id, IP address, user agent, action.</p><p>Storage statistics with quota summary, file type counts, by_entity and by_module breakdowns.</p><p>Pagination via limit and offset query parameters (default limit 50). Response is a JSON array of file objects.</p><p>Filter support on list: source_module, mime_type, entity_type, category, search (ILIKE on original_name), sort (created_at, file_size, original_name), date range (created_after, created_before).</p><p>Orphaned file cleanup: if DB INSERT fails after file save, file is automatically removed from storage.</p><p>Redis caching with graceful degradation (operates without Redis).</p><p>Elasticsearch indexing with graceful degradation (operates without ES).</p><h2>OUT OF SCOPE (Phase 1 --- File Attachment Service boundary):</h2><p><strong>S3/MinIO object storage migration</strong> --- LocalStorageProvider is production-ready; S3StorageProvider is a config swap planned for Phase 2. Storage provider abstraction is already in place.</p><p><strong>Virus/malware scanning</strong> --- scan_status and scanned_at columns exist in file_attachments table but no scanning service is integrated.</p><p><strong>Image thumbnail generation</strong> --- has_thumbnail, thumbnail_path columns exist but no thumbnail generation pipeline is implemented.</p><p>Full-text content extraction from uploaded files (PDF text extraction, OCR).</p><p>Vector embedding of file content for semantic search via Qdrant.</p><p>Real-time file upload progress (WebSocket-based progress tracking).</p><p>Client-side chunked upload for files larger than 100MB.</p><p>CDN integration for cached file delivery.</p><p>File format conversion (PDF to image, document to PDF, etc.).</p><p>Watermarking or digital stamping of downloaded files.</p><p>Bulk import/export of files.</p><p><strong>File-level access control lists (ACLs)</strong> --- access is controlled at entity level via entity_type permissions, not per-file.</p><p><strong>Retention policy enforcement</strong> --- soft-deleted files remain in database indefinitely until hard-deleted.</p><p><strong>Email/SMS notifications on file events</strong> (handled by Notification Service separately).</p><p><strong>Document lifecycle management</strong> (SOPs, versioning, review/approval) --- handled by separate Document Service (document.service.js).</p><h1>3. Clear Responsibility Split</h1><h2>3.1 SaaS Platform (Owned by Platform Team):</h2><p>Provide and maintain the File Attachment Service as a centralised, tenant-isolated binary file management engine.</p><p>Enforce file upload constraints: 100MB max file size (multer + quota), blocked dangerous extensions, per-tenant storage quotas with auto-creation and trigger-based tracking.</p><p>Generate and manage tenant-scoped storage paths: {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext.</p><p>Calculate SHA-256 checksums on every upload for integrity verification.</p><p>Auto-derive source_module from authentication context with priority: req.module.code for combined JWT + API Key mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf'), req.user.moduleCode for API key-only modules, 'platform' for JWT-only users, 'api_key' fallback for API keys without linked modules. This ensures files uploaded by modules on behalf of users are correctly attributed to the originating module in storage statistics.</p><p>Manage file versioning: version number increment, previous_version_id linking, is_current_version flagging, recursive CTE version history retrieval.</p><p>Maintain storage provider abstraction (LocalStorageProvider) with save, delete, exists, getFullPath methods for future S3 migration.</p><p>Enforce tenant isolation on all queries via tenant_id filtering. No cross-tenant file access is possible.</p><p>Provide three authentication modes on all 16 authenticated endpoints via authenticate middleware (1 public route excluded: GET /shared/:token): (a) JWT only for QAssure UI users, (b) JWT + API Key combined for module applications acting on behalf of logged-in users (tenant from JWT, user permissions enforced, source_module from module identity), (c) API Key + X-Tenant-ID for module system/cron operations.</p><p>Validate module-tenant access via tenant_module_access table (enabled = true check). Return MISSING_TENANT or MODULE_NOT_ASSIGNED errors for invalid API Key requests. In combined mode, return TENANT_MISMATCH if JWT tenant differs from API key's assigned tenant, and MODULE_NOT_ACTIVE if the module is deactivated for the tenant.</p><p>Provide UUID validation middleware for all route parameters. Return 400 INVALID_ID_FORMAT for malformed UUIDs.</p><p>Sanitise all error responses to prevent database internal leakage.</p><p>Provide file sharing infrastructure: token generation, expiry enforcement, max_downloads enforcement, public access route.</p><p>Provide storage statistics with per-entity-type and per-module breakdowns.</p><p>Log all file access events (download, preview, checkout, checkin) in file_access_logs.</p><p>Provide Redis caching and Elasticsearch indexing with graceful degradation.</p><p>Expose admin-only quota management endpoint (files:admin permission).</p><h2>3.2 Module Applications (Residing on Platform; Owned by App Teams --- LTTS):</h2><p>Use the File Attachment Service API with the appropriate authentication mode:</p><p><strong>For user-context operations (user uploads a file via module UI):</strong> Send both Authorization: Bearer (JWT obtained from verify-launch-token) and X-API-Key headers. X-Tenant-ID is NOT needed --- tenant is derived from JWT. User permissions (files:read, files:write) are enforced. uploaded_by and file_access_logs.user_id record the real user identity. source_module records the module identity (e.g., 'coc').</p><p><strong>For system/cron operations (no user context):</strong> Send X-API-Key + X-Tenant-ID headers. Module gets full access bypass. source_module records the module identity from API key.</p><p>Specify entity_type and entity_id when uploading files to link them to the correct module entity (e.g., entity_type='documents', entity_id=&lt;document_uuid&gt; for Document Service; entity_type='capa', entity_id=&lt;capa_uuid&gt; for CAPA module).</p><p>Provide required fields on upload: file (multipart), entity_type (string), entity_id (UUID). Optional fields: description, category, tags, metadata (JSONB).</p><p>Use the version upload endpoint (POST /:id/versions) for updating files rather than deleting and re-uploading. This preserves version history and audit trail.</p><p>Use the share endpoint to generate time-limited, download-limited links for external stakeholders (e.g., auditors, suppliers) without granting platform login access.</p><p>Do NOT implement custom file storage logic --- always delegate to platform's file attachment service.</p><p>Do NOT store file metadata in the module's own database --- use platform as the system of record for all file attachments. Use the entity link (entity_type + entity_id) to associate files with module records.</p><p>Do NOT construct file paths manually or access the uploads directory directly --- always use service API endpoints for file access.</p><p>Use SSO launch token flow to obtain both tenant context and user session JWT dynamically in production: call POST /modules/verify-launch-token with X-API-Key and the launch token to receive a JWT (24h expiry), user details (including department, designation, user category), tenant details, and permissions. Use this JWT in Authorization: Bearer header alongside X-API-Key for all user-context platform calls. Use .env TENANT_ID + X-Tenant-ID header for development and system/cron operations only.</p><h1>4. API List (Refer to Excel Sheet shared)</h1><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>#</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Method</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Endpoint</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Auth</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>1</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>POST</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/upload</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write</p></td><td><p>Upload single file (multipart)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>2</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>POST</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/upload/multiple</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write</p></td><td><p>Upload multiple files (up to 10)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>3</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read</p></td><td><p>List files (paginated, filterable)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>4</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Get single file by ID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>5</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>PUT</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Update file metadata</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>6</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>DELETE</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Delete file (soft; ?hard=true for permanent)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>7</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/download</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Download file (Content-Disposition: attachment)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>8</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/preview</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Preview file (Content-Disposition: inline)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>9</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>POST</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/versions</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Upload new version of existing file</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>10</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/versions</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Get version history (recursive CTE)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>11</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>POST</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/:id/share</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Create share link (token, expiry, max_downloads)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>12</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>DELETE</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/shares/:shareId</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:write + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Revoke share link</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>13</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/shared/:token</p></td><td><p>PUBLIC (no auth)</p></td><td><p>Access shared file via token</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>14</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/entity/:entity_type/:entity_id</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read + validateUUID</p></td><td><p>Get files by entity (paginated)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>15</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/stats</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read</p></td><td><p>Get storage statistics (by entity, by module)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>16</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>GET</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/quota</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:read</p></td><td><p>Get tenant storage quota</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>17</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>PUT</strong></p></td><td><p>/api/v1/files/quota</p></td><td><p>authenticate + files:admin</p></td><td><p>Update tenant storage quota (admin only)</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Route ordering note: /stats, /quota, /entity/:type/:id, /shared/:token are registered BEFORE /:id to prevent Express matching static segments as UUID parameters.</em></p><h1>5. Typical Workflow</h1><h2>5.1 Write Path (File Upload &amp; Management):</h2><p><strong>1. Upload Single File:</strong> Tenant user or module calls POST /api/v1/files/upload with multipart form data: file (required, binary), entity_type (required, e.g., 'documents'), entity_id (required, UUID of parent entity), and optional: description, category, tags (comma-separated string or JSON array), metadata (JSONB). The API validates: file presence (returns VALIDATION_ERROR 'No file uploaded'), entity_type and entity_id presence (returns VALIDATION_ERROR 'entity_type and entity_id are required'), file extension not in blocked list (.exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .ps1, .msi, .dll, .com, .scr, .vbs, .js --- returns error 'File type .exe is not allowed'), file size under 100MB (returns FILE_TOO_LARGE 'File size exceeds 100MB limit'), tenant quota not exceeded (returns QUOTA_ERROR for both individual file and total storage).</p><p>Platform generates: stored_name as {uuid}_{sanitized_original_name}.ext, storage path as {tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{stored_name}, SHA-256 checksum via crypto.createHash('sha256').update(buffer).digest('hex'), source_module derived from auth context with priority: req.module.code for combined mode (e.g., 'coc', 'dhf'), 'platform' for JWT-only users, req.user.moduleCode for API key-only modules (e.g., 'aice', 'dhf'), or 'api_key' fallback if API key has no linked module. File is saved to storage via storageProvider.save(relativePath, buffer), then database record is inserted into file_attachments. If DB INSERT fails, file is automatically cleaned up from storage (orphan prevention). Redis cache is invalidated for entity files list. Elasticsearch index is updated via IndexingHooks. Returns full file object with 201 status.</p><p><strong>2. Upload Multiple Files:</strong> POST /api/v1/files/upload/multiple accepts up to 10 files via multer array ('files' field, max 10). All files are uploaded in parallel via Promise.all, sharing the same entity_type and entity_id. Returns array of results with per-file success/error status. Quota is checked per file individually.</p><p><strong>3. Update Metadata:</strong> PUT /api/v1/files/:id updates allowed fields: description (text), category (varchar), tags (cast as text[]), metadata (cast as JSONB). File content changes go through versioning (POST /:id/versions), not metadata update. Sets updated_at timestamp. Returns 'No valid fields to update' error if no recognized fields provided. Returns full file object with 200 status.</p><p><strong>4. Soft Delete:</strong> DELETE /api/v1/files/:id sets deleted_at = NOW() timestamp. PostgreSQL trigger (trg_update_storage_usage) automatically decrements used_storage_bytes and file_count in storage_quotas using GREATEST(..., 0) to prevent negative values. File remains on disk for potential recovery. Redis cache invalidated. Elasticsearch index updated. Returns { success: true, message: 'File deleted' }.</p><p><strong>5. Hard Delete:</strong> DELETE /api/v1/files/:id?hard=true permanently removes: database record (DELETE FROM file_attachments WHERE id = $1 AND tenant_id = $2), physical file from storage via storageProvider.delete(file_path), thumbnail if exists via storageProvider.delete(thumbnail_path). Returns 404 on subsequent GET. Irreversible. Quota adjusts via DELETE trigger.</p><h2>5.2 Versioning:</h2><p><strong>Minor Versioning:</strong> Default behavior. Every POST /api/v1/files/:id/versions with new file (multipart) performs: fetches current record by ID and tenant_id, marks it as is_current_version=false via UPDATE, inserts new record with version = previous_version + 1, is_current_version=true, previous_version_id = old record ID. SHA-256 checksum is calculated for the new file. Both old and new records remain in database --- version history is immutable and never deleted.</p><p><strong>Version History Retrieval:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/:id/versions uses a recursive CTE (Common Table Expression) that traverses the previous_version_id chain in both directions (forward via self-join on previous_version_id, backward via matching previous_version_id = id). Returns complete version lineage with: id, version, file_size, checksum, original_name, uploaded_by_email (resolved via LEFT JOIN users), created_at for each version. Ordered by version number ascending.</p><p><strong>Version Chain Structure:</strong> file_attachments.previous_version_id creates a self-referencing linked list. Version 1 has previous_version_id=null. Version 2 points to Version 1. Version 3 points to Version 2. Only the latest version has is_current_version=true. Standard queries (list, get by entity) only return current versions (WHERE is_current_version = true AND deleted_at IS NULL).</p><h2>5.3 Read/Search Path:</h2><p><strong>Get by ID:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/:id --- Redis cached (300s TTL). Returns full file object with uploaded_by_email resolved via LEFT JOIN users. Filters by tenant_id for isolation.</p><p><strong>List Files:</strong> GET /api/v1/files?limit=50&amp;offset=0 --- returns a JSON array of file objects. Supports limit and offset query parameters for pagination. Supports filters: source_module, mime_type, entity_type, category, search (ILIKE on original_name), sort_by (created_at|file_size|original_name), sort_order (ASC|DESC), created_after, created_before. Only returns active files (deleted_at IS NULL, is_current_version = true).</p><p><strong>Get by Entity:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/entity/:entity_type/:entity_id --- returns a JSON array of all files linked to a specific entity. Used by Document Service, CAPA module, Training module, etc. to retrieve their linked files.</p><p><strong>Storage Stats:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/stats --- returns four sections: quota (max_storage, used_storage, available, usage_percent), files (total, images, pdfs, documents counts), by_entity (count + size per entity_type), and by_module (count + size per source_module e.g., 'platform', 'coc').</p><p><strong>Storage Quota:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/quota --- returns current quota status: max_storage_bytes, used_storage_bytes, file_count, max_file_size_bytes, allowed_mime_types, blocked_extensions, usage_percentage.</p><h2>5.4 File Sharing Path:</h2><p><strong>Create Share:</strong> POST /api/v1/files/:id/share with body: share_type ('link'|'user'), permissions ('view'|'download'), expires_at (ISO timestamp) or expires_in_hours (number, auto-converted), max_downloads (integer), shared_with_user_id, shared_with_email. Service generates 64-char hex token via crypto.randomBytes(32). Returns share object with share_token, share_url, expires_at, max_downloads. Redis cached (3600s TTL).</p><p><strong>Access Shared File:</strong> GET /api/v1/files/shared/:token --- PUBLIC route (no authentication). Service: looks up share by token (Redis cached), validates expiry (expires_at &gt; NOW()), validates download count (current_downloads &lt; max_downloads), increments current_downloads, resolves file path via storageProvider.getFullPath(), serves file with correct Content-Type and Content-Disposition headers. Returns 404 if share not found, expired, or download limit reached.</p><p><strong>Revoke Share:</strong> DELETE /api/v1/files/shares/:shareId --- sets is_active=false. Invalidates Redis cache for the share token.</p><h2>5.5 Retention/Deletion:</h2><p>Phase 1: No automated retention policy enforcement. Soft-deleted files remain in database with deleted_at timestamp set. Hard delete permanently removes file and database record.</p><p><strong>Quota Recovery:</strong> Soft delete triggers automatic quota decrement via PostgreSQL trigger. Restoring a soft-deleted file (clearing deleted_at) would trigger quota increment.</p><p><strong>Planned Phase 2:</strong> Configurable retention periods per entity_type. Scheduled cleanup job to hard-delete files past retention period. Archived storage tier for long-term retention at reduced cost.</p><h2>5.6 Audit Trail:</h2><p>file_access_logs records (inserted on download, preview, and any file access): file_id, tenant_id, user_id, action ('download'|'preview'|'access'), ip_address (from req.ip), user_agent (from req.headers), created_at.</p><p>Storage quota changes tracked via PostgreSQL trigger --- every INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on file_attachments automatically adjusts used_storage_bytes and file_count.</p><p>Share access tracked via current_downloads counter and last_accessed_at timestamp on file_shares.</p><p><strong>Authentication mode impacts audit attribution:</strong> In combined JWT + API Key mode, uploaded_by and file_access_logs.user_id record the real user identity (from JWT), while source_module records the originating module (from API key). This provides GxP-compliant traceability --- auditors can see both who performed the action and which module facilitated it. In API Key-only mode, uploaded_by records the module service account and source_module records the module code. In JWT-only mode, uploaded_by records the platform user and source_module is set to 'platform'.</p><h1>6. PostgreSQL DB --- MODEL</h1><p>The File Attachment Service uses 4 PostgreSQL tables: file_attachments (master record with binary file metadata, entity linking, versioning, and storage path), storage_quotas (per-tenant storage limits with trigger-maintained usage counters), file_shares (token-based file sharing with expiry and download limits), and file_access_logs (audit trail for file access events). All tables enforce multi-tenant isolation via tenant_id foreign key with ON DELETE CASCADE. The file_attachments table serves as the central entity. A PostgreSQL trigger function (update_storage_usage) automatically maintains used_storage_bytes and file_count in storage_quotas on INSERT, UPDATE (soft-delete/restore), and DELETE operations.</p><h2>6.1 ER Diagram:</h2><p><img src="data:image/png;base64," /></p><p><em>Figure 6.1: Entity Relationship Diagram --- File Attachment Service</em></p><p>file_attachments.tenant_id → tenants.id (ON DELETE CASCADE)</p><p>file_attachments.uploaded_by → users.id</p><p>file_attachments.previous_version_id → file_attachments.id (self-referencing version chain)</p><p>storage_quotas.tenant_id → tenants.id (UNIQUE --- one quota per tenant)</p><p>file_shares.tenant_id → tenants.id, file_shares.file_id → file_attachments.id</p><p>file_access_logs.file_id → file_attachments.id, file_access_logs.user_id → users.id</p><h2>6.2 Entities &amp; Attributes:</h2><h3>6.2.1 Entity: file_attachments (32 columns)</h3><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Data Type</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Constraint / FK</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Example</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>PK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()</p></td><td><p>Unique file identifier</p></td><td><p>daf3c8ad-...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tenant_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, INDEX</p></td><td><p>Tenant isolation</p></td><td><p>c0000000-...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>original_name</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(500)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>User-uploaded filename</p></td><td><p>test-upload.txt</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>stored_name</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(500)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>UUID-based stored name</p></td><td><p>daf3c8ad_test-upload.txt</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_path</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(1000)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>Relative storage path</p></td><td><p>c000.../documents/2026/02/daf3...txt</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>mime_type</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(255)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>MIME type</p></td><td><p>text/plain</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_size</strong></p></td><td><p>BIGINT</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>File size in bytes</p></td><td><p>18</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>checksum</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(128)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>SHA-256 hash</p></td><td><p>a591a6d40...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>storage_provider</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'local'</p></td><td><p>Storage backend</p></td><td><p>local</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>storage_bucket</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(255)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>S3 bucket (Phase 2)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>storage_region</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(100)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>S3 region (Phase 2)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>entity_type</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(100)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, INDEX</p></td><td><p>Parent entity type</p></td><td><p>documents</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>entity_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, INDEX</p></td><td><p>Parent entity ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>category</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(100)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>File category</p></td><td><p>specification</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>description</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>File description</p></td><td><p>Test file upload</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tags</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT[]</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>PostgreSQL text array</p></td><td><p>{sop,quality}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>version</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 1</p></td><td><p>Version number</p></td><td><p>1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>is_current_version</strong></p></td><td><p>BOOLEAN</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT true, INDEX (partial)</p></td><td><p>Active version flag</p></td><td><p>true</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>previous_version_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>FK → file_attachments(id), Nullable</p></td><td><p>Version chain link</p></td><td><p>UUID or null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>is_public</strong></p></td><td><p>BOOLEAN</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT false</p></td><td><p>Public access flag</p></td><td><p>false</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>access_level</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'private'</p></td><td><p>Access level</p></td><td><p>private</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>download_count</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 0</p></td><td><p>Total downloads</p></td><td><p>5</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>has_thumbnail</strong></p></td><td><p>BOOLEAN</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT false</p></td><td><p>Thumbnail exists</p></td><td><p>false</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>thumbnail_path</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(1000)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Thumbnail storage path</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>metadata</strong></p></td><td><p>JSONB</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT '{}'</p></td><td><p>Extensible metadata</p></td><td><p>{}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>scan_status</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Virus scan status (Phase 2)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>scanned_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Scan timestamp (Phase 2)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>uploaded_by</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>FK → users(id), Nullable</p></td><td><p>Uploader user ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>source_module</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(100)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'platform', INDEX</p></td><td><p>Origin module</p></td><td><p>platform</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Created timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>updated_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Updated timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>deleted_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>Nullable, INDEX</p></td><td><p>Soft delete timestamp</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>NOTES: tags is TEXT[] not JSONB. file_size is BIGINT (returns as string from node-pg, parsed to integer in _formatAttachment). is_current_version partial index filters WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND is_current_version = TRUE. previous_version_id creates a self-referencing linked list for version chains. source_module is auto-derived from auth context, never user-supplied.</em></p><h3>6.2.2 Entity: storage_quotas (10 columns)</h3><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Data Type</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Constraint / FK</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Example</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>PK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()</p></td><td><p>Quota record ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tenant_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → tenants(id), UNIQUE</p></td><td><p>Tenant isolation</p></td><td><p>c0000000-...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>max_storage_bytes</strong></p></td><td><p>BIGINT</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 10737418240 (10GB)</p></td><td><p>Max total storage</p></td><td><p>10737418240</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>used_storage_bytes</strong></p></td><td><p>BIGINT</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 0</p></td><td><p>Current usage (trigger-maintained)</p></td><td><p>1536</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_count</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 0</p></td><td><p>Active file count (trigger-maintained)</p></td><td><p>15</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>max_file_size_bytes</strong></p></td><td><p>BIGINT</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 104857600 (100MB)</p></td><td><p>Max single file size</p></td><td><p>104857600</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>allowed_mime_types</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT[]</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Whitelist (null = all allowed)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>blocked_extensions</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT[]</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Blacklist</p></td><td><p>{.exe,.bat}</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Created timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>updated_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Updated timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>NOTES: max_storage_bytes and used_storage_bytes are BIGINT. PostgreSQL trigger update_storage_usage() maintains used_storage_bytes and file_count automatically on file_attachments INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE. The trigger uses GREATEST(..., 0) to prevent negative values. Quota auto-creates via service when first upload occurs for a tenant.</em></p><h3>PostgreSQL Trigger Function:</h3><p>CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_storage_usage() --- Handles INSERT (increment), DELETE (decrement), UPDATE with NEW.deleted_at IS NOT NULL AND OLD.deleted_at IS NULL (soft-delete decrement), UPDATE with NEW.deleted_at IS NULL AND OLD.deleted_at IS NOT NULL (restore increment). Uses GREATEST(used_storage_bytes - file_size, 0) and GREATEST(file_count - 1, 0) to prevent negative values.</p><h3>6.2.3 Entity: file_shares (15 columns)</h3><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Data Type</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Constraint / FK</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Example</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>PK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()</p></td><td><p>Share record ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tenant_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE</p></td><td><p>Tenant isolation</p></td><td><p>c0000000-...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → file_attachments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE</p></td><td><p>Shared file</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>share_token</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(255)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, UNIQUE</p></td><td><p>64-char hex token</p></td><td><p>a3f8c2d1...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>share_type</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'link'</p></td><td><p>Share type</p></td><td><p>link</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>shared_with_user_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>FK → users(id), Nullable</p></td><td><p>Target user (for 'user' type)</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>shared_with_email</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(255)</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Target email</p></td><td><p>null</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>permissions</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 'view'</p></td><td><p>Access level</p></td><td><p>view/download</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>expires_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Expiry timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>max_downloads</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Download cap (null = unlimited)</p></td><td><p>5</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>current_downloads</strong></p></td><td><p>INTEGER</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT 0</p></td><td><p>Downloads consumed</p></td><td><p>2</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>is_active</strong></p></td><td><p>BOOLEAN</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT true</p></td><td><p>Active flag (false = revoked)</p></td><td><p>true</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>last_accessed_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Last access time</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_by</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>FK → users(id), Nullable</p></td><td><p>Share creator</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>Created timestamp</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>NOTES: share_token is UNIQUE. expires_at can be set directly or auto-calculated from expires_in_hours (service converts: new Date(Date.now() + hours * 3600000).toISOString()). max_downloads null means unlimited. current_downloads is incremented atomically on each access. is_active=false means share has been revoked.</em></p><h3>6.2.4 Entity: file_access_logs (8 columns)</h3><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Data Type</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Constraint / FK</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Description</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Example</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>PK, DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()</p></td><td><p>Log record ID</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>tenant_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE</p></td><td><p>Tenant isolation</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>file_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → file_attachments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE</p></td><td><p>File accessed</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>user_id</strong></p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL, FK → users(id)</p></td><td><p>Who accessed</p></td><td><p>UUID</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>action</strong></p></td><td><p>VARCHAR(50)</p></td><td><p>NOT NULL</p></td><td><p>Action type</p></td><td><p>download/preview/access</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>ip_address</strong></p></td><td><p>INET</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Client IP</p></td><td><p>192.168.1.1</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>user_agent</strong></p></td><td><p>TEXT</p></td><td><p>Nullable</p></td><td><p>Browser UA string</p></td><td><p>Mozilla/5.0...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>created_at</strong></p></td><td><p>TIMESTAMPTZ</p></td><td><p>DEFAULT NOW()</p></td><td><p>When accessed</p></td><td><p>ISO datetime</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>NOTES: Records are insert-only (append-only audit log). ip_address and user_agent are captured from Express request object when available. action values include 'download', 'preview', 'access' for share access.</em></p><h1>7. Qdrant (Vector DB)</h1><p><strong>Phase 1 Status: NOT USED by File Attachment Service.</strong></p><p>Binary file content is stored on the filesystem via LocalStorageProvider. File metadata is stored in PostgreSQL (file_attachments table). No vector embeddings of file content are generated in Phase 1.</p><h2>Planned for Phase 2:</h2><p>Collection Name: file_content_vec_v1</p><p>Vector Dimension: 1536 (OpenAI text-embedding-3-small) or 768 (sentence-transformers)</p><p>Payload Fields: file_id (string), tenant_id (string --- mandatory filter), original_name (string), entity_type (string), entity_id (string), mime_type (string), category (string), source_module (string), created_at (ISO string)</p><p>Payload Indexes: tenant_id, entity_type, mime_type, source_module, created_at</p><p>Use Case: Semantic search across extracted file content (PDF text, document text), similar file discovery, AI-powered content recommendations, duplicate detection via vector similarity rather than checksum matching.</p><p>Prerequisite: Content extraction pipeline (PDF text extraction, OCR for images, document parsing) must be implemented first to generate text from binary files before vector embedding.</p><h1>8. Object Storage</h1><h2>Folder Structure Hierarchy:</h2><p>Root: UPLOAD_DIR (default: ./uploads/, configurable via environment variable)</p><p>Pattern: {UPLOAD_DIR}/{tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{sanitized_name}.ext</p><p><strong>Example hierarchy:</strong></p><p>uploads/</p><p>  c0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/   (Tenant: Pharma Corp)</p><p>    documents/   (Entity type)</p><p>      2026/   (Year)</p><p>        02/   (Month)</p><p>          daf3c8ad-3660-4c13-8b57-0daf3cc9aaf0_test-upload.txt</p><p>          d7cbcb77-a8f1-4e22-b901-3dc77f8e22a1_report-v2.pdf</p><p>    capa/</p><p>      2026/</p><p>        02/</p><p>          f1a2b3c4-..._corrective-action-photo.jpg</p><p>    training/</p><p>      2026/</p><p>        01/</p><p>          a9b8c7d6-..._sop-training-material.pdf</p><p>  d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002/   (Tenant: Another Org)</p><p>    documents/</p><p>    suppliers/</p><p>    temp/   (Temporary storage)</p><p>    thumbnails/   (Thumbnail storage)</p><h3>Storage Provider Abstraction:</h3><p>LocalStorageProvider (Phase 1 --- current):</p><p>save(relativePath, buffer) --- Creates directory tree via fs.mkdirSync({recursive: true}), writes buffer via fs.writeFileSync.</p><p>delete(relativePath) --- Removes file via fs.unlinkSync. Silently ignores if file doesn't exist.</p><p>exists(relativePath) --- Checks via fs.existsSync.</p><p>getFullPath(relativePath) --- Joins UPLOAD_DIR + relativePath. Controller uses path.resolve() for absolute path.</p><h3>S3 Migration Path (Phase 2):</h3><p>Implement S3StorageProvider with identical interface (save, delete, exists, getFullPath). S3 key structure maps 1:1 to local folder hierarchy: s3://{bucket}/{tenant_id}/{entity_type}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{uuid}_{name}.ext. No changes to service or controller code required --- swap provider via configuration.</p><h1>SECTION 10 --- REDIS CACHE DETAILS</h1><p>File Attachment Service uses 4 Redis cache key patterns with graceful degradation. The service operates normally if Redis is unavailable --- all cache operations are wrapped in try/catch and failures are logged but never block the main operation.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Cache Key Pattern</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Purpose</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>TTL</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Invalidation</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>file:{tenant_id}:{file_id}</p></td><td><p>Single file metadata cache</p></td><td><p>300s (5 min)</p></td><td><p>On update, delete</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>quota:{tenant_id}</p></td><td><p>Tenant storage quota</p></td><td><p>60s (1 min)</p></td><td><p>On upload, delete, quota update</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>share:{share_token}</p></td><td><p>Share token lookup</p></td><td><p>3600s (1 hr)</p></td><td><p>On revoke</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>entity_files:{entity_type}:{entity_id}</p></td><td><p>Files by entity list</p></td><td><p>120s (2 min)</p></td><td><p>On upload, delete to entity</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Redis Service Integration:</h3><p>File: src/infrastructure/cache/redis.service.js --- singleton instance exported as module.exports = new RedisService().</p><p>Methods used: get(key, parseJson=true), set(key, value, ttlSeconds), delete(key). Note: The Redis service uses delete() method, NOT del().</p><p>Cache invalidation method: _invalidateCache(tenantId, fileId, entityType, entityId) --- deletes all relevant cache keys after any write operation (upload, update, delete, share revoke).</p><p>Lazy initialization: getRedis() function returns singleton Redis instance on first call, returns null if Redis is unavailable. Every cache operation checks for null before proceeding.</p><h3>Platform-level Redis usage that benefits File Attachment Service indirectly:</h3><p><strong>Session caching:</strong> JWT session data cached by AuthService for fast auth validation on every request.</p><p><strong>Permission caching:</strong> User permissions cached by PermissionService, used by authorization middleware for files:read/files:write/files:admin checks.</p><h3>Planned Phase 2 enhancements:</h3><p><strong>File content cache:</strong> Large frequently-accessed files cached in Redis for sub-millisecond retrieval.</p><p><strong>Share token bloom filter:</strong> Probabilistic check before DB lookup for invalid/revoked tokens.</p><p><strong>Upload rate limiting:</strong> Per-tenant upload rate tracking via Redis INCR + EXPIRE.</p>	\N	minor_edit	\N	\N	\N	\N	4ccf68ad-485c-495a-935b-10d74b173a52	2026-03-26 05:47:23.332018+00	platform	\N
08a022d0-e144-4439-bf07-213efd51575e	37259066-36bd-498f-94a0-87119cf275ff	352d7e21-5155-4ff8-8169-284bf5ece3e7	0.1	0	1	in_review	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nQAssure\nDocument Service API Integration Guide\nFor Module Developers\nAudience \tModule Developers integrating with QAssure Document\nManagement Service\nBase URL (Dev) \thttp://localhost:3000/api/v1\nBase URL (Prod) \thttps://backendqassure.tech4bizsolutions.com/\napi/v1\nLast Verified \t28-Feb-2026 (all 17 endpoints verified)\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 1 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n1. What is the Document Service?\nThe QAssure Document Service provides a centralized, controlled document management system for\nquality-regulated environments (e.g., Pharma, Manufacturing). It allows modules to:\n• Create and manage controlled documents (SOPs, Policies, Forms, Work Instructions, etc.)\n• Version-control document content with major/minor versioning (e.g., 0.1 → 0.2 → 1.0)\n• Drive a full document lifecycle from draft → in_review → approved → effective → obsolete\n• Lock documents for editing via a Checkout/Checkin mechanism (prevents concurrent edits)\n• Auto-number documents by type and year (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)\n• Trigger periodic review alerts based on category-defined review frequencies\n• Maintain a complete audit trail with workflow history, access logs, and user attribution\n2. Authentication Modes\nThe Document Service supports three authentication modes. Choose based on your module's use case:\nMode A — JWT Only (QAssure UI Users)\nStandard user login via the QAssure UI. Best for direct user-driven operations.\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt_token>\nMode B — JWT + API Key (Combined / Recommended for Modules)\nYour module launches via SSO, obtains a module_jwt, and sends both the JWT and your module's API Key. This\nis the recommended mode for user-context operations.\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\n💡 Advantages of Mode B: Audit trail records the real user identity (not a service account). User's actual\nrole-based permissions are enforced. Module identity is tracked for source attribution. X-Tenant-ID is not\nneeded — tenant is derived from the JWT.\nMode C — API Key + Tenant ID (System / Cron Operations)\nFor background module operations with no user context (automated jobs, cron tasks).\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\nX-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid>\n⚠ Requires document:read and document:write permissions configured in api_key_permissions table.\n3. SSO / Module Launch Flow (Recommended)\nFollow these 3 steps to obtain a module_jwt for Mode B (JWT + API Key):\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 2 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nStep 1 — User Logs into QAssure\nPOST /api/v1/auth/login\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"email": "admin@yourcompany.com",\n"password": "YourPassword"\n}\nResponse: Save data.access_token as jwt_token.\nStep 2 — Launch Your Module\nPOST /api/v1/modules/<your_module_id>/launch\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt_token>\nResponse: Contains data.launch_url with a ?token=<launch_token> parameter. Extract and save the\nlaunch_token.\nStep 3 — Verify Launch Token (Exchange for Module Session JWT)\nPOST /api/v1/modules/verify-launch-token\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"token": "<launch_token>"\n}\nResponse Fields:\nField \tDescription\ndata.token \tModule session JWT — use as Bearer token for all subsequent API calls\ndata.user \tFull user object (id, email, name, department, designation)\ndata.tenant \tTenant details (id, name, slug, company_name, logo)\ndata.permissions \tArray of permission strings granted to this user\ndata.module \tModule identity info\ndata.expires_in \t86400 (24 hours)\ndata.expires_at \tISO timestamp of expiry\nSave data.token as your module_jwt. Use it with Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt> + X-API-Key:\n<your_api_key> for all subsequent document API calls.\n4. Permissions Required\nPermission \tDescription\ndocument:read \tView documents, categories, versions, due-for-review list\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 3 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPermission \tDescription\ndocument:write \tCreate, update, version, checkout/checkin, and all lifecycle actions\nWho gets these permissions automatically:\n• Tenant Admin — has both document:read and document:write (seeded)\n• Super Admin — bypasses all permission checks\n• Custom Roles — when a Tenant Admin grants document permissions\n• API Key (Mode C) — requires explicit document:read / document:write in api_key_permissions table\n• JWT + API Key (Mode B) — user's actual role-based permissions are enforced\n5. API Reference\n5.1 Reference Data APIs\nThese are the first APIs to call. They return static/seeded data your module needs to build dropdowns, filter\noptions, and validate inputs.\nGET /api/v1/documents/categories\nReturns tenant-scoped document categories.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nQuery Parameters \tNone\nExample Request (Mode B):\nGET /api/v1/documents/categories\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [\n{\n"id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",\n"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",\n"code": "SOP",\n"description": "SOPs for regulated operations",\n"parent_id": null,\n"requires_training": true,\n"retention_years": 10,\n"review_frequency_months": 12\n},\n{\n"id": "...",\n"name": "Forms",\n"code": "FRM",\n"review_frequency_months": 24\n}\n]\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 4 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n}\nCategory List (Pharma Corp tenant):\nCode \tName \tReview Frequency\nFRM \tForms \t24 months\nPOL \tPolicies \t12 months\nQM \tQuality Manual \t12 months\nSPEC \tSpecifications \t12 months\nSOP \tStandard Operating Procedures \t12 months\nWI \tWork Instructions \t24 months\n💡 Developer Tip: Save category.id from this response — you will need it in category_id when creating\ndocuments. The review_frequency_months field is used to auto-calculate next_review_date when a document\nbecomes effective.\nGET /api/v1/documents/types\nReturns all available document type codes. No document:read permission required — only authentication.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tAuthenticated only\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [\n{ "code": "SOP", "name": "Standard Operating Procedure" },\n{ "code": "WI", "name": "Work Instruction" },\n{ "code": "POL", "name": "Policy" },\n{ "code": "FRM", "name": "Form" },\n{ "code": "SPEC", "name": "Specification" },\n{ "code": "QM", "name": "Quality Manual" },\n{ "code": "PROC", "name": "Procedure" },\n{ "code": "GUIDE", "name": "Guideline" },\n{ "code": "REF", "name": "Reference Document" }\n]\n}\n💡 The code value is what you pass as document_type when creating a document. The auto-number prefix is\nderived from this code (e.g., SOP-2026-0001).\nGET /api/v1/documents/statuses\nReturns all possible document lifecycle statuses. No document:read permission required.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tAuthenticated only\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 5 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [\n{ "code": "draft", \t"name": "Draft", \t"description": "Document is being created or\nedited" },\n{ "code": "in_review", "name": "In Review", "description": "Document is under review" },\n{ "code": "approved", "name": "Approved", "description": "Document has been approved" },\n{ "code": "effective", "name": "Effective", "description": "Document is currently in effect"\n},\n{ "code": "obsolete", "name": "Obsolete", "description": "Document has been superseded" },\n{ "code": "archived", "name": "Archived", "description": "Document is archived for\nhistorical purposes" }\n]\n}\nGET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review\nReturns effective documents whose next_review_date falls within the specified window. Useful for building\ncompliance dashboards or sending review reminders.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nQuery Parameters:\nParameter \tType \tDefault \tDescription\ndays_ahead \tinteger \t30 \tNumber of days ahead to check\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=90\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n• Only returns documents with a non-null next_review_date (i.e., documents linked to a category)\n• Documents without a category will never appear here (their next_review_date is null)\n5.2 Document CRUD APIs\nPOST /api/v1/documents — Create Document\nCreates a new controlled document. An initial version 0.1 is auto-created. Document number is auto-generated.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tHTTP 201 — Full 19-field document object\nRequest Body Fields:\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 6 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\ntitle \tstring \tRequired \tDocument title (max 500 chars)\ndocument_type \tstring \tRequired \tType code from GET /types (e.g., "SOP")\ndescription \tstring \tOptional \tShort description\ncontent \tstring \tOptional \tPlain-text document body (stored in version 0.1)\ncontent_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of the content\ndepartment \tstring \tOptional \tOwning department name\ncategory_id \tUUID \tOptional \tCategory UUID from GET /categories\nowner_id \tUUID \tOptional \tUser UUID; defaults to the authenticated user\ntags \tstring[] \tOptional \tArray of tag strings\ncustom_fields \tobject \tOptional \tAny additional JSONB metadata\nExample Request (Mode B):\nPOST /api/v1/documents\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"description": "Standard operating procedure for sterile manufacturing",\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Gowning",\n"department": "Manufacturing",\n"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",\n"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "gowning"]\n}\nExample Request (Mode C — API Key only):\nPOST /api/v1/documents\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\nX-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Module-Created SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure"\n}\nAuto-behaviors:\n• document_number auto-generated: <TYPE>-<YEAR>-<NNNN> (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)\n• status defaults to "draft"\n• Initial version 0.1 is auto-created in document_versions table\n• IndexingHooks.indexDocument() is triggered for search indexing\nValidation Error (HTTP 400):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "title and document_type are required" }\n}\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 7 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nGET /api/v1/documents — List Documents\nLists documents for the tenant with pagination and filtering.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nQuery Parameters:\nParameter \tType \tDescription\nlimit \tinteger \tResults per page (default: 50)\noffset \tinteger \tPagination offset (default: 0)\nstatus \tstring \tFilter by status code (e.g., draft, effective)\ncategory_id \tUUID \tFilter by category UUID\ndocument_type \tstring \tFilter by type code (e.g., SOP)\nowner_id \tUUID \tFilter by owner UUID\nsearch \tstring \tFull-text ILIKE search on title, document_number, description\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents?status=effective&document_type=SOP&limit=20&offset=0\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [ /* array of Document Summary objects */ ],\n"pagination": {\n"total": 47,\n"limit": 20,\n"offset": 0\n}\n}\nGET /api/v1/documents/:id — Get Single Document\nReturns full details for a single document by its UUID.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tFull 19-field document object\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 8 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n⚠ Checkout status is NOT included in this response. It is tracked separately in the document_checkouts table.\nNot Found (HTTP 404):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": { "code": "NOT_FOUND", "message": "Document not found" }\n}\nPUT /api/v1/documents/:id — Update Document Metadata\nUpdates document metadata only. Content changes must go through versioning (POST /versions).\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tFull 19-field updated document object\nUpdatable Fields:\nField \tType \tDescription\ntitle \tstring \tDocument title\ndescription \tstring \tDescription\ncategory_id \tUUID \tChange category\nowner_id \tUUID \tReassign owner\ndepartment \tstring \tDepartment\ntags \tstring[] \tReplace tags array\ncustom_fields \tobject \tReplace custom JSONB metadata\nExample Request:\nPUT /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP - Revised",\n"department": "Quality Assurance",\n"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "updated"]\n}\n5.3 Version Management APIs\nDocuments use major.minor versioning. Each new version resets the document to draft status.\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 9 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nVersion Type \tExample Transition \tis_major_version\nMinor edit \t0.1 → 0.2 \tfalse (default)\nMajor revision \t0.2 → 1.0, 1.3 → 2.0 \ttrue\nGET /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — List Versions\nReturns all versions for a document, ordered from newest to oldest.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tArray of 13-field version objects\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n⚠ content is NOT included in the version list response — only metadata is returned.\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — Create New Version\nCreates a new version of a document. The document status is reset to draft — it must go through the review\nprocess again.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tHTTP 201 — New 13-field version object\nRequest Body Fields:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\ncontent \tstring \tOptional \tNew plain-text content body\ncontent_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of content\nchange_summary \tstring \tOptional \tBrief description of what changed\nchange_reason \tstring \tOptional \tReason category (e.g., minor_edit, regulatory_update)\nis_major_version \tboolean \tOptional \ttrue for major version bump (default: false)\nfile_name \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file name\nfile_path \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file path/URL\nfile_size \tinteger \tOptional \tFile size in bytes\nmime_type \tstring \tOptional \tMIME type of attached file\nMinor Version Example:\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 10 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. References\\nISO 14644, EU GMP Annex 1",\n"change_summary": "Added references section",\n"change_reason": "minor_edit"\n}\nMajor Version Example:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"content": "Complete rewrite per new regulatory requirements.",\n"change_summary": "Major revision per EU GMP Annex 1 update",\n"change_reason": "regulatory_update",\n"is_major_version": true\n}\nKey Behaviors:\n• SHA-256 hash is auto-calculated from content for integrity verification\n• Document current_version_id is updated to the new version\n• Document status is reset to "draft"\n5.4 Checkout / Checkin APIs\nThe checkout/checkin mechanism prevents concurrent editing by granting an exclusive 24-hour lock on a\ndocument.\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkout — Checkout Document\nLocks the document for exclusive editing by the current user.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\nreason \tstring \tOptional \tWhy the document is being checked out\nExample Request:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Adding new section on environmental monitoring"\n}\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 11 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPossible Responses:\nScenario \tResponse\nSuccessful new checkout \t{ "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "<ISO timestamp +24h>" }\nSame user re-checking out \t{ "already_checked_out": true, "by_current_user": true }\nDifferent user has it checked out \tHTTP 500 — "Document is already checked out by another user"\n• Checkout expires automatically after 24 hours\n• Checkout status is logged in document_access_log\n• Checkout status is NOT visible in the GET /documents/:id response\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkin — Checkin Document\nReleases the exclusive lock. Only the user who performed the checkout can check in.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nRequest Body \tEmpty {} or no body required\nExample Request:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\nSuccess Response: { "checked_in": true }\nError Response (wrong user): "Document is not checked out by you"\n5.5 Lifecycle Workflow APIs\nThese endpoints drive the document through its full lifecycle. Always run them in the correct order.\n💡 Lifecycle Flow: draft → [Submit] → in_review → [Approve] → approved → [Make Effective] → effective →\n[Obsolete] → obsolete. OR: in_review / approved → [Reject] → draft (re-submit to restart)\nAll lifecycle endpoints return the full 19-field document object.\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/submit — Submit for Review\nSubmits a draft document for review. Starts a document_approval workflow instance.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 12 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nAttribute \tValue\nAllowed From \tdraft status only\nRequest Body \tEmpty {} required\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\nWhat happens internally:\n1. Validates document is in draft status\n2. Calls workflowEngine.startWorkflow({ workflowCode: 'document_approval', ... })\n3. Sets document status = 'in_review'\n4. Saves workflow_instance_id on the document\n5. Updates current version's status to in_review\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/approve — Approve Document\nApproves a document that is under review. Logs in workflow history.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \tin_review status only\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\ncomments \tstring \tOptional \tApproval comments\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"comments": "Reviewed and approved per QA checklist"\n}\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/reject — Reject Document\nRejects a document and returns it to draft. Logs in workflow history.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \tin_review or approved status\nRequest Body:\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 13 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\nreason \tstring \tRequired \tMust provide a rejection reason\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/reject\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Needs additional safety section per regulatory requirement"\n}\nValidation Error (missing reason):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": {\n"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",\n"message": "reason is required when rejecting a document"\n}\n}\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/make-effective — Make Effective\nMarks an approved document as effective. Auto-calculates the next review date.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \tapproved status only\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\neffective_date \tstring (ISO date) \tRequired \te.g., "2026-03-01" or "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"\nsignature_id \tUUID \tOptional \te-Signature UUID if applicable\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"effective_date": "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"\n}\nAuto-calculation of next_review_date:\n• If document has a category_id → next_review_date = effective_date +\ncategory.review_frequency_months\n• If no category → next_review_date = null\n• Example: SOP category has 12-month review → next_review_date = effective + 12 months\n⚠ Does NOT insert workflow history — this is by design in the current implementation.\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 14 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/obsolete — Make Obsolete\nMarks an effective document as obsolete (superseded).\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \teffective status only\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\nreason \tstring \tRequired \tWhy this document is being obsoleted\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Superseded by new revision SOP-2026-0010"\n}\nWhat happens internally:\n• Sets obsolete_date = NOW()\n• Inserts into workflow_history (action = 'obsolete', comments = reason) if workflow_instance_id exists\nValidation Error (missing reason):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": {\n"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",\n"message": "reason is required when making a document obsolete"\n}\n}\n6. Document Lifecycle State Machine\nFrom Status \tAction \tTo Status \tRequired Fields\ndraft \tSubmit \tin_review \t—\nin_review \tApprove \tapproved \tcomments (optional)\nin_review \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)\napproved \tMake Effective \teffective \teffective_date (required)\napproved \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)\neffective \tObsolete \tobsolete \treason (required)\n⚠ Creating a new version (POST /versions) from any status always resets the document to draft.\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 15 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nState Flow:\ndraft ──[Submit]──► in_review ──[Approve]──► approved ──[Make Effective]──►\neffective\n▲ \t│ \t│ \t│\n│ \t[Reject] \t[Reject]\n[Obsolete]\n└───────────────────────┘◄─────────────────────────┘ \t▼\nobsolete\n7. Response Schemas\nDocument Object (Full — 19 Fields)\nReturned by: POST /documents, GET /documents/:id, PUT /documents/:id, and all lifecycle endpoints.\n{\n"id": "uuid",\n"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",\n"description": "Description text",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"category": {\n"id": "uuid",\n"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",\n"code": "SOP"\n},\n"status": "draft",\n"current_version": "0.1",\n"version_status": "draft",\n"owner": {\n"id": "uuid",\n"email": "admin@company.com",\n"name": "Jane Doe"\n},\n"department": "Manufacturing",\n"effective_date": "2026-03-01",\n"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",\n"tags": ["sterile", "gmp"],\n"custom_fields": {},\n"workflow_instance_id": "uuid or null",\n"created_by": "admin@company.com",\n"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z",\n"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"\n}\nDocument Summary (10 Fields)\nReturned by: GET /documents (list) and GET /documents/due-for-review.\n{\n"id": "uuid",\n"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"category": "Standard Operating Procedures",\n"status": "effective",\n"current_version": "1.0",\n"owner": "admin@company.com",\n"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 16 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"\n}\nVersion Object (13 Fields)\nReturned by: GET /documents/:id/versions and POST /documents/:id/versions.\n{\n"id": "uuid",\n"version_number": "0.2",\n"major_version": 0,\n"minor_version": 2,\n"status": "draft",\n"file": {\n"name": "document.pdf",\n"path": "/uploads/document.pdf",\n"size": 204800,\n"mime_type": "application/pdf",\n"hash": "sha256-hex-string"\n},\n"change_summary": "Added references section",\n"change_reason": "minor_edit",\n"approved_by": "approver@company.com",\n"approved_at": "2026-02-28T11:00:00Z",\n"signature_id": "uuid or null",\n"created_by": "author@company.com",\n"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:30:00Z"\n}\n💡 file is null if no file attachment exists. content field is NOT included in the version list response.\n8. Error Reference\nAll errors follow a consistent format:\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": {\n"code": "ERROR_CODE",\n"message": "Human-readable message"\n}\n}\nHTTP\nStatus Code \tMessage \tWhen\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR title and document_type are required \tCreating without required fields\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when rejecting a\ndocument Reject without reason\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR effective_date is required \tMake Effective without date\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when making a\ndocument obsolete Obsolete without reason\n404 \tNOT_FOUND \tDocument not found Document not found or wrong\ntenant\n500 \tCREATE_ERROR \terror detail \tDB or internal error on create\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 17 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nHTTP\nStatus Code \tMessage \tWhen\n500 \tCHECKOUT_ERROR Document is already checked out by\nanother user Concurrent checkout\n500 \tCHECKIN_ERROR \tDocument is not checked out by you \tWrong user trying to checkin\n500 \tSUBMIT_ERROR Only draft documents can be submitted\nfor review Wrong status\n500 \tAPPROVE_ERROR Only documents in review can be\napproved Wrong status\n500 \tREJECT_ERROR Only documents in review or approved\ncan be rejected Wrong status\n500 MAKE_EFFECTIVE_E\nRROR\nOnly approved documents can be made\neffective Wrong status\n500 \tOBSOLETE_ERROR Only effective documents can be made\nobsolete Wrong status\n9. Module Integration Patterns\nPattern 1: Module Creates a Document on Behalf of a User (Most Common)\nUse Mode B (JWT + API Key). The audit trail will show the real user.\n1. User logs in to QAssure → get jwt_token\n2. User launches your module → get launch_token\n3. Module backend calls verify-launch-token → get module_jwt\n4. Module calls POST /documents with:\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n5. Document owner/created_by = real user (not your module)\nPattern 2: Module Does Background / Automated Document Operations\nUse Mode C (API Key + Tenant ID). No user context needed.\n1. Configure document:read + document:write in api_key_permissions for your API key\n2. All requests include:\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nX-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid>\n3. No user JWT needed\n4. Audit trail shows module identity (no user)\nPattern 3: Module Shows a Document Compliance Dashboard\n6. Call GET /documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=30 to get documents needing attention\n7. Call GET /documents?status=effective to list currently active documents\n8. Call GET /documents?status=draft to list documents pending submission\n9. Call GET /documents/categories to build category filter dropdowns\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 18 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPattern 4: Module Manages Full Document Authoring Workflow\n1. Create document \t→ POST /documents\n2. Checkout for editing \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkout\n3. Create new version with edits → POST /documents/:id/versions\n4. Checkin \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkin\n5. Submit for review \t→ POST /documents/:id/submit\n6. Approve (by QA) \t→ POST /documents/:id/approve\n7. Make effective (by admin) \t→ POST /documents/:id/make-effective\n8. (Later) Obsolete when superseded → POST /documents/:id/obsolete\n10. Complete Workflow Example\nA complete, annotated request/response sequence for creating and publishing a document via Combined Auth\n(Mode B).\nStep 1 — Get Categories\nGET /api/v1/documents/categories\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n→ Note the id for the SOP category (e.g., 6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5)\nStep 2 — Create Document\nPOST /api/v1/documents\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Equipment Calibration SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"description": "Procedure for equipment calibration in production areas",\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Calibration Steps",\n"department": "Engineering",\n"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",\n"tags": ["calibration", "equipment", "gmp"]\n}\n→ Status: draft, Version: 0.1, document_number: SOP-2026-0002\n→ Save the data.id as document_id\nStep 3 — Checkout for Editing\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Adding section 4 - Frequency of Calibration"\n}\n→ Response: { "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "..." }\nStep 4 — Create a New Version (Minor Edit)\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 19 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. Frequency\\n4.1 Monthly for critical\nequipment",\n"change_summary": "Added frequency section",\n"change_reason": "minor_edit"\n}\n→ Version bumped to 0.2, document status reset to draft\nStep 5 — Checkin\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\n→ Response: { "checked_in": true }\nStep 6 — Submit for Review\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\n→ Status: in_review, workflow_instance_id is now populated\nStep 7 — Approve\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"comments": "Reviewed and approved - meets regulatory standards"\n}\n→ Status: approved\nStep 8 — Make Effective\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"effective_date": "2026-03-17T00:00:00Z"\n}\n→ Status: effective\n→ next_review_date auto-calculated: 2027-03-17 (SOP category = 12 months)\nStep 9 — (Future) Obsolete When Superseded\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 20 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n"reason": "Superseded by Equipment Calibration SOP v2.0 (SOP-2026-0015)"\n}\n→ Status: obsolete, obsolete_date = NOW()\nQuick Reference Card\nAPI Meth\nod Endpoint \tPermission \tRequired Body Fields\nGet Categories \tGET \t/documents/categories \tdocument:read \t—\nGet Types \tGET \t/documents/types \tAuth only \t—\nGet Statuses \tGET \t/documents/statuses \tAuth only \t—\nDue for Review \tGET /documents/due-for-revi\new document:read \t—\nList Documents \tGET \t/documents \tdocument:read \t—\nGet Document \tGET \t/documents/:id \tdocument:read \t—\nCreate Document POST /documents \tdocument:write title, document_type\nUpdate Document PUT \t/documents/:id \tdocument:write at least one field\nGet Versions \tGET \t/documents/:id/versions document:read \t—\nCreate Version \tPOST /documents/:id/versions document:write —\nCheckout \tPOST /documents/:id/checkout document:write —\nCheckin \tPOST /documents/:id/checkin document:write —\nSubmit for Review POST /documents/:id/submit \tdocument:write {}\nApprove \tPOST /documents/:id/approve document:write —\nReject \tPOST /documents/:id/reject \tdocument:write reason (mandatory)\nMake Effective \tPOST /documents/:id/make-eff\nective document:write effective_date (mandatory)\nObsolete \tPOST /documents/:id/obsolete document:write reason (mandatory)\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 21 of 21 --	<p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>QAssure</p><p>Document Service API Integration Guide</p><p>For Module Developers</p><p>Audience \tModule Developers integrating with QAssure Document</p><p>Management Service</p><p>Base URL (Dev) \thttp://localhost:3000/api/v1</p><p>Base URL (Prod) \thttps://backendqassure.tech4bizsolutions.com/</p><p>api/v1</p><p>Last Verified \t28-Feb-2026 (all 17 endpoints verified)</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 1 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>1. What is the Document Service?</p><p>The QAssure Document Service provides a centralized, controlled document management system for</p><p>quality-regulated environments (e.g., Pharma, Manufacturing). It allows modules to:</p><p>• Create and manage controlled documents (SOPs, Policies, Forms, Work Instructions, etc.)</p><p>• Version-control document content with major/minor versioning (e.g., 0.1 → 0.2 → 1.0)</p><p>• Drive a full document lifecycle from draft → in_review → approved → effective → obsolete</p><p>• Lock documents for editing via a Checkout/Checkin mechanism (prevents concurrent edits)</p><p>• Auto-number documents by type and year (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)</p><p>• Trigger periodic review alerts based on category-defined review frequencies</p><p>• Maintain a complete audit trail with workflow history, access logs, and user attribution</p><p>2. Authentication Modes</p><p>The Document Service supports three authentication modes. Choose based on your module's use case:</p><p>Mode A — JWT Only (QAssure UI Users)</p><p>Standard user login via the QAssure UI. Best for direct user-driven operations.</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token></p><p>Mode B — JWT + API Key (Combined / Recommended for Modules)</p><p>Your module launches via SSO, obtains a module_jwt, and sends both the JWT and your module's API Key. This</p><p>is the recommended mode for user-context operations.</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>💡 Advantages of Mode B: Audit trail records the real user identity (not a service account). User's actual</p><p>role-based permissions are enforced. Module identity is tracked for source attribution. X-Tenant-ID is not</p><p>needed — tenant is derived from the JWT.</p><p>Mode C — API Key + Tenant ID (System / Cron Operations)</p><p>For background module operations with no user context (automated jobs, cron tasks).</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>X-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid></p><p>⚠ Requires document:read and document:write permissions configured in api_key_permissions table.</p><p>3. SSO / Module Launch Flow (Recommended)</p><p>Follow these 3 steps to obtain a module_jwt for Mode B (JWT + API Key):</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 2 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Step 1 — User Logs into QAssure</p><p>POST /api/v1/auth/login</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"email": "admin@yourcompany.com",</p><p>"password": "YourPassword"</p><p>}</p><p>Response: Save data.access_token as jwt_token.</p><p>Step 2 — Launch Your Module</p><p>POST /api/v1/modules/<your_module_id>/launch</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token></p><p>Response: Contains data.launch_url with a ?token=<launch_token> parameter. Extract and save the</p><p>launch_token.</p><p>Step 3 — Verify Launch Token (Exchange for Module Session JWT)</p><p>POST /api/v1/modules/verify-launch-token</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"token": "<launch_token>"</p><p>}</p><p>Response Fields:</p><p>Field \tDescription</p><p>data.token \tModule session JWT — use as Bearer token for all subsequent API calls</p><p>data.user \tFull user object (id, email, name, department, designation)</p><p>data.tenant \tTenant details (id, name, slug, company_name, logo)</p><p>data.permissions \tArray of permission strings granted to this user</p><p>data.module \tModule identity info</p><p>data.expires_in \t86400 (24 hours)</p><p>data.expires_at \tISO timestamp of expiry</p><p>Save data.token as your module_jwt. Use it with Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt> + X-API-Key:</p><p><your_api_key> for all subsequent document API calls.</p><p>4. Permissions Required</p><p>Permission \tDescription</p><p>document:read \tView documents, categories, versions, due-for-review list</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 3 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Permission \tDescription</p><p>document:write \tCreate, update, version, checkout/checkin, and all lifecycle actions</p><p>Who gets these permissions automatically:</p><p>• Tenant Admin — has both document:read and document:write (seeded)</p><p>• Super Admin — bypasses all permission checks</p><p>• Custom Roles — when a Tenant Admin grants document permissions</p><p>• API Key (Mode C) — requires explicit document:read / document:write in api_key_permissions table</p><p>• JWT + API Key (Mode B) — user's actual role-based permissions are enforced</p><p>5. API Reference</p><p>5.1 Reference Data APIs</p><p>These are the first APIs to call. They return static/seeded data your module needs to build dropdowns, filter</p><p>options, and validate inputs.</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/categories</p><p>Returns tenant-scoped document categories.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Query Parameters \tNone</p><p>Example Request (Mode B):</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/categories</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",</p><p>"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",</p><p>"code": "SOP",</p><p>"description": "SOPs for regulated operations",</p><p>"parent_id": null,</p><p>"requires_training": true,</p><p>"retention_years": 10,</p><p>"review_frequency_months": 12</p><p>},</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "...",</p><p>"name": "Forms",</p><p>"code": "FRM",</p><p>"review_frequency_months": 24</p><p>}</p><p>]</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 4 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>}</p><p>Category List (Pharma Corp tenant):</p><p>Code \tName \tReview Frequency</p><p>FRM \tForms \t24 months</p><p>POL \tPolicies \t12 months</p><p>QM \tQuality Manual \t12 months</p><p>SPEC \tSpecifications \t12 months</p><p>SOP \tStandard Operating Procedures \t12 months</p><p>WI \tWork Instructions \t24 months</p><p>💡 Developer Tip: Save category.id from this response — you will need it in category_id when creating</p><p>documents. The review_frequency_months field is used to auto-calculate next_review_date when a document</p><p>becomes effective.</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/types</p><p>Returns all available document type codes. No document:read permission required — only authentication.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tAuthenticated only</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [</p><p>{ "code": "SOP", "name": "Standard Operating Procedure" },</p><p>{ "code": "WI", "name": "Work Instruction" },</p><p>{ "code": "POL", "name": "Policy" },</p><p>{ "code": "FRM", "name": "Form" },</p><p>{ "code": "SPEC", "name": "Specification" },</p><p>{ "code": "QM", "name": "Quality Manual" },</p><p>{ "code": "PROC", "name": "Procedure" },</p><p>{ "code": "GUIDE", "name": "Guideline" },</p><p>{ "code": "REF", "name": "Reference Document" }</p><p>]</p><p>}</p><p>💡 The code value is what you pass as document_type when creating a document. The auto-number prefix is</p><p>derived from this code (e.g., SOP-2026-0001).</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/statuses</p><p>Returns all possible document lifecycle statuses. No document:read permission required.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tAuthenticated only</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 5 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [</p><p>{ "code": "draft", \t"name": "Draft", \t"description": "Document is being created or</p><p>edited" },</p><p>{ "code": "in_review", "name": "In Review", "description": "Document is under review" },</p><p>{ "code": "approved", "name": "Approved", "description": "Document has been approved" },</p><p>{ "code": "effective", "name": "Effective", "description": "Document is currently in effect"</p><p>},</p><p>{ "code": "obsolete", "name": "Obsolete", "description": "Document has been superseded" },</p><p>{ "code": "archived", "name": "Archived", "description": "Document is archived for</p><p>historical purposes" }</p><p>]</p><p>}</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review</p><p>Returns effective documents whose next_review_date falls within the specified window. Useful for building</p><p>compliance dashboards or sending review reminders.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Query Parameters:</p><p>Parameter \tType \tDefault \tDescription</p><p>days_ahead \tinteger \t30 \tNumber of days ahead to check</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=90</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>• Only returns documents with a non-null next_review_date (i.e., documents linked to a category)</p><p>• Documents without a category will never appear here (their next_review_date is null)</p><p>5.2 Document CRUD APIs</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents — Create Document</p><p>Creates a new controlled document. An initial version 0.1 is auto-created. Document number is auto-generated.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tHTTP 201 — Full 19-field document object</p><p>Request Body Fields:</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 6 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>title \tstring \tRequired \tDocument title (max 500 chars)</p><p>document_type \tstring \tRequired \tType code from GET /types (e.g., "SOP")</p><p>description \tstring \tOptional \tShort description</p><p>content \tstring \tOptional \tPlain-text document body (stored in version 0.1)</p><p>content_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of the content</p><p>department \tstring \tOptional \tOwning department name</p><p>category_id \tUUID \tOptional \tCategory UUID from GET /categories</p><p>owner_id \tUUID \tOptional \tUser UUID; defaults to the authenticated user</p><p>tags \tstring[] \tOptional \tArray of tag strings</p><p>custom_fields \tobject \tOptional \tAny additional JSONB metadata</p><p>Example Request (Mode B):</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"description": "Standard operating procedure for sterile manufacturing",</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Gowning",</p><p>"department": "Manufacturing",</p><p>"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",</p><p>"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "gowning"]</p><p>}</p><p>Example Request (Mode C — API Key only):</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>X-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Module-Created SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure"</p><p>}</p><p>Auto-behaviors:</p><p>• document_number auto-generated: <TYPE>-<YEAR>-<NNNN> (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)</p><p>• status defaults to "draft"</p><p>• Initial version 0.1 is auto-created in document_versions table</p><p>• IndexingHooks.indexDocument() is triggered for search indexing</p><p>Validation Error (HTTP 400):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "title and document_type are required" }</p><p>}</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 7 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents — List Documents</p><p>Lists documents for the tenant with pagination and filtering.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Query Parameters:</p><p>Parameter \tType \tDescription</p><p>limit \tinteger \tResults per page (default: 50)</p><p>offset \tinteger \tPagination offset (default: 0)</p><p>status \tstring \tFilter by status code (e.g., draft, effective)</p><p>category_id \tUUID \tFilter by category UUID</p><p>document_type \tstring \tFilter by type code (e.g., SOP)</p><p>owner_id \tUUID \tFilter by owner UUID</p><p>search \tstring \tFull-text ILIKE search on title, document_number, description</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents?status=effective&document_type=SOP&limit=20&offset=0</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [ /* array of Document Summary objects */ ],</p><p>"pagination": {</p><p>"total": 47,</p><p>"limit": 20,</p><p>"offset": 0</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/:id — Get Single Document</p><p>Returns full details for a single document by its UUID.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tFull 19-field document object</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 8 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>⚠ Checkout status is NOT included in this response. It is tracked separately in the document_checkouts table.</p><p>Not Found (HTTP 404):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": { "code": "NOT_FOUND", "message": "Document not found" }</p><p>}</p><p>PUT /api/v1/documents/:id — Update Document Metadata</p><p>Updates document metadata only. Content changes must go through versioning (POST /versions).</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tFull 19-field updated document object</p><p>Updatable Fields:</p><p>Field \tType \tDescription</p><p>title \tstring \tDocument title</p><p>description \tstring \tDescription</p><p>category_id \tUUID \tChange category</p><p>owner_id \tUUID \tReassign owner</p><p>department \tstring \tDepartment</p><p>tags \tstring[] \tReplace tags array</p><p>custom_fields \tobject \tReplace custom JSONB metadata</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>PUT /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP - Revised",</p><p>"department": "Quality Assurance",</p><p>"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "updated"]</p><p>}</p><p>5.3 Version Management APIs</p><p>Documents use major.minor versioning. Each new version resets the document to draft status.</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 9 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Version Type \tExample Transition \tis_major_version</p><p>Minor edit \t0.1 → 0.2 \tfalse (default)</p><p>Major revision \t0.2 → 1.0, 1.3 → 2.0 \ttrue</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — List Versions</p><p>Returns all versions for a document, ordered from newest to oldest.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tArray of 13-field version objects</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>⚠ content is NOT included in the version list response — only metadata is returned.</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — Create New Version</p><p>Creates a new version of a document. The document status is reset to draft — it must go through the review</p><p>process again.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tHTTP 201 — New 13-field version object</p><p>Request Body Fields:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>content \tstring \tOptional \tNew plain-text content body</p><p>content_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of content</p><p>change_summary \tstring \tOptional \tBrief description of what changed</p><p>change_reason \tstring \tOptional \tReason category (e.g., minor_edit, regulatory_update)</p><p>is_major_version \tboolean \tOptional \ttrue for major version bump (default: false)</p><p>file_name \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file name</p><p>file_path \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file path/URL</p><p>file_size \tinteger \tOptional \tFile size in bytes</p><p>mime_type \tstring \tOptional \tMIME type of attached file</p><p>Minor Version Example:</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 10 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. References\\nISO 14644, EU GMP Annex 1",</p><p>"change_summary": "Added references section",</p><p>"change_reason": "minor_edit"</p><p>}</p><p>Major Version Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"content": "Complete rewrite per new regulatory requirements.",</p><p>"change_summary": "Major revision per EU GMP Annex 1 update",</p><p>"change_reason": "regulatory_update",</p><p>"is_major_version": true</p><p>}</p><p>Key Behaviors:</p><p>• SHA-256 hash is auto-calculated from content for integrity verification</p><p>• Document current_version_id is updated to the new version</p><p>• Document status is reset to "draft"</p><p>5.4 Checkout / Checkin APIs</p><p>The checkout/checkin mechanism prevents concurrent editing by granting an exclusive 24-hour lock on a</p><p>document.</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkout — Checkout Document</p><p>Locks the document for exclusive editing by the current user.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>reason \tstring \tOptional \tWhy the document is being checked out</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Adding new section on environmental monitoring"</p><p>}</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 11 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Possible Responses:</p><p>Scenario \tResponse</p><p>Successful new checkout \t{ "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "<ISO timestamp +24h>" }</p><p>Same user re-checking out \t{ "already_checked_out": true, "by_current_user": true }</p><p>Different user has it checked out \tHTTP 500 — "Document is already checked out by another user"</p><p>• Checkout expires automatically after 24 hours</p><p>• Checkout status is logged in document_access_log</p><p>• Checkout status is NOT visible in the GET /documents/:id response</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkin — Checkin Document</p><p>Releases the exclusive lock. Only the user who performed the checkout can check in.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Request Body \tEmpty {} or no body required</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>Success Response: { "checked_in": true }</p><p>Error Response (wrong user): "Document is not checked out by you"</p><p>5.5 Lifecycle Workflow APIs</p><p>These endpoints drive the document through its full lifecycle. Always run them in the correct order.</p><p>💡 Lifecycle Flow: draft → [Submit] → in_review → [Approve] → approved → [Make Effective] → effective →</p><p>[Obsolete] → obsolete. OR: in_review / approved → [Reject] → draft (re-submit to restart)</p><p>All lifecycle endpoints return the full 19-field document object.</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/submit — Submit for Review</p><p>Submits a draft document for review. Starts a document_approval workflow instance.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 12 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Allowed From \tdraft status only</p><p>Request Body \tEmpty {} required</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>What happens internally:</p><p>1. Validates document is in draft status</p><p>2. Calls workflowEngine.startWorkflow({ workflowCode: 'document_approval', ... })</p><p>3. Sets document status = 'in_review'</p><p>4. Saves workflow_instance_id on the document</p><p>5. Updates current version's status to in_review</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/approve — Approve Document</p><p>Approves a document that is under review. Logs in workflow history.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \tin_review status only</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>comments \tstring \tOptional \tApproval comments</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"comments": "Reviewed and approved per QA checklist"</p><p>}</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/reject — Reject Document</p><p>Rejects a document and returns it to draft. Logs in workflow history.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \tin_review or approved status</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 13 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>reason \tstring \tRequired \tMust provide a rejection reason</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/reject</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Needs additional safety section per regulatory requirement"</p><p>}</p><p>Validation Error (missing reason):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": {</p><p>"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",</p><p>"message": "reason is required when rejecting a document"</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/make-effective — Make Effective</p><p>Marks an approved document as effective. Auto-calculates the next review date.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \tapproved status only</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>effective_date \tstring (ISO date) \tRequired \te.g., "2026-03-01" or "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"</p><p>signature_id \tUUID \tOptional \te-Signature UUID if applicable</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"effective_date": "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>Auto-calculation of next_review_date:</p><p>• If document has a category_id → next_review_date = effective_date +</p><p>category.review_frequency_months</p><p>• If no category → next_review_date = null</p><p>• Example: SOP category has 12-month review → next_review_date = effective + 12 months</p><p>⚠ Does NOT insert workflow history — this is by design in the current implementation.</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 14 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/obsolete — Make Obsolete</p><p>Marks an effective document as obsolete (superseded).</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \teffective status only</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>reason \tstring \tRequired \tWhy this document is being obsoleted</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Superseded by new revision SOP-2026-0010"</p><p>}</p><p>What happens internally:</p><p>• Sets obsolete_date = NOW()</p><p>• Inserts into workflow_history (action = 'obsolete', comments = reason) if workflow_instance_id exists</p><p>Validation Error (missing reason):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": {</p><p>"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",</p><p>"message": "reason is required when making a document obsolete"</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>6. Document Lifecycle State Machine</p><p>From Status \tAction \tTo Status \tRequired Fields</p><p>draft \tSubmit \tin_review \t—</p><p>in_review \tApprove \tapproved \tcomments (optional)</p><p>in_review \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)</p><p>approved \tMake Effective \teffective \teffective_date (required)</p><p>approved \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)</p><p>effective \tObsolete \tobsolete \treason (required)</p><p>⚠ Creating a new version (POST /versions) from any status always resets the document to draft.</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 15 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>State Flow:</p><p>draft ──[Submit]──► in_review ──[Approve]──► approved ──[Make Effective]──►</p><p>effective</p><p>▲ \t│ \t│ \t│</p><p>│ \t[Reject] \t[Reject]</p><p>[Obsolete]</p><p>└───────────────────────┘◄─────────────────────────┘ \t▼</p><p>obsolete</p><p>7. Response Schemas</p><p>Document Object (Full — 19 Fields)</p><p>Returned by: POST /documents, GET /documents/:id, PUT /documents/:id, and all lifecycle endpoints.</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",</p><p>"description": "Description text",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"category": {</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",</p><p>"code": "SOP"</p><p>},</p><p>"status": "draft",</p><p>"current_version": "0.1",</p><p>"version_status": "draft",</p><p>"owner": {</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"email": "admin@company.com",</p><p>"name": "Jane Doe"</p><p>},</p><p>"department": "Manufacturing",</p><p>"effective_date": "2026-03-01",</p><p>"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",</p><p>"tags": ["sterile", "gmp"],</p><p>"custom_fields": {},</p><p>"workflow_instance_id": "uuid or null",</p><p>"created_by": "admin@company.com",</p><p>"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z",</p><p>"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>Document Summary (10 Fields)</p><p>Returned by: GET /documents (list) and GET /documents/due-for-review.</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"category": "Standard Operating Procedures",</p><p>"status": "effective",</p><p>"current_version": "1.0",</p><p>"owner": "admin@company.com",</p><p>"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 16 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>Version Object (13 Fields)</p><p>Returned by: GET /documents/:id/versions and POST /documents/:id/versions.</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"version_number": "0.2",</p><p>"major_version": 0,</p><p>"minor_version": 2,</p><p>"status": "draft",</p><p>"file": {</p><p>"name": "document.pdf",</p><p>"path": "/uploads/document.pdf",</p><p>"size": 204800,</p><p>"mime_type": "application/pdf",</p><p>"hash": "sha256-hex-string"</p><p>},</p><p>"change_summary": "Added references section",</p><p>"change_reason": "minor_edit",</p><p>"approved_by": "approver@company.com",</p><p>"approved_at": "2026-02-28T11:00:00Z",</p><p>"signature_id": "uuid or null",</p><p>"created_by": "author@company.com",</p><p>"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:30:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>💡 file is null if no file attachment exists. content field is NOT included in the version list response.</p><p>8. Error Reference</p><p>All errors follow a consistent format:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": {</p><p>"code": "ERROR_CODE",</p><p>"message": "Human-readable message"</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>HTTP</p><p>Status Code \tMessage \tWhen</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR title and document_type are required \tCreating without required fields</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when rejecting a</p><p>document Reject without reason</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR effective_date is required \tMake Effective without date</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when making a</p><p>document obsolete Obsolete without reason</p><p>404 \tNOT_FOUND \tDocument not found Document not found or wrong</p><p>tenant</p><p>500 \tCREATE_ERROR \terror detail \tDB or internal error on create</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 17 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>HTTP</p><p>Status Code \tMessage \tWhen</p><p>500 \tCHECKOUT_ERROR Document is already checked out by</p><p>another user Concurrent checkout</p><p>500 \tCHECKIN_ERROR \tDocument is not checked out by you \tWrong user trying to checkin</p><p>500 \tSUBMIT_ERROR Only draft documents can be submitted</p><p>for review Wrong status</p><p>500 \tAPPROVE_ERROR Only documents in review can be</p><p>approved Wrong status</p><p>500 \tREJECT_ERROR Only documents in review or approved</p><p>can be rejected Wrong status</p><p>500 MAKE_EFFECTIVE_E</p><p>RROR</p><p>Only approved documents can be made</p><p>effective Wrong status</p><p>500 \tOBSOLETE_ERROR Only effective documents can be made</p><p>obsolete Wrong status</p><p>9. Module Integration Patterns</p><p>Pattern 1: Module Creates a Document on Behalf of a User (Most Common)</p><p>Use Mode B (JWT + API Key). The audit trail will show the real user.</p><p>1. User logs in to QAssure → get jwt_token</p><p>2. User launches your module → get launch_token</p><p>3. Module backend calls verify-launch-token → get module_jwt</p><p>4. Module calls POST /documents with:</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>5. Document owner/created_by = real user (not your module)</p><p>Pattern 2: Module Does Background / Automated Document Operations</p><p>Use Mode C (API Key + Tenant ID). No user context needed.</p><p>1. Configure document:read + document:write in api_key_permissions for your API key</p><p>2. All requests include:</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>X-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid></p><p>3. No user JWT needed</p><p>4. Audit trail shows module identity (no user)</p><p>Pattern 3: Module Shows a Document Compliance Dashboard</p><p>6. Call GET /documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=30 to get documents needing attention</p><p>7. Call GET /documents?status=effective to list currently active documents</p><p>8. Call GET /documents?status=draft to list documents pending submission</p><p>9. Call GET /documents/categories to build category filter dropdowns</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 18 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Pattern 4: Module Manages Full Document Authoring Workflow</p><p>1. Create document \t→ POST /documents</p><p>2. Checkout for editing \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkout</p><p>3. Create new version with edits → POST /documents/:id/versions</p><p>4. Checkin \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkin</p><p>5. Submit for review \t→ POST /documents/:id/submit</p><p>6. Approve (by QA) \t→ POST /documents/:id/approve</p><p>7. Make effective (by admin) \t→ POST /documents/:id/make-effective</p><p>8. (Later) Obsolete when superseded → POST /documents/:id/obsolete</p><p>10. Complete Workflow Example</p><p>A complete, annotated request/response sequence for creating and publishing a document via Combined Auth</p><p>(Mode B).</p><p>Step 1 — Get Categories</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/categories</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>→ Note the id for the SOP category (e.g., 6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5)</p><p>Step 2 — Create Document</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Equipment Calibration SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"description": "Procedure for equipment calibration in production areas",</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Calibration Steps",</p><p>"department": "Engineering",</p><p>"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",</p><p>"tags": ["calibration", "equipment", "gmp"]</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: draft, Version: 0.1, document_number: SOP-2026-0002</p><p>→ Save the data.id as document_id</p><p>Step 3 — Checkout for Editing</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Adding section 4 - Frequency of Calibration"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Response: { "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "..." }</p><p>Step 4 — Create a New Version (Minor Edit)</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 19 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. Frequency\\n4.1 Monthly for critical</p><p>equipment",</p><p>"change_summary": "Added frequency section",</p><p>"change_reason": "minor_edit"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Version bumped to 0.2, document status reset to draft</p><p>Step 5 — Checkin</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>→ Response: { "checked_in": true }</p><p>Step 6 — Submit for Review</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>→ Status: in_review, workflow_instance_id is now populated</p><p>Step 7 — Approve</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"comments": "Reviewed and approved - meets regulatory standards"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: approved</p><p>Step 8 — Make Effective</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"effective_date": "2026-03-17T00:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: effective</p><p>→ next_review_date auto-calculated: 2027-03-17 (SOP category = 12 months)</p><p>Step 9 — (Future) Obsolete When Superseded</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 20 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>"reason": "Superseded by Equipment Calibration SOP v2.0 (SOP-2026-0015)"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: obsolete, obsolete_date = NOW()</p><p>Quick Reference Card</p><p>API Meth</p><p>od Endpoint \tPermission \tRequired Body Fields</p><p>Get Categories \tGET \t/documents/categories \tdocument:read \t—</p><p>Get Types \tGET \t/documents/types \tAuth only \t—</p><p>Get Statuses \tGET \t/documents/statuses \tAuth only \t—</p><p>Due for Review \tGET /documents/due-for-revi</p><p>ew document:read \t—</p><p>List Documents \tGET \t/documents \tdocument:read \t—</p><p>Get Document \tGET \t/documents/:id \tdocument:read \t—</p><p>Create Document POST /documents \tdocument:write title, document_type</p><p>Update Document PUT \t/documents/:id \tdocument:write at least one field</p><p>Get Versions \tGET \t/documents/:id/versions document:read \t—</p><p>Create Version \tPOST /documents/:id/versions document:write —</p><p>Checkout \tPOST /documents/:id/checkout document:write —</p><p>Checkin \tPOST /documents/:id/checkin document:write —</p><p>Submit for Review POST /documents/:id/submit \tdocument:write {}</p><p>Approve \tPOST /documents/:id/approve document:write —</p><p>Reject \tPOST /documents/:id/reject \tdocument:write reason (mandatory)</p><p>Make Effective \tPOST /documents/:id/make-eff</p><p>ective document:write effective_date (mandatory)</p><p>Obsolete \tPOST /documents/:id/obsolete document:write reason (mandatory)</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 21 of 21 --</p>	Initial draft	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	4ccf68ad-485c-495a-935b-10d74b173a52	2026-03-27 14:03:04.092055+00	platform	\N
89bfad8c-fcf2-4f3b-9867-066fa1cea592	7db1ab09-d54d-4368-97a6-7da076d541f1	352d7e21-5155-4ff8-8169-284bf5ece3e7	0.1	0	1	in_review	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nQAssure\nDocument Service API Integration Guide\nFor Module Developers\nAudience \tModule Developers integrating with QAssure Document\nManagement Service\nBase URL (Dev) \thttp://localhost:3000/api/v1\nBase URL (Prod) \thttps://backendqassure.tech4bizsolutions.com/\napi/v1\nLast Verified \t28-Feb-2026 (all 17 endpoints verified)\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 1 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n1. What is the Document Service?\nThe QAssure Document Service provides a centralized, controlled document management system for\nquality-regulated environments (e.g., Pharma, Manufacturing). It allows modules to:\n• Create and manage controlled documents (SOPs, Policies, Forms, Work Instructions, etc.)\n• Version-control document content with major/minor versioning (e.g., 0.1 → 0.2 → 1.0)\n• Drive a full document lifecycle from draft → in_review → approved → effective → obsolete\n• Lock documents for editing via a Checkout/Checkin mechanism (prevents concurrent edits)\n• Auto-number documents by type and year (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)\n• Trigger periodic review alerts based on category-defined review frequencies\n• Maintain a complete audit trail with workflow history, access logs, and user attribution\n2. Authentication Modes\nThe Document Service supports three authentication modes. Choose based on your module's use case:\nMode A — JWT Only (QAssure UI Users)\nStandard user login via the QAssure UI. Best for direct user-driven operations.\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt_token>\nMode B — JWT + API Key (Combined / Recommended for Modules)\nYour module launches via SSO, obtains a module_jwt, and sends both the JWT and your module's API Key. This\nis the recommended mode for user-context operations.\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\n💡 Advantages of Mode B: Audit trail records the real user identity (not a service account). User's actual\nrole-based permissions are enforced. Module identity is tracked for source attribution. X-Tenant-ID is not\nneeded — tenant is derived from the JWT.\nMode C — API Key + Tenant ID (System / Cron Operations)\nFor background module operations with no user context (automated jobs, cron tasks).\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\nX-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid>\n⚠ Requires document:read and document:write permissions configured in api_key_permissions table.\n3. SSO / Module Launch Flow (Recommended)\nFollow these 3 steps to obtain a module_jwt for Mode B (JWT + API Key):\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 2 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nStep 1 — User Logs into QAssure\nPOST /api/v1/auth/login\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"email": "admin@yourcompany.com",\n"password": "YourPassword"\n}\nResponse: Save data.access_token as jwt_token.\nStep 2 — Launch Your Module\nPOST /api/v1/modules/<your_module_id>/launch\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt_token>\nResponse: Contains data.launch_url with a ?token=<launch_token> parameter. Extract and save the\nlaunch_token.\nStep 3 — Verify Launch Token (Exchange for Module Session JWT)\nPOST /api/v1/modules/verify-launch-token\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"token": "<launch_token>"\n}\nResponse Fields:\nField \tDescription\ndata.token \tModule session JWT — use as Bearer token for all subsequent API calls\ndata.user \tFull user object (id, email, name, department, designation)\ndata.tenant \tTenant details (id, name, slug, company_name, logo)\ndata.permissions \tArray of permission strings granted to this user\ndata.module \tModule identity info\ndata.expires_in \t86400 (24 hours)\ndata.expires_at \tISO timestamp of expiry\nSave data.token as your module_jwt. Use it with Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt> + X-API-Key:\n<your_api_key> for all subsequent document API calls.\n4. Permissions Required\nPermission \tDescription\ndocument:read \tView documents, categories, versions, due-for-review list\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 3 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPermission \tDescription\ndocument:write \tCreate, update, version, checkout/checkin, and all lifecycle actions\nWho gets these permissions automatically:\n• Tenant Admin — has both document:read and document:write (seeded)\n• Super Admin — bypasses all permission checks\n• Custom Roles — when a Tenant Admin grants document permissions\n• API Key (Mode C) — requires explicit document:read / document:write in api_key_permissions table\n• JWT + API Key (Mode B) — user's actual role-based permissions are enforced\n5. API Reference\n5.1 Reference Data APIs\nThese are the first APIs to call. They return static/seeded data your module needs to build dropdowns, filter\noptions, and validate inputs.\nGET /api/v1/documents/categories\nReturns tenant-scoped document categories.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nQuery Parameters \tNone\nExample Request (Mode B):\nGET /api/v1/documents/categories\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [\n{\n"id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",\n"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",\n"code": "SOP",\n"description": "SOPs for regulated operations",\n"parent_id": null,\n"requires_training": true,\n"retention_years": 10,\n"review_frequency_months": 12\n},\n{\n"id": "...",\n"name": "Forms",\n"code": "FRM",\n"review_frequency_months": 24\n}\n]\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 4 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n}\nCategory List (Pharma Corp tenant):\nCode \tName \tReview Frequency\nFRM \tForms \t24 months\nPOL \tPolicies \t12 months\nQM \tQuality Manual \t12 months\nSPEC \tSpecifications \t12 months\nSOP \tStandard Operating Procedures \t12 months\nWI \tWork Instructions \t24 months\n💡 Developer Tip: Save category.id from this response — you will need it in category_id when creating\ndocuments. The review_frequency_months field is used to auto-calculate next_review_date when a document\nbecomes effective.\nGET /api/v1/documents/types\nReturns all available document type codes. No document:read permission required — only authentication.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tAuthenticated only\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [\n{ "code": "SOP", "name": "Standard Operating Procedure" },\n{ "code": "WI", "name": "Work Instruction" },\n{ "code": "POL", "name": "Policy" },\n{ "code": "FRM", "name": "Form" },\n{ "code": "SPEC", "name": "Specification" },\n{ "code": "QM", "name": "Quality Manual" },\n{ "code": "PROC", "name": "Procedure" },\n{ "code": "GUIDE", "name": "Guideline" },\n{ "code": "REF", "name": "Reference Document" }\n]\n}\n💡 The code value is what you pass as document_type when creating a document. The auto-number prefix is\nderived from this code (e.g., SOP-2026-0001).\nGET /api/v1/documents/statuses\nReturns all possible document lifecycle statuses. No document:read permission required.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tAuthenticated only\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 5 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [\n{ "code": "draft", \t"name": "Draft", \t"description": "Document is being created or\nedited" },\n{ "code": "in_review", "name": "In Review", "description": "Document is under review" },\n{ "code": "approved", "name": "Approved", "description": "Document has been approved" },\n{ "code": "effective", "name": "Effective", "description": "Document is currently in effect"\n},\n{ "code": "obsolete", "name": "Obsolete", "description": "Document has been superseded" },\n{ "code": "archived", "name": "Archived", "description": "Document is archived for\nhistorical purposes" }\n]\n}\nGET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review\nReturns effective documents whose next_review_date falls within the specified window. Useful for building\ncompliance dashboards or sending review reminders.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nQuery Parameters:\nParameter \tType \tDefault \tDescription\ndays_ahead \tinteger \t30 \tNumber of days ahead to check\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=90\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n• Only returns documents with a non-null next_review_date (i.e., documents linked to a category)\n• Documents without a category will never appear here (their next_review_date is null)\n5.2 Document CRUD APIs\nPOST /api/v1/documents — Create Document\nCreates a new controlled document. An initial version 0.1 is auto-created. Document number is auto-generated.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tHTTP 201 — Full 19-field document object\nRequest Body Fields:\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 6 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\ntitle \tstring \tRequired \tDocument title (max 500 chars)\ndocument_type \tstring \tRequired \tType code from GET /types (e.g., "SOP")\ndescription \tstring \tOptional \tShort description\ncontent \tstring \tOptional \tPlain-text document body (stored in version 0.1)\ncontent_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of the content\ndepartment \tstring \tOptional \tOwning department name\ncategory_id \tUUID \tOptional \tCategory UUID from GET /categories\nowner_id \tUUID \tOptional \tUser UUID; defaults to the authenticated user\ntags \tstring[] \tOptional \tArray of tag strings\ncustom_fields \tobject \tOptional \tAny additional JSONB metadata\nExample Request (Mode B):\nPOST /api/v1/documents\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"description": "Standard operating procedure for sterile manufacturing",\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Gowning",\n"department": "Manufacturing",\n"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",\n"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "gowning"]\n}\nExample Request (Mode C — API Key only):\nPOST /api/v1/documents\nX-API-Key: <your_module_api_key>\nX-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Module-Created SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure"\n}\nAuto-behaviors:\n• document_number auto-generated: <TYPE>-<YEAR>-<NNNN> (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)\n• status defaults to "draft"\n• Initial version 0.1 is auto-created in document_versions table\n• IndexingHooks.indexDocument() is triggered for search indexing\nValidation Error (HTTP 400):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "title and document_type are required" }\n}\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 7 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nGET /api/v1/documents — List Documents\nLists documents for the tenant with pagination and filtering.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nQuery Parameters:\nParameter \tType \tDescription\nlimit \tinteger \tResults per page (default: 50)\noffset \tinteger \tPagination offset (default: 0)\nstatus \tstring \tFilter by status code (e.g., draft, effective)\ncategory_id \tUUID \tFilter by category UUID\ndocument_type \tstring \tFilter by type code (e.g., SOP)\nowner_id \tUUID \tFilter by owner UUID\nsearch \tstring \tFull-text ILIKE search on title, document_number, description\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents?status=effective&document_type=SOP&limit=20&offset=0\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nExample Response:\n{\n"success": true,\n"data": [ /* array of Document Summary objects */ ],\n"pagination": {\n"total": 47,\n"limit": 20,\n"offset": 0\n}\n}\nGET /api/v1/documents/:id — Get Single Document\nReturns full details for a single document by its UUID.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tFull 19-field document object\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 8 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n⚠ Checkout status is NOT included in this response. It is tracked separately in the document_checkouts table.\nNot Found (HTTP 404):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": { "code": "NOT_FOUND", "message": "Document not found" }\n}\nPUT /api/v1/documents/:id — Update Document Metadata\nUpdates document metadata only. Content changes must go through versioning (POST /versions).\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tFull 19-field updated document object\nUpdatable Fields:\nField \tType \tDescription\ntitle \tstring \tDocument title\ndescription \tstring \tDescription\ncategory_id \tUUID \tChange category\nowner_id \tUUID \tReassign owner\ndepartment \tstring \tDepartment\ntags \tstring[] \tReplace tags array\ncustom_fields \tobject \tReplace custom JSONB metadata\nExample Request:\nPUT /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP - Revised",\n"department": "Quality Assurance",\n"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "updated"]\n}\n5.3 Version Management APIs\nDocuments use major.minor versioning. Each new version resets the document to draft status.\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 9 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nVersion Type \tExample Transition \tis_major_version\nMinor edit \t0.1 → 0.2 \tfalse (default)\nMajor revision \t0.2 → 1.0, 1.3 → 2.0 \ttrue\nGET /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — List Versions\nReturns all versions for a document, ordered from newest to oldest.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:read\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tArray of 13-field version objects\nExample Request:\nGET /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n⚠ content is NOT included in the version list response — only metadata is returned.\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — Create New Version\nCreates a new version of a document. The document status is reset to draft — it must go through the review\nprocess again.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nResponse \tHTTP 201 — New 13-field version object\nRequest Body Fields:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\ncontent \tstring \tOptional \tNew plain-text content body\ncontent_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of content\nchange_summary \tstring \tOptional \tBrief description of what changed\nchange_reason \tstring \tOptional \tReason category (e.g., minor_edit, regulatory_update)\nis_major_version \tboolean \tOptional \ttrue for major version bump (default: false)\nfile_name \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file name\nfile_path \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file path/URL\nfile_size \tinteger \tOptional \tFile size in bytes\nmime_type \tstring \tOptional \tMIME type of attached file\nMinor Version Example:\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 10 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. References\\nISO 14644, EU GMP Annex 1",\n"change_summary": "Added references section",\n"change_reason": "minor_edit"\n}\nMajor Version Example:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"content": "Complete rewrite per new regulatory requirements.",\n"change_summary": "Major revision per EU GMP Annex 1 update",\n"change_reason": "regulatory_update",\n"is_major_version": true\n}\nKey Behaviors:\n• SHA-256 hash is auto-calculated from content for integrity verification\n• Document current_version_id is updated to the new version\n• Document status is reset to "draft"\n5.4 Checkout / Checkin APIs\nThe checkout/checkin mechanism prevents concurrent editing by granting an exclusive 24-hour lock on a\ndocument.\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkout — Checkout Document\nLocks the document for exclusive editing by the current user.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\nreason \tstring \tOptional \tWhy the document is being checked out\nExample Request:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Adding new section on environmental monitoring"\n}\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 11 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPossible Responses:\nScenario \tResponse\nSuccessful new checkout \t{ "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "<ISO timestamp +24h>" }\nSame user re-checking out \t{ "already_checked_out": true, "by_current_user": true }\nDifferent user has it checked out \tHTTP 500 — "Document is already checked out by another user"\n• Checkout expires automatically after 24 hours\n• Checkout status is logged in document_access_log\n• Checkout status is NOT visible in the GET /documents/:id response\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkin — Checkin Document\nReleases the exclusive lock. Only the user who performed the checkout can check in.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAuth Modes \tA, B, C\nRequest Body \tEmpty {} or no body required\nExample Request:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\nSuccess Response: { "checked_in": true }\nError Response (wrong user): "Document is not checked out by you"\n5.5 Lifecycle Workflow APIs\nThese endpoints drive the document through its full lifecycle. Always run them in the correct order.\n💡 Lifecycle Flow: draft → [Submit] → in_review → [Approve] → approved → [Make Effective] → effective →\n[Obsolete] → obsolete. OR: in_review / approved → [Reject] → draft (re-submit to restart)\nAll lifecycle endpoints return the full 19-field document object.\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/submit — Submit for Review\nSubmits a draft document for review. Starts a document_approval workflow instance.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 12 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nAttribute \tValue\nAllowed From \tdraft status only\nRequest Body \tEmpty {} required\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\nWhat happens internally:\n1. Validates document is in draft status\n2. Calls workflowEngine.startWorkflow({ workflowCode: 'document_approval', ... })\n3. Sets document status = 'in_review'\n4. Saves workflow_instance_id on the document\n5. Updates current version's status to in_review\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/approve — Approve Document\nApproves a document that is under review. Logs in workflow history.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \tin_review status only\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\ncomments \tstring \tOptional \tApproval comments\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"comments": "Reviewed and approved per QA checklist"\n}\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/reject — Reject Document\nRejects a document and returns it to draft. Logs in workflow history.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \tin_review or approved status\nRequest Body:\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 13 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\nreason \tstring \tRequired \tMust provide a rejection reason\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/reject\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Needs additional safety section per regulatory requirement"\n}\nValidation Error (missing reason):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": {\n"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",\n"message": "reason is required when rejecting a document"\n}\n}\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/make-effective — Make Effective\nMarks an approved document as effective. Auto-calculates the next review date.\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \tapproved status only\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\neffective_date \tstring (ISO date) \tRequired \te.g., "2026-03-01" or "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"\nsignature_id \tUUID \tOptional \te-Signature UUID if applicable\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"effective_date": "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"\n}\nAuto-calculation of next_review_date:\n• If document has a category_id → next_review_date = effective_date +\ncategory.review_frequency_months\n• If no category → next_review_date = null\n• Example: SOP category has 12-month review → next_review_date = effective + 12 months\n⚠ Does NOT insert workflow history — this is by design in the current implementation.\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 14 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPOST /api/v1/documents/:id/obsolete — Make Obsolete\nMarks an effective document as obsolete (superseded).\nAttribute \tValue\nPermissions \tdocument:write\nAllowed From \teffective status only\nRequest Body:\nField \tType \tRequired \tDescription\nreason \tstring \tRequired \tWhy this document is being obsoleted\nExample:\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Superseded by new revision SOP-2026-0010"\n}\nWhat happens internally:\n• Sets obsolete_date = NOW()\n• Inserts into workflow_history (action = 'obsolete', comments = reason) if workflow_instance_id exists\nValidation Error (missing reason):\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": {\n"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",\n"message": "reason is required when making a document obsolete"\n}\n}\n6. Document Lifecycle State Machine\nFrom Status \tAction \tTo Status \tRequired Fields\ndraft \tSubmit \tin_review \t—\nin_review \tApprove \tapproved \tcomments (optional)\nin_review \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)\napproved \tMake Effective \teffective \teffective_date (required)\napproved \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)\neffective \tObsolete \tobsolete \treason (required)\n⚠ Creating a new version (POST /versions) from any status always resets the document to draft.\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 15 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nState Flow:\ndraft ──[Submit]──► in_review ──[Approve]──► approved ──[Make Effective]──►\neffective\n▲ \t│ \t│ \t│\n│ \t[Reject] \t[Reject]\n[Obsolete]\n└───────────────────────┘◄─────────────────────────┘ \t▼\nobsolete\n7. Response Schemas\nDocument Object (Full — 19 Fields)\nReturned by: POST /documents, GET /documents/:id, PUT /documents/:id, and all lifecycle endpoints.\n{\n"id": "uuid",\n"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",\n"description": "Description text",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"category": {\n"id": "uuid",\n"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",\n"code": "SOP"\n},\n"status": "draft",\n"current_version": "0.1",\n"version_status": "draft",\n"owner": {\n"id": "uuid",\n"email": "admin@company.com",\n"name": "Jane Doe"\n},\n"department": "Manufacturing",\n"effective_date": "2026-03-01",\n"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",\n"tags": ["sterile", "gmp"],\n"custom_fields": {},\n"workflow_instance_id": "uuid or null",\n"created_by": "admin@company.com",\n"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z",\n"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"\n}\nDocument Summary (10 Fields)\nReturned by: GET /documents (list) and GET /documents/due-for-review.\n{\n"id": "uuid",\n"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",\n"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"category": "Standard Operating Procedures",\n"status": "effective",\n"current_version": "1.0",\n"owner": "admin@company.com",\n"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 16 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"\n}\nVersion Object (13 Fields)\nReturned by: GET /documents/:id/versions and POST /documents/:id/versions.\n{\n"id": "uuid",\n"version_number": "0.2",\n"major_version": 0,\n"minor_version": 2,\n"status": "draft",\n"file": {\n"name": "document.pdf",\n"path": "/uploads/document.pdf",\n"size": 204800,\n"mime_type": "application/pdf",\n"hash": "sha256-hex-string"\n},\n"change_summary": "Added references section",\n"change_reason": "minor_edit",\n"approved_by": "approver@company.com",\n"approved_at": "2026-02-28T11:00:00Z",\n"signature_id": "uuid or null",\n"created_by": "author@company.com",\n"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:30:00Z"\n}\n💡 file is null if no file attachment exists. content field is NOT included in the version list response.\n8. Error Reference\nAll errors follow a consistent format:\n{\n"success": false,\n"error": {\n"code": "ERROR_CODE",\n"message": "Human-readable message"\n}\n}\nHTTP\nStatus Code \tMessage \tWhen\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR title and document_type are required \tCreating without required fields\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when rejecting a\ndocument Reject without reason\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR effective_date is required \tMake Effective without date\n400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when making a\ndocument obsolete Obsolete without reason\n404 \tNOT_FOUND \tDocument not found Document not found or wrong\ntenant\n500 \tCREATE_ERROR \terror detail \tDB or internal error on create\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 17 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nHTTP\nStatus Code \tMessage \tWhen\n500 \tCHECKOUT_ERROR Document is already checked out by\nanother user Concurrent checkout\n500 \tCHECKIN_ERROR \tDocument is not checked out by you \tWrong user trying to checkin\n500 \tSUBMIT_ERROR Only draft documents can be submitted\nfor review Wrong status\n500 \tAPPROVE_ERROR Only documents in review can be\napproved Wrong status\n500 \tREJECT_ERROR Only documents in review or approved\ncan be rejected Wrong status\n500 MAKE_EFFECTIVE_E\nRROR\nOnly approved documents can be made\neffective Wrong status\n500 \tOBSOLETE_ERROR Only effective documents can be made\nobsolete Wrong status\n9. Module Integration Patterns\nPattern 1: Module Creates a Document on Behalf of a User (Most Common)\nUse Mode B (JWT + API Key). The audit trail will show the real user.\n1. User logs in to QAssure → get jwt_token\n2. User launches your module → get launch_token\n3. Module backend calls verify-launch-token → get module_jwt\n4. Module calls POST /documents with:\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n5. Document owner/created_by = real user (not your module)\nPattern 2: Module Does Background / Automated Document Operations\nUse Mode C (API Key + Tenant ID). No user context needed.\n1. Configure document:read + document:write in api_key_permissions for your API key\n2. All requests include:\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nX-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid>\n3. No user JWT needed\n4. Audit trail shows module identity (no user)\nPattern 3: Module Shows a Document Compliance Dashboard\n6. Call GET /documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=30 to get documents needing attention\n7. Call GET /documents?status=effective to list currently active documents\n8. Call GET /documents?status=draft to list documents pending submission\n9. Call GET /documents/categories to build category filter dropdowns\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 18 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPattern 4: Module Manages Full Document Authoring Workflow\n1. Create document \t→ POST /documents\n2. Checkout for editing \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkout\n3. Create new version with edits → POST /documents/:id/versions\n4. Checkin \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkin\n5. Submit for review \t→ POST /documents/:id/submit\n6. Approve (by QA) \t→ POST /documents/:id/approve\n7. Make effective (by admin) \t→ POST /documents/:id/make-effective\n8. (Later) Obsolete when superseded → POST /documents/:id/obsolete\n10. Complete Workflow Example\nA complete, annotated request/response sequence for creating and publishing a document via Combined Auth\n(Mode B).\nStep 1 — Get Categories\nGET /api/v1/documents/categories\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\n→ Note the id for the SOP category (e.g., 6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5)\nStep 2 — Create Document\nPOST /api/v1/documents\nAuthorization: Bearer <module_jwt>\nX-API-Key: <your_api_key>\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"title": "Equipment Calibration SOP",\n"document_type": "SOP",\n"description": "Procedure for equipment calibration in production areas",\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Calibration Steps",\n"department": "Engineering",\n"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",\n"tags": ["calibration", "equipment", "gmp"]\n}\n→ Status: draft, Version: 0.1, document_number: SOP-2026-0002\n→ Save the data.id as document_id\nStep 3 — Checkout for Editing\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"reason": "Adding section 4 - Frequency of Calibration"\n}\n→ Response: { "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "..." }\nStep 4 — Create a New Version (Minor Edit)\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 19 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. Frequency\\n4.1 Monthly for critical\nequipment",\n"change_summary": "Added frequency section",\n"change_reason": "minor_edit"\n}\n→ Version bumped to 0.2, document status reset to draft\nStep 5 — Checkin\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\n→ Response: { "checked_in": true }\nStep 6 — Submit for Review\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit\nContent-Type: application/json\n{}\n→ Status: in_review, workflow_instance_id is now populated\nStep 7 — Approve\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"comments": "Reviewed and approved - meets regulatory standards"\n}\n→ Status: approved\nStep 8 — Make Effective\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\n"effective_date": "2026-03-17T00:00:00Z"\n}\n→ Status: effective\n→ next_review_date auto-calculated: 2027-03-17 (SOP category = 12 months)\nStep 9 — (Future) Obsolete When Superseded\nPOST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete\nContent-Type: application/json\n{\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 20 of 21 --\n\nQAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026\n"reason": "Superseded by Equipment Calibration SOP v2.0 (SOP-2026-0015)"\n}\n→ Status: obsolete, obsolete_date = NOW()\nQuick Reference Card\nAPI Meth\nod Endpoint \tPermission \tRequired Body Fields\nGet Categories \tGET \t/documents/categories \tdocument:read \t—\nGet Types \tGET \t/documents/types \tAuth only \t—\nGet Statuses \tGET \t/documents/statuses \tAuth only \t—\nDue for Review \tGET /documents/due-for-revi\new document:read \t—\nList Documents \tGET \t/documents \tdocument:read \t—\nGet Document \tGET \t/documents/:id \tdocument:read \t—\nCreate Document POST /documents \tdocument:write title, document_type\nUpdate Document PUT \t/documents/:id \tdocument:write at least one field\nGet Versions \tGET \t/documents/:id/versions document:read \t—\nCreate Version \tPOST /documents/:id/versions document:write —\nCheckout \tPOST /documents/:id/checkout document:write —\nCheckin \tPOST /documents/:id/checkin document:write —\nSubmit for Review POST /documents/:id/submit \tdocument:write {}\nApprove \tPOST /documents/:id/approve document:write —\nReject \tPOST /documents/:id/reject \tdocument:write reason (mandatory)\nMake Effective \tPOST /documents/:id/make-eff\nective document:write effective_date (mandatory)\nObsolete \tPOST /documents/:id/obsolete document:write reason (mandatory)\nConfidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage\n\n-- 21 of 21 --	<p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>QAssure</p><p>Document Service API Integration Guide</p><p>For Module Developers</p><p>Audience \tModule Developers integrating with QAssure Document</p><p>Management Service</p><p>Base URL (Dev) \thttp://localhost:3000/api/v1</p><p>Base URL (Prod) \thttps://backendqassure.tech4bizsolutions.com/</p><p>api/v1</p><p>Last Verified \t28-Feb-2026 (all 17 endpoints verified)</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 1 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>1. What is the Document Service?</p><p>The QAssure Document Service provides a centralized, controlled document management system for</p><p>quality-regulated environments (e.g., Pharma, Manufacturing). It allows modules to:</p><p>• Create and manage controlled documents (SOPs, Policies, Forms, Work Instructions, etc.)</p><p>• Version-control document content with major/minor versioning (e.g., 0.1 → 0.2 → 1.0)</p><p>• Drive a full document lifecycle from draft → in_review → approved → effective → obsolete</p><p>• Lock documents for editing via a Checkout/Checkin mechanism (prevents concurrent edits)</p><p>• Auto-number documents by type and year (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)</p><p>• Trigger periodic review alerts based on category-defined review frequencies</p><p>• Maintain a complete audit trail with workflow history, access logs, and user attribution</p><p>2. Authentication Modes</p><p>The Document Service supports three authentication modes. Choose based on your module's use case:</p><p>Mode A — JWT Only (QAssure UI Users)</p><p>Standard user login via the QAssure UI. Best for direct user-driven operations.</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token></p><p>Mode B — JWT + API Key (Combined / Recommended for Modules)</p><p>Your module launches via SSO, obtains a module_jwt, and sends both the JWT and your module's API Key. This</p><p>is the recommended mode for user-context operations.</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>💡 Advantages of Mode B: Audit trail records the real user identity (not a service account). User's actual</p><p>role-based permissions are enforced. Module identity is tracked for source attribution. X-Tenant-ID is not</p><p>needed — tenant is derived from the JWT.</p><p>Mode C — API Key + Tenant ID (System / Cron Operations)</p><p>For background module operations with no user context (automated jobs, cron tasks).</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>X-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid></p><p>⚠ Requires document:read and document:write permissions configured in api_key_permissions table.</p><p>3. SSO / Module Launch Flow (Recommended)</p><p>Follow these 3 steps to obtain a module_jwt for Mode B (JWT + API Key):</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 2 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Step 1 — User Logs into QAssure</p><p>POST /api/v1/auth/login</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"email": "admin@yourcompany.com",</p><p>"password": "YourPassword"</p><p>}</p><p>Response: Save data.access_token as jwt_token.</p><p>Step 2 — Launch Your Module</p><p>POST /api/v1/modules/<your_module_id>/launch</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token></p><p>Response: Contains data.launch_url with a ?token=<launch_token> parameter. Extract and save the</p><p>launch_token.</p><p>Step 3 — Verify Launch Token (Exchange for Module Session JWT)</p><p>POST /api/v1/modules/verify-launch-token</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"token": "<launch_token>"</p><p>}</p><p>Response Fields:</p><p>Field \tDescription</p><p>data.token \tModule session JWT — use as Bearer token for all subsequent API calls</p><p>data.user \tFull user object (id, email, name, department, designation)</p><p>data.tenant \tTenant details (id, name, slug, company_name, logo)</p><p>data.permissions \tArray of permission strings granted to this user</p><p>data.module \tModule identity info</p><p>data.expires_in \t86400 (24 hours)</p><p>data.expires_at \tISO timestamp of expiry</p><p>Save data.token as your module_jwt. Use it with Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt> + X-API-Key:</p><p><your_api_key> for all subsequent document API calls.</p><p>4. Permissions Required</p><p>Permission \tDescription</p><p>document:read \tView documents, categories, versions, due-for-review list</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 3 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Permission \tDescription</p><p>document:write \tCreate, update, version, checkout/checkin, and all lifecycle actions</p><p>Who gets these permissions automatically:</p><p>• Tenant Admin — has both document:read and document:write (seeded)</p><p>• Super Admin — bypasses all permission checks</p><p>• Custom Roles — when a Tenant Admin grants document permissions</p><p>• API Key (Mode C) — requires explicit document:read / document:write in api_key_permissions table</p><p>• JWT + API Key (Mode B) — user's actual role-based permissions are enforced</p><p>5. API Reference</p><p>5.1 Reference Data APIs</p><p>These are the first APIs to call. They return static/seeded data your module needs to build dropdowns, filter</p><p>options, and validate inputs.</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/categories</p><p>Returns tenant-scoped document categories.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Query Parameters \tNone</p><p>Example Request (Mode B):</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/categories</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",</p><p>"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",</p><p>"code": "SOP",</p><p>"description": "SOPs for regulated operations",</p><p>"parent_id": null,</p><p>"requires_training": true,</p><p>"retention_years": 10,</p><p>"review_frequency_months": 12</p><p>},</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "...",</p><p>"name": "Forms",</p><p>"code": "FRM",</p><p>"review_frequency_months": 24</p><p>}</p><p>]</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 4 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>}</p><p>Category List (Pharma Corp tenant):</p><p>Code \tName \tReview Frequency</p><p>FRM \tForms \t24 months</p><p>POL \tPolicies \t12 months</p><p>QM \tQuality Manual \t12 months</p><p>SPEC \tSpecifications \t12 months</p><p>SOP \tStandard Operating Procedures \t12 months</p><p>WI \tWork Instructions \t24 months</p><p>💡 Developer Tip: Save category.id from this response — you will need it in category_id when creating</p><p>documents. The review_frequency_months field is used to auto-calculate next_review_date when a document</p><p>becomes effective.</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/types</p><p>Returns all available document type codes. No document:read permission required — only authentication.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tAuthenticated only</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [</p><p>{ "code": "SOP", "name": "Standard Operating Procedure" },</p><p>{ "code": "WI", "name": "Work Instruction" },</p><p>{ "code": "POL", "name": "Policy" },</p><p>{ "code": "FRM", "name": "Form" },</p><p>{ "code": "SPEC", "name": "Specification" },</p><p>{ "code": "QM", "name": "Quality Manual" },</p><p>{ "code": "PROC", "name": "Procedure" },</p><p>{ "code": "GUIDE", "name": "Guideline" },</p><p>{ "code": "REF", "name": "Reference Document" }</p><p>]</p><p>}</p><p>💡 The code value is what you pass as document_type when creating a document. The auto-number prefix is</p><p>derived from this code (e.g., SOP-2026-0001).</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/statuses</p><p>Returns all possible document lifecycle statuses. No document:read permission required.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tAuthenticated only</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 5 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [</p><p>{ "code": "draft", \t"name": "Draft", \t"description": "Document is being created or</p><p>edited" },</p><p>{ "code": "in_review", "name": "In Review", "description": "Document is under review" },</p><p>{ "code": "approved", "name": "Approved", "description": "Document has been approved" },</p><p>{ "code": "effective", "name": "Effective", "description": "Document is currently in effect"</p><p>},</p><p>{ "code": "obsolete", "name": "Obsolete", "description": "Document has been superseded" },</p><p>{ "code": "archived", "name": "Archived", "description": "Document is archived for</p><p>historical purposes" }</p><p>]</p><p>}</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review</p><p>Returns effective documents whose next_review_date falls within the specified window. Useful for building</p><p>compliance dashboards or sending review reminders.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Query Parameters:</p><p>Parameter \tType \tDefault \tDescription</p><p>days_ahead \tinteger \t30 \tNumber of days ahead to check</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=90</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>• Only returns documents with a non-null next_review_date (i.e., documents linked to a category)</p><p>• Documents without a category will never appear here (their next_review_date is null)</p><p>5.2 Document CRUD APIs</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents — Create Document</p><p>Creates a new controlled document. An initial version 0.1 is auto-created. Document number is auto-generated.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tHTTP 201 — Full 19-field document object</p><p>Request Body Fields:</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 6 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>title \tstring \tRequired \tDocument title (max 500 chars)</p><p>document_type \tstring \tRequired \tType code from GET /types (e.g., "SOP")</p><p>description \tstring \tOptional \tShort description</p><p>content \tstring \tOptional \tPlain-text document body (stored in version 0.1)</p><p>content_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of the content</p><p>department \tstring \tOptional \tOwning department name</p><p>category_id \tUUID \tOptional \tCategory UUID from GET /categories</p><p>owner_id \tUUID \tOptional \tUser UUID; defaults to the authenticated user</p><p>tags \tstring[] \tOptional \tArray of tag strings</p><p>custom_fields \tobject \tOptional \tAny additional JSONB metadata</p><p>Example Request (Mode B):</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"description": "Standard operating procedure for sterile manufacturing",</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Gowning",</p><p>"department": "Manufacturing",</p><p>"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",</p><p>"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "gowning"]</p><p>}</p><p>Example Request (Mode C — API Key only):</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_module_api_key></p><p>X-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Module-Created SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure"</p><p>}</p><p>Auto-behaviors:</p><p>• document_number auto-generated: <TYPE>-<YEAR>-<NNNN> (e.g., SOP-2026-0001)</p><p>• status defaults to "draft"</p><p>• Initial version 0.1 is auto-created in document_versions table</p><p>• IndexingHooks.indexDocument() is triggered for search indexing</p><p>Validation Error (HTTP 400):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "title and document_type are required" }</p><p>}</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 7 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents — List Documents</p><p>Lists documents for the tenant with pagination and filtering.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Query Parameters:</p><p>Parameter \tType \tDescription</p><p>limit \tinteger \tResults per page (default: 50)</p><p>offset \tinteger \tPagination offset (default: 0)</p><p>status \tstring \tFilter by status code (e.g., draft, effective)</p><p>category_id \tUUID \tFilter by category UUID</p><p>document_type \tstring \tFilter by type code (e.g., SOP)</p><p>owner_id \tUUID \tFilter by owner UUID</p><p>search \tstring \tFull-text ILIKE search on title, document_number, description</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents?status=effective&document_type=SOP&limit=20&offset=0</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Example Response:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": true,</p><p>"data": [ /* array of Document Summary objects */ ],</p><p>"pagination": {</p><p>"total": 47,</p><p>"limit": 20,</p><p>"offset": 0</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/:id — Get Single Document</p><p>Returns full details for a single document by its UUID.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tFull 19-field document object</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 8 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>⚠ Checkout status is NOT included in this response. It is tracked separately in the document_checkouts table.</p><p>Not Found (HTTP 404):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": { "code": "NOT_FOUND", "message": "Document not found" }</p><p>}</p><p>PUT /api/v1/documents/:id — Update Document Metadata</p><p>Updates document metadata only. Content changes must go through versioning (POST /versions).</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tFull 19-field updated document object</p><p>Updatable Fields:</p><p>Field \tType \tDescription</p><p>title \tstring \tDocument title</p><p>description \tstring \tDescription</p><p>category_id \tUUID \tChange category</p><p>owner_id \tUUID \tReassign owner</p><p>department \tstring \tDepartment</p><p>tags \tstring[] \tReplace tags array</p><p>custom_fields \tobject \tReplace custom JSONB metadata</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>PUT /api/v1/documents/d1234567-abcd-ef01-2345-6789abcdef01</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP - Revised",</p><p>"department": "Quality Assurance",</p><p>"tags": ["sterile", "gmp", "updated"]</p><p>}</p><p>5.3 Version Management APIs</p><p>Documents use major.minor versioning. Each new version resets the document to draft status.</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 9 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Version Type \tExample Transition \tis_major_version</p><p>Minor edit \t0.1 → 0.2 \tfalse (default)</p><p>Major revision \t0.2 → 1.0, 1.3 → 2.0 \ttrue</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — List Versions</p><p>Returns all versions for a document, ordered from newest to oldest.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:read</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tArray of 13-field version objects</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>⚠ content is NOT included in the version list response — only metadata is returned.</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/versions — Create New Version</p><p>Creates a new version of a document. The document status is reset to draft — it must go through the review</p><p>process again.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Response \tHTTP 201 — New 13-field version object</p><p>Request Body Fields:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>content \tstring \tOptional \tNew plain-text content body</p><p>content_html \tstring \tOptional \tHTML version of content</p><p>change_summary \tstring \tOptional \tBrief description of what changed</p><p>change_reason \tstring \tOptional \tReason category (e.g., minor_edit, regulatory_update)</p><p>is_major_version \tboolean \tOptional \ttrue for major version bump (default: false)</p><p>file_name \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file name</p><p>file_path \tstring \tOptional \tAttached file path/URL</p><p>file_size \tinteger \tOptional \tFile size in bytes</p><p>mime_type \tstring \tOptional \tMIME type of attached file</p><p>Minor Version Example:</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 10 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. References\\nISO 14644, EU GMP Annex 1",</p><p>"change_summary": "Added references section",</p><p>"change_reason": "minor_edit"</p><p>}</p><p>Major Version Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"content": "Complete rewrite per new regulatory requirements.",</p><p>"change_summary": "Major revision per EU GMP Annex 1 update",</p><p>"change_reason": "regulatory_update",</p><p>"is_major_version": true</p><p>}</p><p>Key Behaviors:</p><p>• SHA-256 hash is auto-calculated from content for integrity verification</p><p>• Document current_version_id is updated to the new version</p><p>• Document status is reset to "draft"</p><p>5.4 Checkout / Checkin APIs</p><p>The checkout/checkin mechanism prevents concurrent editing by granting an exclusive 24-hour lock on a</p><p>document.</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkout — Checkout Document</p><p>Locks the document for exclusive editing by the current user.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>reason \tstring \tOptional \tWhy the document is being checked out</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Adding new section on environmental monitoring"</p><p>}</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 11 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Possible Responses:</p><p>Scenario \tResponse</p><p>Successful new checkout \t{ "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "<ISO timestamp +24h>" }</p><p>Same user re-checking out \t{ "already_checked_out": true, "by_current_user": true }</p><p>Different user has it checked out \tHTTP 500 — "Document is already checked out by another user"</p><p>• Checkout expires automatically after 24 hours</p><p>• Checkout status is logged in document_access_log</p><p>• Checkout status is NOT visible in the GET /documents/:id response</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/checkin — Checkin Document</p><p>Releases the exclusive lock. Only the user who performed the checkout can check in.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Auth Modes \tA, B, C</p><p>Request Body \tEmpty {} or no body required</p><p>Example Request:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>Success Response: { "checked_in": true }</p><p>Error Response (wrong user): "Document is not checked out by you"</p><p>5.5 Lifecycle Workflow APIs</p><p>These endpoints drive the document through its full lifecycle. Always run them in the correct order.</p><p>💡 Lifecycle Flow: draft → [Submit] → in_review → [Approve] → approved → [Make Effective] → effective →</p><p>[Obsolete] → obsolete. OR: in_review / approved → [Reject] → draft (re-submit to restart)</p><p>All lifecycle endpoints return the full 19-field document object.</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/submit — Submit for Review</p><p>Submits a draft document for review. Starts a document_approval workflow instance.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 12 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Allowed From \tdraft status only</p><p>Request Body \tEmpty {} required</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>What happens internally:</p><p>1. Validates document is in draft status</p><p>2. Calls workflowEngine.startWorkflow({ workflowCode: 'document_approval', ... })</p><p>3. Sets document status = 'in_review'</p><p>4. Saves workflow_instance_id on the document</p><p>5. Updates current version's status to in_review</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/approve — Approve Document</p><p>Approves a document that is under review. Logs in workflow history.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \tin_review status only</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>comments \tstring \tOptional \tApproval comments</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"comments": "Reviewed and approved per QA checklist"</p><p>}</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/reject — Reject Document</p><p>Rejects a document and returns it to draft. Logs in workflow history.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \tin_review or approved status</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 13 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>reason \tstring \tRequired \tMust provide a rejection reason</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/reject</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Needs additional safety section per regulatory requirement"</p><p>}</p><p>Validation Error (missing reason):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": {</p><p>"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",</p><p>"message": "reason is required when rejecting a document"</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/make-effective — Make Effective</p><p>Marks an approved document as effective. Auto-calculates the next review date.</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \tapproved status only</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>effective_date \tstring (ISO date) \tRequired \te.g., "2026-03-01" or "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"</p><p>signature_id \tUUID \tOptional \te-Signature UUID if applicable</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"effective_date": "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>Auto-calculation of next_review_date:</p><p>• If document has a category_id → next_review_date = effective_date +</p><p>category.review_frequency_months</p><p>• If no category → next_review_date = null</p><p>• Example: SOP category has 12-month review → next_review_date = effective + 12 months</p><p>⚠ Does NOT insert workflow history — this is by design in the current implementation.</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 14 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/:id/obsolete — Make Obsolete</p><p>Marks an effective document as obsolete (superseded).</p><p>Attribute \tValue</p><p>Permissions \tdocument:write</p><p>Allowed From \teffective status only</p><p>Request Body:</p><p>Field \tType \tRequired \tDescription</p><p>reason \tstring \tRequired \tWhy this document is being obsoleted</p><p>Example:</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Superseded by new revision SOP-2026-0010"</p><p>}</p><p>What happens internally:</p><p>• Sets obsolete_date = NOW()</p><p>• Inserts into workflow_history (action = 'obsolete', comments = reason) if workflow_instance_id exists</p><p>Validation Error (missing reason):</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": {</p><p>"code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",</p><p>"message": "reason is required when making a document obsolete"</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>6. Document Lifecycle State Machine</p><p>From Status \tAction \tTo Status \tRequired Fields</p><p>draft \tSubmit \tin_review \t—</p><p>in_review \tApprove \tapproved \tcomments (optional)</p><p>in_review \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)</p><p>approved \tMake Effective \teffective \teffective_date (required)</p><p>approved \tReject \tdraft \treason (required)</p><p>effective \tObsolete \tobsolete \treason (required)</p><p>⚠ Creating a new version (POST /versions) from any status always resets the document to draft.</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 15 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>State Flow:</p><p>draft ──[Submit]──► in_review ──[Approve]──► approved ──[Make Effective]──►</p><p>effective</p><p>▲ \t│ \t│ \t│</p><p>│ \t[Reject] \t[Reject]</p><p>[Obsolete]</p><p>└───────────────────────┘◄─────────────────────────┘ \t▼</p><p>obsolete</p><p>7. Response Schemas</p><p>Document Object (Full — 19 Fields)</p><p>Returned by: POST /documents, GET /documents/:id, PUT /documents/:id, and all lifecycle endpoints.</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",</p><p>"description": "Description text",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"category": {</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"name": "Standard Operating Procedures",</p><p>"code": "SOP"</p><p>},</p><p>"status": "draft",</p><p>"current_version": "0.1",</p><p>"version_status": "draft",</p><p>"owner": {</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"email": "admin@company.com",</p><p>"name": "Jane Doe"</p><p>},</p><p>"department": "Manufacturing",</p><p>"effective_date": "2026-03-01",</p><p>"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",</p><p>"tags": ["sterile", "gmp"],</p><p>"custom_fields": {},</p><p>"workflow_instance_id": "uuid or null",</p><p>"created_by": "admin@company.com",</p><p>"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z",</p><p>"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>Document Summary (10 Fields)</p><p>Returned by: GET /documents (list) and GET /documents/due-for-review.</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"document_number": "SOP-2026-0001",</p><p>"title": "Sterile Manufacturing SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"category": "Standard Operating Procedures",</p><p>"status": "effective",</p><p>"current_version": "1.0",</p><p>"owner": "admin@company.com",</p><p>"next_review_date": "2027-03-01",</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 16 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>"updated_at": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>Version Object (13 Fields)</p><p>Returned by: GET /documents/:id/versions and POST /documents/:id/versions.</p><p>{</p><p>"id": "uuid",</p><p>"version_number": "0.2",</p><p>"major_version": 0,</p><p>"minor_version": 2,</p><p>"status": "draft",</p><p>"file": {</p><p>"name": "document.pdf",</p><p>"path": "/uploads/document.pdf",</p><p>"size": 204800,</p><p>"mime_type": "application/pdf",</p><p>"hash": "sha256-hex-string"</p><p>},</p><p>"change_summary": "Added references section",</p><p>"change_reason": "minor_edit",</p><p>"approved_by": "approver@company.com",</p><p>"approved_at": "2026-02-28T11:00:00Z",</p><p>"signature_id": "uuid or null",</p><p>"created_by": "author@company.com",</p><p>"created_at": "2026-02-28T10:30:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>💡 file is null if no file attachment exists. content field is NOT included in the version list response.</p><p>8. Error Reference</p><p>All errors follow a consistent format:</p><p>{</p><p>"success": false,</p><p>"error": {</p><p>"code": "ERROR_CODE",</p><p>"message": "Human-readable message"</p><p>}</p><p>}</p><p>HTTP</p><p>Status Code \tMessage \tWhen</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR title and document_type are required \tCreating without required fields</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when rejecting a</p><p>document Reject without reason</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR effective_date is required \tMake Effective without date</p><p>400 \tVALIDATION_ERROR reason is required when making a</p><p>document obsolete Obsolete without reason</p><p>404 \tNOT_FOUND \tDocument not found Document not found or wrong</p><p>tenant</p><p>500 \tCREATE_ERROR \terror detail \tDB or internal error on create</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 17 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>HTTP</p><p>Status Code \tMessage \tWhen</p><p>500 \tCHECKOUT_ERROR Document is already checked out by</p><p>another user Concurrent checkout</p><p>500 \tCHECKIN_ERROR \tDocument is not checked out by you \tWrong user trying to checkin</p><p>500 \tSUBMIT_ERROR Only draft documents can be submitted</p><p>for review Wrong status</p><p>500 \tAPPROVE_ERROR Only documents in review can be</p><p>approved Wrong status</p><p>500 \tREJECT_ERROR Only documents in review or approved</p><p>can be rejected Wrong status</p><p>500 MAKE_EFFECTIVE_E</p><p>RROR</p><p>Only approved documents can be made</p><p>effective Wrong status</p><p>500 \tOBSOLETE_ERROR Only effective documents can be made</p><p>obsolete Wrong status</p><p>9. Module Integration Patterns</p><p>Pattern 1: Module Creates a Document on Behalf of a User (Most Common)</p><p>Use Mode B (JWT + API Key). The audit trail will show the real user.</p><p>1. User logs in to QAssure → get jwt_token</p><p>2. User launches your module → get launch_token</p><p>3. Module backend calls verify-launch-token → get module_jwt</p><p>4. Module calls POST /documents with:</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>5. Document owner/created_by = real user (not your module)</p><p>Pattern 2: Module Does Background / Automated Document Operations</p><p>Use Mode C (API Key + Tenant ID). No user context needed.</p><p>1. Configure document:read + document:write in api_key_permissions for your API key</p><p>2. All requests include:</p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>X-Tenant-ID: <tenant_uuid></p><p>3. No user JWT needed</p><p>4. Audit trail shows module identity (no user)</p><p>Pattern 3: Module Shows a Document Compliance Dashboard</p><p>6. Call GET /documents/due-for-review?days_ahead=30 to get documents needing attention</p><p>7. Call GET /documents?status=effective to list currently active documents</p><p>8. Call GET /documents?status=draft to list documents pending submission</p><p>9. Call GET /documents/categories to build category filter dropdowns</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 18 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>Pattern 4: Module Manages Full Document Authoring Workflow</p><p>1. Create document \t→ POST /documents</p><p>2. Checkout for editing \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkout</p><p>3. Create new version with edits → POST /documents/:id/versions</p><p>4. Checkin \t→ POST /documents/:id/checkin</p><p>5. Submit for review \t→ POST /documents/:id/submit</p><p>6. Approve (by QA) \t→ POST /documents/:id/approve</p><p>7. Make effective (by admin) \t→ POST /documents/:id/make-effective</p><p>8. (Later) Obsolete when superseded → POST /documents/:id/obsolete</p><p>10. Complete Workflow Example</p><p>A complete, annotated request/response sequence for creating and publishing a document via Combined Auth</p><p>(Mode B).</p><p>Step 1 — Get Categories</p><p>GET /api/v1/documents/categories</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>→ Note the id for the SOP category (e.g., 6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5)</p><p>Step 2 — Create Document</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents</p><p>Authorization: Bearer <module_jwt></p><p>X-API-Key: <your_api_key></p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"title": "Equipment Calibration SOP",</p><p>"document_type": "SOP",</p><p>"description": "Procedure for equipment calibration in production areas",</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n3.1 Calibration Steps",</p><p>"department": "Engineering",</p><p>"category_id": "6f418ad8-c345-4003-98dd-033ab989b3a5",</p><p>"tags": ["calibration", "equipment", "gmp"]</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: draft, Version: 0.1, document_number: SOP-2026-0002</p><p>→ Save the data.id as document_id</p><p>Step 3 — Checkout for Editing</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkout</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"reason": "Adding section 4 - Frequency of Calibration"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Response: { "checked_out": true, "expires_at": "..." }</p><p>Step 4 — Create a New Version (Minor Edit)</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 19 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/versions</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"content": "1. Purpose\\n2. Scope\\n3. Procedure\\n4. Frequency\\n4.1 Monthly for critical</p><p>equipment",</p><p>"change_summary": "Added frequency section",</p><p>"change_reason": "minor_edit"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Version bumped to 0.2, document status reset to draft</p><p>Step 5 — Checkin</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/checkin</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>→ Response: { "checked_in": true }</p><p>Step 6 — Submit for Review</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/submit</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{}</p><p>→ Status: in_review, workflow_instance_id is now populated</p><p>Step 7 — Approve</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/approve</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"comments": "Reviewed and approved - meets regulatory standards"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: approved</p><p>Step 8 — Make Effective</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/make-effective</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>"effective_date": "2026-03-17T00:00:00Z"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: effective</p><p>→ next_review_date auto-calculated: 2027-03-17 (SOP category = 12 months)</p><p>Step 9 — (Future) Obsolete When Superseded</p><p>POST /api/v1/documents/<document_id>/obsolete</p><p>Content-Type: application/json</p><p>{</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 20 of 21 --</p><p>QAssure — Document Service API Integration GuideLast Verified: 28-Feb-2026</p><p>"reason": "Superseded by Equipment Calibration SOP v2.0 (SOP-2026-0015)"</p><p>}</p><p>→ Status: obsolete, obsolete_date = NOW()</p><p>Quick Reference Card</p><p>API Meth</p><p>od Endpoint \tPermission \tRequired Body Fields</p><p>Get Categories \tGET \t/documents/categories \tdocument:read \t—</p><p>Get Types \tGET \t/documents/types \tAuth only \t—</p><p>Get Statuses \tGET \t/documents/statuses \tAuth only \t—</p><p>Due for Review \tGET /documents/due-for-revi</p><p>ew document:read \t—</p><p>List Documents \tGET \t/documents \tdocument:read \t—</p><p>Get Document \tGET \t/documents/:id \tdocument:read \t—</p><p>Create Document POST /documents \tdocument:write title, document_type</p><p>Update Document PUT \t/documents/:id \tdocument:write at least one field</p><p>Get Versions \tGET \t/documents/:id/versions document:read \t—</p><p>Create Version \tPOST /documents/:id/versions document:write —</p><p>Checkout \tPOST /documents/:id/checkout document:write —</p><p>Checkin \tPOST /documents/:id/checkin document:write —</p><p>Submit for Review POST /documents/:id/submit \tdocument:write {}</p><p>Approve \tPOST /documents/:id/approve document:write —</p><p>Reject \tPOST /documents/:id/reject \tdocument:write reason (mandatory)</p><p>Make Effective \tPOST /documents/:id/make-eff</p><p>ective document:write effective_date (mandatory)</p><p>Obsolete \tPOST /documents/:id/obsolete document:write reason (mandatory)</p><p>Confidential — QAssure Internal DocumentationPage</p><p>-- 21 of 21 --</p>	Initial draft	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	4ccf68ad-485c-495a-935b-10d74b173a52	2026-03-27 14:24:17.319349+00	platform	\N
